{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools","id":1238731,"title":"A concern for Lunars: Alternate dice pools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-25T17:46:38-07:00","id":1238731,"title":"A concern for Lunars: Alternate dice pools","content":"Vance has confirmed that in Lunars 3e we will be seeing new charms that will allow Lunars to attack with Strength, Defend with parry, and likely some other things. Maybe Intelligence for Guile? Who knows. These charms will be likely be endlessly replicated if not in official works then fan homebrew. Attempting to do so is like trying to stop the tides themselves. If we don't see an alternate attack stat for Sidereals, people will then complain that their favorite pet splat is left out in the dust.<br /> <br /> So here's my question: Why are we having what is essentially feat taxes?<br /> <br /> I propose that 3e would only have an improvement if we have alternate abilities for certain actions <i>baked into the base ruleset</i> then things would only improve from there. How you ask?<br /> <br /> 1) As mentioned previously, people who want to play as a standard barbarian warlord no longer needs to choose between playing with what is essentially their arm cut off or paying a feat tax for having the 'privledge' of a decent dice pool for his core concept. The same thing goes for using social stats too.<br /> <br /> 2) Dexterity is no longer the king of everything ever in combat. Making a quick rule to say that you can use Strength in place of Dexterity for Melee/Brawl attacks? Whoopie, +4 max potential damage difference! Try then fighting against a kiting character, you'd be at a major disadvantage. Dexterity would still be the best, but at least builds that don't want to be gymnasts are viable.<br /> <br /> 3) The sooner we nip this in the bud the easier it is to build things down the line. &quot;But Sandact! What about Warstriders!? Increasing Strength Exercise!? Animals with high strength values that Lunars can abuse! Surely this breaks the game!&quot; Want the quick and easy fixes kids? &quot;Only the character's <i>natural</i> strength is used for damage calculation. A Lunar who is in an animal form who uses a lower strength rating uses the higher one. If an animals strength is higher then the accuracy value is treated as +0&quot;. Maybe the rest as charm dice but that reeks of dice adders somewhat, but point is we can nip this in the ass now. If we wait until further down the line we'd need fixes for Gentimen's, Sidereals, Exigents, Alchemicals, Infernals, Liminals, and Cosmic Exalts. Plus add a few more in those.<br /> <br /> 4) &quot;Dexterity is hand-eye coordination and Strength is raw br-&quot; Oh cut the crap. Multiple games have done this before. Because you want to know why? Balance! It promotes multiple playstyles! With all the freedom in this game it boggle my mind that this still remains! I'm asking for anything insane. I'm not saying that we should make Intelligence also work for melee attack rolls too, that doesn't make sense. Those alternate dice pool charms can be used for more interesting methods. Maybe an Ebon Dragon charm could allow an Infernal to use Manipulation as his attribute for any single roll for some cost? Maybe a Sidereal who perfectly planned out a chosen assault could use Intelligence on some rolls until his plan goes array? Maybe Strength can be used for Performance because your muscles are that good at saying things without words? But at base there should be SOME attributes that can be swapped out for such things! Why is it that multiple other RPG's allow such a thing but Exalted does not?<br /> <br /> [quote=Vance]Errata isn't a thing we get paid for and something we want to avoid.[quote]<br /> <br /> Sweetie I get it. Rolling out errata this early in a line doesn't look good. But this wound is only going to fester and get worse as time goes on. Sure its not the flesh eating disease that was paranoia combat from 2e but if we have a chance to improve 3e for the better why not take that chance? Are you really going to miss the three dollars you probably would've made typing out such stuff? Or put it into a new book as stealth errata, there will be some slight confusion but everyone would at least be happier. Trying to do the same in 2e would be very hard as you have to convert... 30 or so books of material? Right now in 3e you only have 4 (Core, Arms, DB's, Lunars, bits and pieces of Raksha and Exigents). Do you want to pick up a five pound weight or a 50 pound weight?<br /> <br /> Go ahead, state your thoughts below. If you think I'm wrong tell me why I'm taking crazy pills.<br /> <br /> Edit: You want math and more in depth reasoning without needing wade through 8 pages? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239612#post1239612\">Here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 07-28-2018, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T18:26:51-07:00","id":1238738,"title":"","content":"Here are my thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. It fits for Lunars who already have all sorts of ways to bring different attributes to the party, via their stunting and excellencies. They could hit you with how pretty they are if they wanted to. <br /> <br /> Outside of esoteric interpretations of Black Claw style, this isn\u2019t something other Exalts can do.<br /> <br /> 2. It is possibly a feature of the Attribute based Charmset, and thus I\u2019d expect Alchemicals (Unsurpassed Mathematical targeting Reticule) and Liminal Exalted (Hand-Eye co-ordination) to have similar charms in their set with different levels of ease of pulling this off.<br /> <br /> 3. The Solar charmset (Dragonblooded too?) does similar things for Abilities, see swap Stealth for Awareness when reckoning Join Battle. As far as I know Lunars do not get this trick. So there is some level of mechanical balance there.<br /> <br /> Basically where you saw something that cried out for house rules inclusion (and I admit it\u2019s a cool thing to scream \u201cScrew you Dex, you are nothing to me!\u201d) I see internal system consistency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T18:29:30-07:00","id":1238740,"title":"","content":"Maybe there might be Charms allowing Perception to substitute for Wits on Join Battle rolls and Intelligence to substitute for any other Attribute on crafting rolls, but I don\u2019t expect it to happen for anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T18:59:52-07:00","id":1238746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238738#post1238738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are my thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. It fits for Lunars who already have all sorts of ways to bring different attributes to the party, via their stunting and excellencies. They could hit you with how pretty they are if they wanted to.<br /> <br /> Outside of esoteric interpretations of Black Claw style, this isn\u2019t something other Exalts can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stunting via excellencies costs motes. If you are forcing yourself to stunt a DEX+APP roll to hit something because your dicepool is crap to begin with then that's newbie hazing. Do you remember how fun it was in 2e for people to buy at the most an additional Ox-Body? I'll tell you in case you didn't play 2e: Not fun enough.<br /> <br /> It's set up to be &quot;Timmy trap&quot; in glass tower design which originated in card games. Cards were deliberately designed to be better than the other, the point was to encourage Timmy to gain system mastery by learning what the real effective cards do. When he does he can alter his deck.<br /> <br /> This does not work in tabletop games. If you spend all that time and effort to make a character (Which in Exalted is a lot more than usual. Even reading through Essence 1 charms is a lot of work for new people) and he turns out to be crap because you picked what sounded cool or effective without deeper system mastery? You are screwed. You are forced to pay out of the nose with XP. Go ahead and use Flat XP or BP, the point is the same. Why should Timmy be taxed because he picked something that sounded cool? Why is it that Lunars should have the privledge of using alternate attributes when nearly every other RPG allows differing attributes for different pools.<br /> <br /> This isn't something other <i>exalts</i> should be able to do. This is something <i>everyone</i> should be able to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238738#post1238738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. It is possibly a feature of the Attribute based Charmset, and thus I\u2019d expect Alchemicals (Unsurpassed Mathematical targeting Reticule) and Liminal Exalted (Hand-Eye co-ordination) to have similar charms in their set with different levels of ease of pulling this off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but why bother? These are feat taxes for a character concept. They are boring to look at, they are dull to use. Words can be better spent other things. They're not hard, hell I can make one right now.<br /> <br /> HEROIC FIGHTER'S BRAVADO<br /> Cost\u200b: -\u037e Mins\u200b: Melee 1 Essence 1\u037e Type:\u200b Permanent<br /> Keywords\u200b: Merged<br /> Duration\u200b: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite charms\u200b: None<br /> <br /> The Solar's own muscles allow him to strike with speed beyond imagining or turn aside blades with furious force. This charm allows the Solar to use his Strength pool to calculate his melee derived accuracy and defense. When attacking with Strength and the attack roll shows at least one 10, the Solar turns one dice of post soak into an automatic success. Charms or methods that temporarily increase strength, such as Increasing Strength Exercise and Warstriders, do not boost the Solar's accuracy. Only his natural strength does. This charm also exists in Brawl under the same name.<br /> <br /> See how easy that was? See how easy it was to fit it within the fluff of Solars and not just Attribute based exalts? Do you see why this would become a staple of every Strength based Melee character? Excellencies for most Exalts were made free in 3e because of exactly this, they were dull, boring, imposed a gatelock, and hazed you if you tried to run without them. Why are we wanting to continue that tradition?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238738#post1238738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. The Solar charmset (Dragonblooded too?) does similar things for Abilities, see swap Stealth for Awareness when reckoning Join Battle. As far as I know Lunars do not get this trick. So there is some level of mechanical balance there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not against swapping if it provides an unorthodox method of using said attribute/ability in the specific situation, I said that in my post. Did you read that?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238738#post1238738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically where you saw something that cried out for house rules inclusion (and I admit it\u2019s a cool thing to scream \u201cScrew you Dex, you are nothing to me!\u201d) I see internal system consistency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where you see internal system consistency I see rusty cogs in those machine. Sure they do the job, but they're not pretty. You can replace those cogs and make the whole thing work not just fine, but even better. I am not crying out Death to dexterity. Even in the most ideal scenario you'd still have it be an accuracy option for melee/brawl and Archery/thrown AND defense. I'm asking why is Exalted using this dead cow, these broken gears when other systems have done otherwise and have only been improved by it?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T19:05:48-07:00","id":1238748,"title":"","content":"Friend Sandact6, if you want to post combatively, you will get combative replies. Think on that for a period while I respond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T19:12:55-07:00","id":1238749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238748#post1238748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Friend Sandact6, if you want to post combatively, you will get combative replies. Think on that for a period while I respond.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be factious but I am civil. Exalted 3e is a game and only a game. I am not offended by you or anything you posted and in fact want to see the discourse continue further. Let's us, and everyone, keep that in mind going forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T19:17:33-07:00","id":1238751,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing. You can write whatever charm you want but that's not something that would make sense in the solar charmset. A solar doesn't have the ability to shift attribute uses. Which is what this is. We'll have to see the charm to see if it's &quot;just&quot; a shift and not a shift plus extra bonuses but make no mistake that by switching STR with attack and Stamina for parry, they are able to do things no other being can. So it might cost a charm it still gives them options no one else has.<br /> <br /> And in this edition being able to parry with stamina as well as resist with it, has insane utility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T19:56:25-07:00","id":1238764,"title":"","content":"If you bake freely swapping attributes in the base rules, then what's the point of having attributes? Everything just becomes ability + 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T20:13:42-07:00","id":1238767,"title":"","content":"Being able to attack and deal damage with Strength has great utility as well, but still doesn't make it an ultimately boring choice when you can do more interesting things with it.<br /> <br /> &quot;It opens up new options!&quot;<br /> <br /> So its a speedbump like old excellencies, gating your utility and base competency behind a feat tax. Got it.<br /> <br /> In order to create I feel boundaries need to be pushed or expanded. Fate Core allows crafters to use Craft as their attack ability if they made the item they're using. That's cool and balanced in the area of Fate. DnD 3.5e/4e/5e/Pathfinder allows Strength to be used as the primary method of hitting and has been doing so for yes as one of the least problematic things about it. They did this to broaden options. Why are we not allowing the same thing here?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T20:16:58-07:00","id":1238768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238764#post1238764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you bake freely swapping attributes in the base rules, then what's the point of having attributes? Everything just becomes ability + 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly thought about the same thing, but it becomes a bit more complicated with other splats. I mean the Lightbringers homebrew from 2e made your attacking stat 5 + ability, but that's because only Solars were playable. How would this work for Lunars, Alchemicals, etc...? It's a bit easier to do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T20:20:48-07:00","id":1238769,"title":"","content":"I was just about to bring up D&amp;D actually. But as a counter argument.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D has from the start always had strength to hit with Melee Weapons. (And Dex for ranged, much the same argument) <br /> <br /> In 3.5/4/5e there were exceptions to this (you can use Dex or Con or Cha) and these are a big deal so much so that entire character concepts get mapped around them. (2e? Before my time)<br /> <br /> So that maps more to what Exalted is doing- there are expected stats mapped to things and being able to break that rule is a major character defining change, as is this Charm for Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T20:57:38-07:00","id":1238774,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with Lunars (and possibly other Attribute based Exalted) being able to change out which Attribute they use in conjunction with various Abilities. One of the annoying things about Lunars in 1st and 2nd edition was that they were pretty much mandated to pick up Dexterity as a favored Attribute (not much fun when you only had 1 favored attribute). If you have a bit more freedom in being able to use other Attributes for combat, it helps to give Lunar characters more build variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T21:48:09-07:00","id":1238787,"title":"","content":"Its because they made it from the start to do such a thing that things didn't require much effort. This is why I'm saying that to do this at the start of the game is best. I don't have a time machine to go back in time to yell at Holden and Morke, and I'm not saying that it will take some work doing so. But the work would be <i>much</i> less now compared to when we have 8 splats and charms spread across how many books.<br /> <br /> As for major character defining change? I'll one up that for you. Its a setting defining change. Regardless of what Exalted started as, somewhere in 1e and 2e it ended up as a Wuxia setting. I don't know how this happened, and I still like the idea of Realm castles being chinese themed. It doesn't matter if it WAS Wuxia, it cannot be denied those who knew about the game at large thought about this. In Wuxia you have wire jumping and fancy sword fights. Back then it made sense to have everything tied to Dexterity. I was once one of these people.<br /> <br /> But 3e is supposed to be a grand rebirth of the line. Of the setting, of the perceptions, and of the mechanics. We have a chance to do it and maybe keep errata involving this about half a page at most. Do we really want to wait until we need Scroll of Errata 2 with another several hundred pages with retroactive fixes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T21:57:27-07:00","id":1238788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238774#post1238774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm okay with Lunars (and possibly other Attribute based Exalted) being able to change out which Attribute they use in conjunction with various Abilities. One of the annoying things about Lunars in 1st and 2nd edition was that they were pretty much mandated to pick up Dexterity as a favored Attribute (not much fun when you only had 1 favored attribute). If you have a bit more freedom in being able to use other Attributes for combat, it helps to give Lunar characters more build variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't just Lunars who suffered from this. Literally every character who had Dexterity less than 4 felt as if having their arm cut off, ESPECIALLY in 2e with IAM being a massive factor.<br /> <br /> 3e closed the gap a bit sure. It's more forgiving on withering, but landing a decisive is going to be agonizing. I don't feel one splat should have this. This isn't an impressive base ability like sharing charms across multiple attack abilities, shapeshifting, or quasi-immortality. This is just letting people have a chance at other character concepts without having to be a ballerina. You know why Solar Glory was spread across five abilities rather than just one? It was because players didn't want their Conan to be a bookworm to get those juicy extra motes. Motes that were everything in 2e. Motes that essentially became a gatekeeper from playing a good character to one of the upper tiers. Before it was an ability tax to those who didn't want to play second fiddle to Twilights or anyone stupid enough who didn't go into Lore. After it became a pointless charm tax that was needed for the upper levels of the game because <i>it was that damn good</i>. Now the Attribute charms are here again to impose a feat tax on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T00:10:52-07:00","id":1238812,"title":"","content":"My first thought is that the central premise of your complaint remains unproven and unjustified. &quot;This is a feat tax, which means whatever I want it to mean, so the rule need to change until I decide they aren't a feat tax, because feat taxes are bad,&quot; isn't really a compelling argument even if you expand it into a much larger post.<br /> <br /> My second thought is that Exalted would only benefit from loosening Attributes (and Abilities) for a very specific style of play that isn't the primary focus on the game. It works great in the Storypath system, but the Storypath system is a much lighter system that doesn't require nearly as much mechanical consistency in such matters. Exalted is a very complex game, and keeping it running requires a heavier hand from the rules. That's why Exalted relies on Charms for such things (and 3e has so far avoided Merits doing it). Charm design gives the developers the controls necessary to keep everything working smoothly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T04:37:56-07:00","id":1238864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238751#post1238751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... A solar doesn't have the ability to shift attribute uses....</div> </div> </div> </div>Devil-Strangling Attitude wants to have a word with you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T04:47:25-07:00","id":1238868,"title":"","content":"Oh, hey, there we go.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://78.media.tumblr.com/5740b1545fa6fd4ed6eefeb4548bb533/tumblr_pch1zbUTp61sateyko1_540.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T05:22:02-07:00","id":1238873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238812#post1238812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first thought is that the central premise of your complaint remains unproven and unjustified. &quot;This is a feat tax, which means whatever I want it to mean, so the rule need to change until I decide they aren't a feat tax, because feat taxes are bad,&quot; isn't really a compelling argument even if you expand it into a much larger post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me keep it short for you then. Why are still having this despite free excellencies? Why did we get rid of IAM and still keeping this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238812#post1238812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My second thought is that Exalted would only benefit from loosening Attributes (and Abilities) for a very specific style of play that isn't the primary focus on the game. It works great in the Storypath system, but the Storypath system is a much lighter system that doesn't require nearly as much mechanical consistency in such matters. Exalted is a very complex game, and keeping it running requires a heavier hand from the rules. That's why Exalted relies on Charms for such things (and 3e has so far avoided Merits doing it). Charm design gives the developers the controls necessary to keep everything working smoothly.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the system was shoddy in 2e there were things called &quot;Band-aid&quot; charms made by the community. These were things made in order for the game to continue smoothy despite mechanical hiccups and involved using charm tech to fix problems with the core system of the game. One of these things were free excellencies.<br /> <br /> Eventually someone asked &quot;...Wait? Why are we making these band-aid fixes instead of altering the core or base of the game itself?<br /> <br /> This is what led us to having free excellencies and IAM not being a thing in 3e<br /> <br /> If a base system has problems then charm design is only going to mask those problems. They're not going to go away regardless of good design or them pretending them not to be there. This was something learned in 2.Xe paranoia combat.<br /> <br /> Secondly it doesn't matter if you're using Storypath or not. I know Ex3 and Storypath fairly well. I've done thought experiments and tested such things multiple times. Nothing will break. Just making the fix now means a lot less work down the road.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T05:33:08-07:00","id":1238878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238788#post1238788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't just Lunars who suffered from this. Literally every character who had Dexterity less than 4 felt as if having their arm cut off, ESPECIALLY in 2e with IAM being a massive factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason it was an issue for Lunars is that if they didn't have Dex favored, they got gouged on a significant portion of their <i>charms</i>. Solars don't have that problem. And getting an attribute to 4/5 isn't that hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T06:08:28-07:00","id":1238883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238878#post1238878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason it was an issue for Lunars is that if they didn't have Dex favored, they got gouged on a significant portion of their <i>charms</i>. Solars don't have that problem. And getting an attribute to 4/5 isn't that hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone should be allowed to play a towering brute who is slow but terrifying without being the fucking idiot who was stupid enough to take Strength 5/Dex 3 because turns out being slow kills your concept. I <i>watched</i> this happen, it fucked a game up when the strength focused combat monster was behind the people with half their combat Charms but Dex5.<br /> <br /> If the system <i>forces</i> you to abandon your valid concept for mechanical coolness, the fact that you can just buy up an ability that you <i>don't want to have</i> isn't a solution. It's a middle finger in the face of the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T06:25:26-07:00","id":1238890,"title":"","content":"So make devil-strangling attitude but for melee or whatever.<br /> <br /> Sundering Cleave Technique - It doesn't matter how well you block, I'm hitting you anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T06:37:03-07:00","id":1238892,"title":"","content":"&quot;Feat Taxes&quot;, if you want to call them this, exist because they make an Attribute do one more thing than it would previously do, which is something that should be taxed for balancing reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T06:59:38-07:00","id":1238896,"title":"","content":"I think anything that lessens Dexterity's God Status a bit is in itself balancing, and therefore shouldn't be taxed. But thats just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T07:04:44-07:00","id":1238898,"title":"","content":"While I kind of agree with that, in Ex3 you also got weapon accuracy boni, and a tendency to not have to hit arbitrarily large defenses a lot, so Dex 3 v Dex 5 isn't always that interesting a difference, if you're, say, using a light weapon. Or an artifact. Or charms.<br /> It's still the best stat, so you're not wrong. But it used to be far worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T07:24:56-07:00","id":1238902,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1183_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1183\" data-vbnamecard=\"1183\">Sandact6</a> what if the charms that open the functionality also have rider effects that would be worth it on their own or for other characters? Something like an athletics charm that lets you use strength on attacks and boosts some aspect of stronglitude might be good. It would at least help blurr the line between feat tax and &quot;some charms are very good for certain concepts&quot;<br /> <br /> I suppose the core problem would still exist for mortals but the setting has always had some element of mortals being more limited by not having magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 07-26-2018, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T07:28:46-07:00","id":1238903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238864#post1238864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Devil-Strangling Attitude wants to have a word with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>A charm that is much worse than what lunars are getting. It's one charm out of an entire 600 charm set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T07:32:12-07:00","id":1238904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238903#post1238903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A charm that is much worse than what lunars are getting. It's one charm out of an entire 600 charm set.</div> </div> </div> </div>And?<br /> <br /> It still shows that yes, Solars can and do already have limited Attribute swap capabilities.<br /> <br /> So your previous statement is untrue and any conversation based on it is null.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T07:35:54-07:00","id":1238905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238788#post1238788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't just Lunars who suffered from this. Literally every character who had Dexterity less than 4 felt as if having their arm cut off, ESPECIALLY in 2e with IAM being a massive factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't about dice pools, the problem is about Charm purchases. <br /> <br /> Ability Exalted have a lot of different stats to invest in for combat - Melee, Archery, Martial Arts, etc. This gives a Solar (or Dragon Blooded or Abyssal or whatever) player a lot of options in how to build their character while still being able to participate effectively in for combat. Meanwhile, Attribute Exalted have exactly one stat they can invest in for combat - Dexterity. Trying to play an Attribute Exalt who doesn't favor Dexterity is like trying to play an Ability Exalt who doesn't favor any of the combat abilities. You can maybe kind of skate by with a grappling build if you favor Strength but that's it.<br /> <br /> So I don't have an issue with Attribute Exalted having a few more options and a little more versatility in which Attributes are useful for combat. It's not something that needs to be baked into the base system because it's not an issue for people who aren't purchasing Attribute based Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-26-2018, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T07:42:09-07:00","id":1238908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238898#post1238898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I kind of agree with that, in Ex3 you also got weapon accuracy boni, and a tendency to not have to hit arbitrarily large defenses a lot, so Dex 3 v Dex 5 isn't always that interesting a difference, if you're, say, using a light weapon. Or an artifact. Or charms.<br /> It's still the best stat, so you're not wrong. But it used to be far worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>For combat purposes:<br /> <br /> Str - Damage Enchancer<br /> <br /> Dex - Attack, Defense, Combat Movement<br /> <br /> Sta - Damage Reduction<br /> <br /> I see no problem with an Ability Charm that lets you change Attack to Str and Defense to Sta.<br /> <br /> A Resistance Charm that lets you Parry with Sta.<br /> <br /> A Melee Charm that lets you attack with Str.<br /> <br /> They would still be weaker than Lunars', which affect the pools regardless of Ability. The Solar/DB version would limit the swap to the Ability in question.<br /> <br /> I'm also not against just including those options as rider on other Charms, say include it as an option for the DB Excellency, or on Fire and Stones Strike, as to eliminate the tax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T07:48:43-07:00","id":1238912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238883#post1238883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone should be allowed to play a towering brute who is slow but terrifying without being the fucking idiot who was stupid enough to take Strength 5/Dex 3 because turns out being slow kills your concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I think that's the rub. I mean, Accuracy more or less represents how well one can hit a moving target. If somebody's character concept is being slow but deadly when they do manage to hit, does it not kind of make sense that it's hard for them to hit a reasonably fast moving target? It would seem that referring to one's character concept as being slow would mean acceptance? Otherwise, what does one want out of the concept that they're describing; to be slow, but still manage to hit most of the time?<br /> <br /> Now, if it was a matter of Strength being an insufficient boon to damage rolls, that's probably a thing more for figuring out some way to build up Strength rather than tear down Dexterity. If it's a matter of &quot;Strength is fine, but Defence is so binary that my slow character never actually gets a chance to hit somebody at all&quot;, well... maybe there are ways to represent a system in which not managing to hit can viably build up towards getting in a major blow, but I think that's a foundational thing, something that would require the base system to be different from the ground up (and might constitute its own opportunity cost), not something with a quick fix.<br /> <br /> If it's a case of wanting to roll Strength in Accuracy rolls, then I feel as though it kind of becomes a case of playing a fast character, just that their fast because of Strength rather than Dexterity. And if Strength is still calculated in damage rolls, being able to pull double duty seems as though it undermines Dexterity a bit.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't really feel the loss of the &quot;slow but heavy hitting&quot; character concept, because it has no reflection in reality; as far as I know, there is not one single fighting style that does not emphasize the importance of being as fast as possible*.<br /> <br /> And I know that Exalted is hanging on the edge of verismilitudinous and stylized genre fiction, and that in the latter the image of being strong but heavy is viable, so there's a basis for others to be attached to it and motivation to represent it in a game such as this. I still question the means of doing that, barring being a major system revision.<br /> <br /> That being said, I will cop to one thing; when the prior developers were first talking about their shiny new combat system and how great it was going to be, I was thinking that it was going to account for ways in which momentum (as we were calling it back then) might be built up that <i>weren't</i> reliant on being able to hit your opponent. Particularly considering a lot of the complaints around combat in Second Edition. And I do think that the combat system that we got did develop a number of good things, and was an improvement on the predecessor, but... it still labours under the issue of how insufficient Accuracy against a sufficiently high Defence makes participation a bit of a non-starter. <br /> <br /> Which really goes back to issues that others have expressed with getting some viable fighting out of mortals and animals. Same going in the other direction; that there's limited recourse to being able to take part if your Defence is low enough that you will never not be hit.<br /> <br /> Hmm, yeah, I do sometimes think that Initiative was not really being utilised to its full potential; that the foundational concept of &quot;you're building up a battlefield advantage before you actually get the chance to make attacks on health levels&quot; might have been a basis for implementing means of building up that advantage other than &quot;be consistently accurate enough to overcome an opponent's defence&quot;.<br /> <br /> * Well, strictly speaking, it's about being to move with as little tell as possible, which the human eye tends to interpret as speed, but the general principle is the same.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:10:53-07:00","id":1238916,"title":"","content":"Yeah, strong, lumbering characters aren't generally protagonists. They show up as like, giant mooks and shit. Big hulking protags tend to be fast despite their bulk. <br /> <br /> It's like that bit in dragonball where trunks gets a super bulky Super saiyan upgrade, but it turns out to be useless because it slows him down too much to actually hit anything.<br /> <br /> It makes sense that bending reality to make such a build viable would be charm territory. Absent that, a high strength, low dex character could work as maybe a builder or something, who is strong but, ultimately, not actually that good in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:23:35-07:00","id":1238918,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I wonder if making strength a source of withering damage that doesn't require &quot;hitting&quot; could help the situation.<br /> <br /> Spitvalling for a sec, maybe if missed attacks still rolled strength as withering damage, it could represent the huge lumbering fuckoff character as a threat that can't be trivialized by a high parry score. <br /> <br /> Maybe penalizing clash attacks by the difference in strength could make some space for them as combatants who you need to avoid going head to head with.<br /> <br /> I suppose that still meets with the problem of hitting decisive attacks without having dexterity. Maybe that's better off being the place where dexterity excels. The narrative space for huge slow dudes in media usually isn't winning many major fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:35:31-07:00","id":1238927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238912#post1238912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, I think that's the rub. I mean, Accuracy more or less represents how well one can hit a moving target. If somebody's character concept is being slow but deadly when they do manage to hit, does it not kind of make sense that it's hard for them to hit a reasonably fast moving target? It would seem that referring to one's character concept as being slow would mean acceptance? Otherwise, what does one want out of the concept that they're describing; to be slow, but still manage to hit most of the time?<br /> <br /> Now, if it was a matter of Strength being an insufficient boon to damage rolls, that's probably a thing more for figuring out some way to build up Strength rather than tear down Dexterity. If it's a matter of &quot;Strength is fine, but Defence is so binary that my slow character never actually gets a chance to hit somebody at all&quot;, well... maybe there are ways to represent a system in which not managing to hit can viably build up towards getting in a major blow, but I think that's a foundational thing, something that would require the base system to be different from the ground up (and might constitute its own opportunity cost), not something with a quick fix.<br /> <br /> If it's a case of wanting to roll Strength in Accuracy rolls, then I feel as though it kind of becomes a case of playing a fast character, just that their fast because of Strength rather than Dexterity. And if Strength is still calculated in damage rolls, being able to pull double duty seems as though it undermines Dexterity a bit.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't really feel the loss of the &quot;slow but heavy hitting&quot; character concept, because it has no reflection in reality; as far as I know, there is not one single fighting style that does not emphasize the importance of being as fast as possible*.<br /> <br /> And I know that Exalted is hanging on the edge of verismilitudinous and stylized genre fiction, and that in the latter the image of being strong but heavy is viable, so there's a basis for others to be attached to it and motivation to represent it in a game such as this. I still question the means of doing that, barring being a major system revision.<br /> <br /> That being said, I will cop to one thing; when the prior developers were first talking about their shiny new combat system and how great it was going to be, I was thinking that it was going to account for ways in which momentum (as we were calling it back then) might be built up that <i>weren't</i> reliant on being able to hit your opponent. Particularly considering a lot of the complaints around combat in Second Edition. And I do think that the combat system that we got did develop a number of good things, and was an improvement on the predecessor, but... it still labours under the issue of how insufficient Accuracy against a sufficiently high Defence makes participation a bit of a non-starter.<br /> <br /> Which really goes back to issues that others have expressed with getting some viable fighting out of mortals and animals. Same going in the other direction; that there's limited recourse to being able to take part if your Defence is low enough that you will never not be hit.<br /> <br /> Hmm, yeah, I do sometimes think that Initiative was not really being utilised to its full potential; that the foundational concept of &quot;you're building up a battlefield advantage before you actually get the chance to make attacks on health levels&quot; might have been a basis for implementing means of building up that advantage other than &quot;be consistently accurate enough to overcome an opponent's defence&quot;.<br /> <br /> * Well, strictly speaking, it's about being to move with as little tell as possible, which the human eye tends to interpret as speed, but the general principle is the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a brute in heavy armor who is precise but can't run as far or move as dextrously isn't what I'd call a fast character. Slow, but accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:37:13-07:00","id":1238928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238918#post1238918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I wonder if making strength a source of withering damage that doesn't require &quot;hitting&quot; could help the situation.<br /> <br /> Spitvalling for a sec, maybe if missed attacks still rolled strength as withering damage, it could represent the huge lumbering fuckoff character as a threat that can't be trivialized by a high parry score.<br /> <br /> Maybe penalizing clash attacks by the difference in strength could make some space for them as combatants who you need to avoid going head to head with.<br /> <br /> I suppose that still meets with the problem of hitting decisive attacks without having dexterity. Maybe that's better off being the place where dexterity excels. The narrative space for huge slow dudes in media usually isn't winning many major fights.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I was tinkering with some application of the above a few months ago over in the &quot;What Breaks If?&quot; thread, I came to the conclusion that base rules for Decisive Attacks should be Attribute of Choice, rather than Dex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:41:23-07:00","id":1238929,"title":"","content":"&quot;Of course strong but slow characters aren't effective, they're not protagonist material&quot; honestly strikes me as a sour-grapes justification of a weakness in the ruleset. I've seen the same thing applied in D&amp;D to explain why <i>dexterity-</i>based melee characters can't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 07-26-2018, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:50:59-07:00","id":1238932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238928#post1238928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I was tinkering with some application of the above a few months ago over in the &quot;What Breaks If?&quot; thread, I came to the conclusion that base rules for Decisive Attacks should be Attribute of Choice, rather than Dex.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. l think it is the place where there should be a lot of leeway for stunts changing the dicepool for your attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 07-26-2018, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:57:28-07:00","id":1238935,"title":"","content":"One thing we need to do to get the genre conventions right is to make heavy weapons the weapon of choice for big, strong characters. As it stands they work better for weak, speedy characters, which is weird. <br /> <br /> So to float an idea I literally just had: What if we have heavy weapons apply a penalty to parry (but not dodge) equal to the difference between the defender's strength and the attacker's, if the latter's is higher?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:10:04-07:00","id":1238940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238935#post1238935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing we need to do to get the genre conventions right is to make heavy weapons the weapon of choice for big, strong characters. As it stands they work better for weak, speedy characters, which is weird.<br /> <br /> So to float an idea I literally just had: What if we have heavy weapons apply a penalty to parry (but not dodge) equal to the difference between the defender's strength and the attacker's, if the latter's is higher?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like exalted combat is already heavy with fiddly math and trying to remember rules and exceptions that apply to every roll of the dice. And then you add charms on top of that and you need a spreadsheet or a script editor to actually get the numbers right. Doubling down on that does not seem to be a progressive direction to go. <br /> <br /> The other issue with it is that quick characters don't have a 'strength score' they have an attack pool and a damage pool. I've gone down the path of trying to reverse engineer the stats based on those pools and it's a complicated and ultimately futile endeavor.<br /> <br /> Though, your point about weak, quick characters getting the most benefit from big slow weapons is well made. However I will point out that to even wield a heavy melee weapon you need strength 3 which is not 'weak'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:17:57-07:00","id":1238944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238927#post1238927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a brute in heavy armor who is precise but can't run as far or move as dextrously isn't what I'd call a fast character. Slow, but accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving aside game mechanics and talking about realistic considerations, if you'll indulge me for the moment, it's a question of how precise you can be against a target that is not only moving, but moving specifically in response to you.<br /> <br /> If your attacks are slow, how does it matter how precise they are if the other person always gets out of the way?<br /> <br /> Mind, there's also a matter of kinetic energy; a slow strike, of any kind, is just not going to impart as much energy, and that matters for things such as impact and penetration. It's like expecting there to be parity between a tossed stone and a fired bullet.<br /> <br /> I should note that actual heavy armour (when it wasn't the kind of thing that was only ever supposed to be worn while on horseback for sporting purposes) was something designed to not actually inhibit mobility at all. You can get people that can perform some acrobatic manuevers while wearing full plate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:25:52-07:00","id":1238948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238940#post1238940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other issue with it is that quick characters don't have a 'strength score' they have an attack pool and a damage pool. I've gone down the path of trying to reverse engineer the stats based on those pools and it's a complicated and ultimately futile endeavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, this is true. If such a rule had been in place in canon, I suspect they would have noted the strength score of all QCs, much like they note appearance. But it's not, so they didn't.<br /> <br /> This isn't really the place to discuss the question &quot;How do we make heavy weapons better in a way that primarily benefits high strength, low dex builds?&quot; though. That seems like something that could be it's own thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:26:04-07:00","id":1238949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238944#post1238944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Leaving aside game mechanics and talking about realistic considerations, if you'll indulge me for the moment, it's a question of how precise you can be against a target that is not only moving, but moving specifically in response to you.<br /> <br /> If your attacks are slow, how does it matter how precise they are if the other person always gets out of the way?<br /> <br /> Mind, there's also a matter of kinetic energy; a slow strike, of any kind, is just not going to impart as much energy, and that matters for things such as impact and penetration. It's like expecting there to be parity between a tossed stone and a fired bullet.<br /> <br /> I should note that actual heavy armour (when it wasn't the kind of thing that was only ever supposed to be worn while on horseback for sporting purposes) was something designed to not actually inhibit mobility at all. You can get people that can perform some acrobatic manuevers while wearing full plate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I care more about allowing for the aesthetic of the slow-moving titan who nevertheless strikes with speed and precision. It's not about being dextrous, it's about being precise with your raw power. No acrobatics or flurries of rapid strikes, Just...okay, I have it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/MqT2RU7mnio?t=743\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/MqT2RU7mnio?t=743\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/MqT2RU7mnio?t=743\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/MqT2RU7mnio?t=743 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> I moved the video to the exact moment that shows what I mean. The weight and power this character has while being slow moving in heavy armor, but brutal and powerful in the close fight itself. It's about the aesthetic of fighting with <i>strength,</i> not <i>dexterity.</i> It's the same argument for Exalted 3rd edition using weapon templates and abstracting into battlegroups. It's about the story and the aesthetic and letting people fight how they want to fight without having to worry that a goremaul is statistically inferior to a reaper daiklave.<br /> <br /> Let people have the aesthetics they want to have, and throw the &quot;realism&quot; right out the window. It's a game, let people have their fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:31:11-07:00","id":1238952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238949#post1238949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weight and power this character has while being slow moving in heavy armor, but brutal and powerful in the close fight itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but feel that this characters fighting ability was greatly improved by his opponents just standing there and letting him hit them though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:33:20-07:00","id":1238953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238949#post1238949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I care more about allowing for the aesthetic of the slow-moving titan who nevertheless strikes with speed and precision. It's not about being dextrous, it's about being precise with your raw power. No acrobatics or flurries of rapid strikes, Just...okay, I have it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/MqT2RU7mnio?t=743\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/MqT2RU7mnio?t=743\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/MqT2RU7mnio?t=743\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/MqT2RU7mnio?t=743 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> I moved the video to the exact moment that shows what I mean. The weight and power this character has while being slow moving in heavy armor, but brutal and powerful in the close fight itself. It's about the aesthetic of fighting with <i>strength,</i> not <i>dexterity.</i> It's the same argument for Exalted 3rd edition using weapon templates and abstracting into battlegroups. It's about the story and the aesthetic and letting people fight how they want to fight without having to worry that a goremaul is statistically inferior to a reaper daiklave.<br /> <br /> Let people have the aesthetics they want to have, and throw the &quot;realism&quot; right out the window. It's a game, let people have their fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love how you bring forward a video of turn-based fighting to illustrate your point. <br /> <br /> The target literally just stands there doing <i>nothing</i> while he gets shredded by a guy he could defeat by just <i>walking away.</i> If that's the aesthetic you want, okay, but I'm just sitting here laughing my ass off about how useless that character would be in a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:35:42-07:00","id":1238955,"title":"","content":"Martial Art based around turn-based combat. <br /> <br /> The charms all revolve around getting your opponent to stand there while you hit them, with the payoff being that you have to do the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:43:10-07:00","id":1238956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238953#post1238953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love how you bring forward a video of turn-based fighting to illustrate your point.<br /> <br /> The target literally just stands there doing <i>nothing</i> while he gets shredded by a guy he could defeat by just <i>walking away.</i> If that's the aesthetic you want, okay, but I'm just sitting here laughing my ass off about how useless that character would be in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I love how you're incapable of wrapping your mind around such advanced concepts as <i>abstractions.</i> His hit rate is 100, his damage is 45. His enemy has 40 health and a 15% chance to hit him for zero damage.<br /> <br /> This paints the picture of someone too fast to defeat in single combat, able to block any hit, and tank any hit that he can't block, while dealing out one hit KOs.<br /> <br /> I hope that these concepts aren't completely beyond your ability to grasp, if you'd like, I can dumb the math down a little for you. Do you need me to explain basic percentiles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:44:55-07:00","id":1238957,"title":"","content":"Yeah, *thump* too *thump* fast *thump* to *thump* defeat. *thump*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T10:49:37-07:00","id":1238983,"title":"","content":"Would there be viable Charm space for a Charm that effectively does &quot;chip damage&quot; against a target in return for successfully hitting you but failing to get through your Soak or having any actual impact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:14:34-07:00","id":1238992,"title":"","content":"I understand the concern for attribute-based exalts being forced to invest heavily in Dex. Though, the devs have done a nice job of limiting this with Lunar's, so I'm not overly concerned. However, ability-based exalts don't need to worry nearly as much about this. I've run 3 games in Exalted so far, with a total of 10 players. The vast majority only had 3 dots of Dex, and they easily handled opponents like cataphracts, manticores, blood apes, and even Octavian. Most of my players have a combat ability 4 and Dex 3, and they've had no problems what so ever. I've even had to come up with creative changes to make things difficult (buck-ogres in full plate armor was amusing). Anyone arguing you need a 4 or 5 to reliably hit simply hasn't been running games in 3E. I've watched my players hit nearly every supernatural foe listed in the corebook with little to no difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:19:43-07:00","id":1238995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238983#post1238983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would there be viable Charm space for a Charm that effectively does &quot;chip damage&quot; against a target in return for successfully hitting you but failing to get through your Soak or having any actual impact?</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: nvm misread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:21:15-07:00","id":1238997,"title":"","content":"In terms of possible semi-realistic bases on which a game system might base a process for a slow but powerful character to conduct themselves, I thought of Kevis vs Marv in Sin City:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=txF-UPGCrEo\" data-code=\"txF-UPGCrEo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/txF-UPGCrEo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> (Be warned that the clip contains violent and possibly distressing imagery in the latter half)<br /> <br /> Not wrestling or other grappling based styles in general, mind; those still place a priority on speed to both get into holds and prevent them from closing around you.<br /> <br /> But, in a system looking to implement it from the beginning, there might be something to the idea of taking hits from an enemy until an opportune moment to counter while they're too extended to do anything about it.<br /> <br /> (I say semi-realistic, because I have an impression that in realistic terms, any fighting based on the assumption or permitting that your opponent will manage to hit you a lot is not a very good one.<br /> <br /> Similar with heavily armoured men-at-arms; people are smart, so when armour developed to the point of being virtually impenetrable, you didn't have people bashing away in futility, you had people develop weapons that were hooked in a manner good for catching an armoured person in the joints, forcing them to the ground, and prying the plates open.)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:50:59-07:00","id":1239009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238873#post1238873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are still having this despite free excellencies? Why did we get rid of IAM and still keeping this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are these equivalent? There's no logic connector that says dumping I(A)M is the same as letting Attributes be a matter of choice.<br /> <br /> Also, free Excellencies are a Solar thing so far. Dragon-blooded don't have them for free. This clearly goes against your point, because the designers feel that &quot;taxing&quot; is a viable design technique. In this case it helps highlight the gap between Celestial and Terrestrial Exalted with less &quot;your Charms are just worse,&quot; and more, &quot;it takes more investment for you to get the same.&quot;<br /> <br /> I(A)M also just doesn't make much sense in 3e's Charm design. Besides all the problems it as in 2e's paradigm, the automatic 5m regen per turn in 3e, and dumping Combos are both very good reasons to dump it that have nothing to do it &quot;feat taxes.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the system was shoddy in 2e there were things called &quot;Band-aid&quot; charms made by the community. </div> </div> </div>The game runs without the ability to select with Attributes you use for attacks as a default thing everyone can do, instead of a special thing only Exalts can do with Charms. It doesn't need a band-aid.<br /> <br /> Don't confuse, &quot;I'd rather things worked this way, so I want to house rule it,&quot; with, &quot;there is an objective flaw in the system.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly it doesn't matter if you're using Storypath or not. </div> </div> </div>Storypath is built from the ground up with the expectations that characters will be allowed flexibility in Attribute assignment. That's why Storypath generally avoids &quot;Attribute&quot; or &quot;Skill&quot; powers, and even things like Epic Strength in Scion 2e has applications when you're not actually rolling Strength.<br /> <br /> Exalted is built from the ground up with the expectations that characters do not have much flexibility with Attribute assignment. Given that Exalted uses Attributes and Abilities as the basis for Charm structures, there's a solid reason to maintain it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing will break. </div> </div> </div>Great. That still hasn't demonstrated that there's a flaw in the first place; just a design decision you don't like, and you can get around with house rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238956#post1238956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I love how you're incapable of wrapping your mind around such advanced concepts as <i>abstractions.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument isn't really that honest to the concept of abstractions either. The whole issue here is not the levels of abstraction, or that the games abstract, but where what gets abstracted.<br /> <br /> As well, the video you showed doesn't really show a character that has any obvious reasons to be considered &quot;slow&quot; in Exalted in a fashion that would imply low Dexterity that would impede his high accuracy. It implies a dearth of Athletics and Dodge, making tactical movement in combat hard even with high Dexterity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This paints the picture of someone too fast to defeat in single combat, able to block any hit, and tank any hit that he can't block, while dealing out one hit KOs. </div> </div> </div>Sounds like someone with high physical Attributes across the board, but focused on Melee and Resistance, and skimped on Athletics and Dodge.<br /> <br /> So... yeah... &quot;lumbering titan&quot; isn't just &quot;how much Dexterity do you have.&quot; Have those characters skimp on Athletics and Dodge, and watch them get destroyed by high mobility characters that don't stand around to be cut up by his Dex 5/Melee 5/Specialty dice pools, because they're always disengaging to safety and he can't keep up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T13:04:12-07:00","id":1239029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238997#post1238997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I thought of Kevis vs Marv in Sin City:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=txF-UPGCrEo\" data-code=\"txF-UPGCrEo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/txF-UPGCrEo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is freaky, I left for lunch and was thinking about this discussion and how it related to this exact same thing lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T13:12:43-07:00","id":1239031,"title":"","content":"The thing is that Dex is the attribute for both hand to eye coordination and agility.<br /> <br /> The system doesn't separate an olympic gymnast from an olympic target shooter.<br /> <br /> So if you want to be a heavy, accurate boxer, like let's say George Foreman, you can't.<br /> <br /> You can't just be the world's best archer, while not having the physical characteristics of a world class acrobat, sprint runner and climber.<br /> <br /> The simulationist nature of the system already fails in that regard.<br /> <br /> So I don't see why substituting Str for Dex in an attack pool is somehow an unnacceptable corruption of an already corrupted simulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T14:33:40-07:00","id":1239048,"title":"","content":"Exalted isn't really a simulation heavy system.<br /> <br /> And why can't you make George Foreman? You're making a lot of assumptions about how a character looks based on their Attributes. The idea that specific visual aesthetics are inherently tied to Attributes simply isn't true in Exalted. You can make a big bulky looking character that still has high Dexterity.<br /> <br /> And, of course, there's always an abstraction issue as long as one trait applies to more than one activity. As long as any Attribute does more than one thing, you can't make the world's best person at one of those things, that doesn't have the same maxed out Attribute for whatever else it does. But that's why we have Attributes and Abilities as I noted in my last post. Taking Dexterity 5/Archery 5 to make the world's best archer doesn't inherently mean you have the Athletics to make you a particularly special sprinter or climber, or Performance to be a great acrobat.<br /> <br /> For mortals it doesn't matter if you have Dexterity 5/Athletics 1, or Dexterity 3/Athletics 3 in terms of your basic aptitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T15:03:01-07:00","id":1239051,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> <br /> \u200bThe simulation was addressed at the statement on accuracy and moving targets, and what the engine was trying to simulate.<br /> <br /> Who is talking about what a character looks like?<br /> <br /> I was talking about making a character who is the best possible at hitting with punches but can't do a backflip.<br /> <br /> If you have Dex 5 your pool is equal or better at any sport than most trained people at whatever physical activity that is not lifting weights.<br /> <br /> If you have Dex 5 you are the equal of a Dex 2 pro sprinter (Athletics 3). And you haven't even dedicated anything to Athletics. You'll also be as skilled with a bow as the town's best hunter, as good in a knifefight as the best local toughs and as effective with a sword as the captain of the guard. With 0 invested in the respective Abilities.<br /> <br /> If you have Dex 5 you can learn the basics of boxing and start hitting like a pro in a week, and you can start at the tracks and be town champ in a week. If you have Dex 3 you can't.<br /> <br /> This matters to mortals, and to anyone really.<br /> <br /> That is why Attributes are more expensive, they are much broader and serve you much better than Abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T16:19:47-07:00","id":1239070,"title":"","content":"Wow I leave for work for a day and things blow up.<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can address some points when I get back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T16:55:47-07:00","id":1239079,"title":"","content":"Having watched some footage of George Foreman fighting, I'll admit that to my extremely layman's eye, he does make something of a case for throwing punches that don't look like the fastest/least telegraphed that I've ever seen, but appear to have a lot of weight behind them.<br /> <br /> Irrespective of this subject, I actually want to go and look for anything that might analyse his style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239070#post1239070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow I leave for work for a day and things blow up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you want ants? Because this is how you get ants.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T17:49:24-07:00","id":1239109,"title":"","content":"edit: wrong thread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T18:51:12-07:00","id":1239139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238912#post1238912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's a case of wanting to roll Strength in Accuracy rolls, then I feel as though it kind of becomes a case of playing a fast character, just that their fast because of Strength rather than Dexterity. And if Strength is still calculated in damage rolls, being able to pull double duty seems as though it undermines Dexterity a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I've been in combat encounters where my character's inability to do much damage was a significant limiting factor.<br /> I wouldn't expect to be taken seriously if I said that I envisioned my strength 2 character as an elegant, graceful killing machine rather than a hulking brute and thus should determine raw damage with Dexterity instead of Strength without a charm purchase or merit.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T18:57:08-07:00","id":1239145,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=TGUEIROS;n1239051]Who is talking about what a character looks like?[/quote<br /> <br /> Your post sounded a lot more aesthetic based than mechanic based.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was talking about making a character who is the best possible at hitting with punches but can't do a backflip. </div> </div> </div>Which I addressed pretty directly. Attributes are broad abstract traits that cover a lot of things. Abilities are the primary way the game specializes, followed by Merits/Flaws, and Specialties (though Charms go above all that).<br /> <br /> I mean, we can play the &quot;I want a character that's the best at X, but can't do Y, where X and Y both benefit from the same Attribute,&quot; dance to absurd levels.<br /> <br /> I want a character that can throw the world's best uppercut, but is shit at jabs... what do you suggest I do about this? Even if uppercuts were Strength and jabs are Dexterity, I'd have Brawl 5 for a decent jab pool not a shitty one.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the answer is just going to be, &quot;it's too specific to care about.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have Dex 5 your pool is equal or better at any sport than most trained people at whatever physical activity that is not lifting weights. </div> </div> </div>Sounds more like a case to bring back untrained penalties than adding free Attribute switching.<br /> <br /> And a lot of this is just how 3e defines traits with 4s and 5s being ridiculously rare for normal folks to have, but regular for Exalts to have. But this also applies to every Attribute. Strength 5 lets you do Strength based stuff without the appropriate Ability on par with what most towns best people can do. Appearance 5 will let you out social 99% of mortals in Creation even if you don't take any social Abilities (worse here, because you'll get the high App bonus, not just a good base dice poll by normal folk standards).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have Dex 5 you can learn the basics of boxing and start hitting like a pro in a week, and you can start at the tracks and be town champ in a week. If you have Dex 3 you can't. </div> </div> </div>Not really... and we're talking a mighty 2 dice difference here. This doesn't account for damage, soak (or lasting power in general for boxing which doesn't really work well under the base combat rules), footwork, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239079#post1239079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having watched some footage of George Foreman fighting, I'll admit that to my extremely layman's eye, he does make something of a case for throwing punches that don't look like the fastest/least telegraphed that I've ever seen, but appear to have a lot of weight behind them.<br /> <br /> Irrespective of this subject, I actually want to go and look for anything that might analyse his style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Foreman was a KO artist for the majority of his career (he adapted later during his comebacks as his age forced him to adjust his approach).<br /> <br /> His general style involved hitting people as hard as possible as soon as possible. While Foreman could take hits, he didn't have the best endurance, and his loses tended to involve longer fights.<br /> <br /> He tended to struggle with two types of opponents: good counter-punchers that could take his hits and return them to wear him down (basically how Ali beat him in at the Rumble in the Jungle), and aggressive more nimble fighters that could get hits in to throw his offense off kilter.<br /> <br /> It's important, when watching boxing, to remember the sport aspect of it. Weight classes skew perceptions because members of the same weight class look very close in terms of things like speed and all, but it's because you're seeing them in comparison to each other, not compared to everyday folks. As well, there are how scoring influences how boxers are trained. Boxers need to throw a bunch of &quot;showy&quot; hits that might not actually do much to impress the judges. Boxers throw a lot of punches in a bout, and scoring if the fight goes the distance is largely about perception of control over the fight, and landing 'big' hits. You want to throw a good number of &quot;slow&quot; punches so the judges see them, otherwise your ten body shots that are really wearing your opponent down might not mean anything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T18:58:47-07:00","id":1239148,"title":"","content":"For a second, I flirted with the thought of &quot;use higher of Str or Dex for Attack Roll, use the lower for Damage&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your forceful attack is difficult to get around, but the placement defines how much it actually damages.<br /> <br /> Kinda washes things out though, unless it is a conscious choice, &quot;i'll use the lower of my stats to attack, so that I can get a higher guaranteed damage pool&quot; but then we are back to how weapon stats are. You would have to have just the right spread for that to actually be advantageous thanks for Extra Successes adding to damage.<br /> <br /> edit: I had also run into the same problem called out up thread, about trying to work in some way for damage pool disparity to factor in to parries. I made a spreadsheet. Even just a simple additional check of my base damage to yours is just one more check in an already complex resolution system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 07-26-2018, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T20:45:19-07:00","id":1239180,"title":"","content":"Holy crap I wish I had two monitors doing this. It\u2019s painful on one screen. I\u2019ll just address things by post number at a time with the name next to it. I\u2019m not quoting multiple times.<br /> <br /> <b>#22 Cheshire Cat</b> \u2013 Please read my original post. I am not against alternate attributes if used in new and interesting ways. Using Strength for an attack pool is nothing new or interesting, in fact it has been done multiple times over tons of RPG\u2019s. Why is Exalted different? And to address what you said in #24, no. Accuracy is only a stopgap. Trying to hit someone when you have 2 DEX and they have DEX 5 (assuming 5 in each combat ability)? It is suffering. They\u2019ll have two higher defense than you if they also slam an excellency or defense booster. This is not good.<br /> <br /> <b>#25 Steamfunk</b> \u2013 Why not cut out the middleman then? If we have a charm that allows us to use Stamina as parry and you want to make charm spawning off that that allows you to do something like apply a penalty to the opponent\u2019s defense because of how damn tough you are, why not just skip the charm that is essentially a tax to let you do a cool thing and just get to the cool thing already?<br /> <br /> <b>#28 AnubisXy</b> \u2013 Four abilities! Oh boy! \u2026That all use Dex. Yea unless you\u2019re a Dragonblooded then sorry honey you\u2019re getting shafted on your dice pools.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt's not something that needs to be baked into the base system because it's not an issue for people who aren't purchasing Attribute based Charms.\u201d<br /> <br /> Horsecrap. I remember a similar line in 2.Xe. \u201cWe don\u2019t need a new system, what we have is fine if you just pretend it doesn\u2019t exist because I don\u2019t have a problem with it. Thing is going \u201cLALALA I\u2019M NOT NOTICING ANYTHING LALALA\u201d isn\u2019t going to make the problem go away. Its still there, it still a newbie hazing ritual. It should be dragged behind the barn and shot at with the rest of the 2.Xe scared mechanics cows, only it appears Holdorke ran out of ammo and it was spared.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not advocating burning all of 3e, but I advocating why this is a dumb and annoying precedent the game will be setting that can be changed now without another +100 pages of errata.<br /> <br /> <b>#30 Isator Levi</b> \u2013 It doesn\u2019t undermine too much. You get a potential +4 damage boost. Its not gamebreaking, especially when Dexterity can still kite. In fact I find it a cool incentive for Melee/Brawl users: Do I go Strength to make my attacks really have weight with charms that run off them or do I go Dexterity for that sweet movement?<br /> <br /> <b>#31 Elfive</b> \u2013 Yea pretty much my thoughts as well.<br /> <br /> <b>#32 Steamfunk</b> \u2013 You can do such a thing but that way often lies madness. You\u2019d need to add quite a bit of stuff, not as much rewriting though.<br /> <br /> <b>#35 Morty</b> \u2013 I\u2019m happy I\u2019m not taking crazy pills it seems.<br /> <br /> <b>#36 Elfive</b> \u2013 I\u2019ve seen the \u201cSTR is used as 2e APP was for Parry\u201d and that way lies madness, or at least making things more complicated. The easier fix is just using Strength, but I have seen your way done.<br /> <br /> <b>#41 Fenrir666</b> \u2013 I wouldn\u2019t throw everything out with it. I\u2019d still only make one of two attributes used for a defense/attack pool rather than everything, make certain charms that let you use them in unique and odd ways. If you\u2019re letting people use any attribute for an attack you might as well just set dice pools at 5+ability.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should finish making that magic system so people can attack with Intelligence.<br /> <br /> <b>#47 Paradim</b> \u2013 Yes actually. Fire and Stones Strike can kinda be like that, but I toyed around with the idea in my latest artifact. Check out River Rushes Around Rock <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/193Ry6qV0rCuHF-ksc5H_05catVHoOXgJs9K7a_PK-mw/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <b>#48 TalosX</b> \u2013 See my reply to AnubisXy\u2019s post. Just because you don\u2019t have a problem with it doesn\u2019t mean others have not. If you want to use numbers as an example I\u2019ve been in 10 3e games with at least 30 people and probably just as many 2e games (Three of which were long term). In 2e a common conversation was:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cCan I attack with strength?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut there\u2019s a Brutal Attack background in this book!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFirst that\u2019s Scroll of Kings, burn that book. Second Strength to attack is overpowered. Lunars become gods, Increasing Strength Exercise becomes gross, monsters with fuckhuge strength totals become monsters, its just gross. Ignore.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh\u2026 OK\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Also people could usually wipe the floor with anything in the 2e corebook (minus Mask of Winters). BIG enemies later in the line will be much deadlier. This isn\u2019t saying \u201cOh your PC\u2019s didn\u2019t minmax right\u201d, just purely their powers are going to do it. Watch: Lunars is going to advance the charmtech by quite a bit. Not just because of Lunar doing Lunar charms, but because some charms are going to do neat things in new ways. Maybe we\u2019ll have better war charms. That\u2019d be nice. Then we have a flood of homebrew until we eventually get Glories 2.0.<br /> <br /> <b>#51 Heavy Arms</b> \u2013 They\u2019re equilvant because they\u2019re feat taxes. The \u201cGet this or you are stupid\u201d charms. The ones that don\u2019t make your concept fun, but merely remotely viable.<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies is going to be a Lunar thing as well. Dragonblooded excellencies are (in principle) give bonuses built in. Rerolling 6\u2019s on damage for 1m? Damn son. Reducing the cost of your Melee excellency each time it is used? Holy shit! Some charms are indeed bad or boring (Dice or successes\u2026 Yay?), but I\u2019ll be taking a chainsaw to those later. Vance made the entire set and after making two splats I know the pain he went through but worse to get it done in a deadline.<br /> <br /> There is an objective flaw in the system. See above. Just because you ignore it and pretend it doesn\u2019t exist doesn\u2019t mean its not there. Its not as major as paranoia combat and if it isn\u2019t fixed? Fuck it, there\u2019s still other things that are worse in the game by far (Sail, Craft). You\u2019re correct it doesn\u2019t need a band-aid. The band-aids are charms. What we need to do is remove a tumor before it grows and becomes a pain in the ass to remove later.<br /> <br /> I have read Storypath and also know how it works very well. Let me tell you this: 3e isn\u2019t as fragile as you think. I attempt to push the system for fun, you really think I wouldn\u2019t know its limits?<br /> <br /> \u201c&gt;Get around it with house rules!\u201d<br /> <br /> Rule 0 fallacy.<br /> <br /> And by using your lumbering titan issue you proved exactly my point. Dex characters can kite for ages and can destroy slower ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 07-26-2018, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T20:56:33-07:00","id":1239183,"title":"","content":"Man, I'd only heard legends of Lunar threads; I gotta say, this mess does -not- disappoint. I'm inclined to agree that using one ability in place of another <i>could</i> be tricky to balance, but like, man, never too early to extrapolate from a handful of datapoints, freak all the way out about something, and histrionically insist that everyone else is wrong I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T21:13:07-07:00","id":1239188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239183#post1239183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I'd only heard legends of Lunar threads; I gotta say, this mess does -not- disappoint. I'm inclined to agree that using one ability in place of another <i>could</i> be tricky to balance, but like, man, never too early to extrapolate from a handful of datapoints, freak all the way out about something, and histrionically insist that everyone else is wrong I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less of Lunars, more of a general thread about a certain topic in the game.<br /> <br /> But yes if writing two splats, nearly a thousand pages of material, stress testing both 2e and 3e constantly, countless hours playing games and talking to other players and Gamemasters, similar experiences with other people and using logic to introduce points as &quot;insisting everyone else is wrong&quot; isn't enough qualification? Then oh well I guess I'll hang my hat up.<br /> <br /> If you got a point then say it. Don't hide behind passive aggressive language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 07-27-2018, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T21:44:49-07:00","id":1239194,"title":"","content":"Also the archetypal barbarian warlord - <i>you know the one</i> - was hardly the uncoordinated slab of beef folks might be trying to paint him as; he was agile enough to sneak undetected through hostile territory while wearing armor, dexterous enough to scale sheer surfaces barehanded, and quick enough to make <i>throwing a treasure chest</i> into a surprise attack.<br /> <br /> Robert E. Howard's brain-child would not be represented as just having Strength 5; his other physical attributes were equally impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-27-2018, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T23:39:25-07:00","id":1239206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239180#post1239180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not cut out the middleman then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the middleman can still be cool and/or valuable enough to warrant a cost of its own.<br /> <br /> By your logic, why shouldn't a Charm like Excellent Strike not just be part of a Solar's free Excellency, so they can get to Fire and Stone Strike, and One Weapon, Two Blows, without a middleman? Your logic isn't based on whether or not the effect is useful, just that it isn't 'special' enough. So why is Excellent Strike not something that's just default free for Solar Melee?<br /> <br /> Being able to parry with Stamina is already a &quot;cool thing&quot; you're buying a Charm to do. More Charms building off that, that do even more cool things, is how all Charms work: tress that build on a theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I remember a similar line in 2.Xe. </div> </div> </div>So what? I remember people saying lots of stuff about 2e. Sometimes the people arguing that something with it wasn't broken were right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019m not advocating burning all of 3e, but I advocating why this is a dumb and annoying precedent the game will be setting that can be changed now without another +100 pages of errata. </div> </div> </div>And you're doing a piss poor job of advocating for it, because you're still just gong, &quot;this is dumb because I say so, and despite being said I need to actually justify this, I don't because... feat tax!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See my reply to AnubisXy\u2019s post. Just because you don\u2019t have a problem with it doesn\u2019t mean others have not. </div> </div> </div>And the same goes the other way. Just because you have a problem with it, doesn't mean others will. Your personal preferences are not adequate proof of a fundamental flaw in the system that needs to be fixed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then we have a flood of homebrew... </div> </div> </div>Who cares? Homebrew isn't official material that matters to how the books do things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They\u2019re equilvant because they\u2019re feat taxes. </div> </div> </div>That doesn't make any sense. I(A)M isn't a feat tax, it's a bad Charm that broke the mote economy... it's only effect was to reduce the mote cost of other Charms. &quot;Feat tax&quot; as you're using it, is a meaningless phrase that amounts to being, &quot;I don't like it but I don't want to have to actually explain why in a fully thought out fashion!&quot;<br /> <br /> And I directly addressed I(A)M in detail, which you're skipping, which only reaffirms you don't have a reason beyond wanting the devs to make your preferences the official rules instead of actually caring about improving the game for as many people as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The \u201cGet this or you are stupid\u201d charms. The ones that don\u2019t make your concept fun, but merely remotely viable. </div> </div> </div>This is fundamentally just a matter of perspective. If my concept includes &quot;wrestling giant monsters,&quot; there's a specific Brawl Charm my Solar needs to buy. Does that make it no longer a fun Charm because I designed a character specifically around doing that awesome thing?<br /> <br /> Yes, not every Charm is equally, &quot;get this or you're stupid,&quot; but the majority of Charms relevant to whatever your concept is, are ones you want to buy. So this doesn't work as a clarification; how many Essence 1 Solar Charms aren't &quot;get this or you are stupid&quot; if you want to be good at that Ability? How many of them are bread and butter Charms that are more about functioning at higher level, than they are flashy effects?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Free Excellencies is going to be a Lunar thing as well. </div> </div> </div>You saw me say &quot;Celestial&quot; there, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dragonblooded excellencies are (in principle) give bonuses built in. </div> </div> </div>You still need to buy them, which you're saying is bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is an objective flaw in the system. See above. </div> </div> </div>Above contains no objective flaw demonstrated in the system. Repeatedly saying it's there when you haven't actually demonstrated it's there doesn't mean it's there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let me tell you this: 3e isn\u2019t as fragile as you think. </div> </div> </div>You don't know what I &quot;think.&quot; And I didn't call it fragile, I simply said that the Charms being based on Attributes and Abilities necessitates a heavier hand on Attribute and Ability default assignments than a game where powers don't have default links to traits like that. This is actually less about it being fragile, and more about that big concern of yours: newbie traps. If you make Attribute assignment more flexible, you make it harder to avoid creating Charms that screw newbies that didn't invest in Attribute B because they thought they only had to worry about Attribute A to be effective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I attempt to push the system for fun, you really think I wouldn\u2019t know its limits? </div> </div> </div>I don't think your own ego is proof of your knowledge or whether or not you're correct on any specific issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rule 0 fallacy. </div> </div> </div>Nope. I never asserted that the system isn't broken because you can fix it. I said that you having a preference that's different from the primary design of the game, and house ruling the game to fit the preference, isn't proof that the system is broken.<br /> <br /> You're just tossing out buzzwords to paper over you haven't demonstrated a break in the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And by using your lumbering titan issue you proved exactly my point. Dex characters can kite for ages and can destroy slower ones. </div> </div> </div>How does this prove anything about your points? It just proves that combat is a lot more complicated than maxing out your to-hit dice-pool.<br /> <br /> Your assertion here also further demonstrates your poor argumentation as you ignore how Abilities factor into these things. Mobility is not just how much Dex you have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239188#post1239188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...using logic to introduce points...</div> </div> </div> </div>Facts not in evidence.<br /> <br /> Also, listing off your bone fides doesn't mean anything if you're not applying them in a useful fashion. Someone with 1% of the experience you're claiming would look at the push back in this thread and consider that it's more likely they failed to adequately communicate their base assertions than everyone else being wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't hide behind passive aggressive language. </div> </div> </div>Ah, the good old, &quot;I'm right, so I'm allowed to be an ass, but everyone else has to treat me like the Queen or they get dismissed,&quot; bullcrap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T00:36:01-07:00","id":1239216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239180#post1239180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>#48 TalosX</b> \u2013 See my reply to AnubisXy\u2019s post. Just because you don\u2019t have a problem with it doesn\u2019t mean others have not. If you want to use numbers as an example I\u2019ve been in 10 3e games with at least 30 people and probably just as many 2e games (Three of which were long term). In 2e a common conversation was:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cCan I attack with strength?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut there\u2019s a Brutal Attack background in this book!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFirst that\u2019s Scroll of Kings, burn that book. Second Strength to attack is overpowered. Lunars become gods, Increasing Strength Exercise becomes gross, monsters with fuckhuge strength totals become monsters, its just gross. Ignore.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh\u2026 OK\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Also people could usually wipe the floor with anything in the 2e corebook (minus Mask of Winters). BIG enemies later in the line will be much deadlier. This isn\u2019t saying \u201cOh your PC\u2019s didn\u2019t minmax right\u201d, just purely their powers are going to do it. Watch: Lunars is going to advance the charmtech by quite a bit. Not just because of Lunar doing Lunar charms, but because some charms are going to do neat things in new ways. Maybe we\u2019ll have better war charms. That\u2019d be nice. Then we have a flood of homebrew until we eventually get Glories 2.0.</div> </div> </div> </div>This literally has almost nothing to do with my point. My point was you do not need 5 dots of Dex to hit someone in combat. However, you're response was about Str replacing Dex. Okay, we'll discuss that if you want. Lunar's already do it, but I don't believe Solars or Dragonbloods need it. Though nothing really breaks if you give Solars/Dragonbloods a &quot;use Str instead of Dex for attacks&quot; charm. If that's what you want, well that's why we have the Golden Rule! You don't even need the Golden Rule though, the devs encourage charm development.<br /> <br /> So about not needing 5 dots in Dex and/or relevant combat abilities. Your belief that much deadlier opponents yet to be released will change this, is flawed. The devs have stated and reiterated multiple times that 3E will remain a lower level game then previous editions. Those same devs have confirmed it was Essence 3 exalts that defeated the Primordials. The days of being required to have 5 dots in every applicable ability and attribute to fight end-game monsters died with 2E. The evidence is already starting to pile-up. We've got multiple monsters and NPC via &quot;Hundred Devils Night Parade&quot; and &quot;Adversaries of the Righteous&quot;. Not one of them, not even the behemoths require you to max out every combat stat to compete with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T01:17:02-07:00","id":1239224,"title":"","content":"Damn. I am getting some serious flashbacks to 2008 right now. O.O","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T03:04:04-07:00","id":1239235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238956#post1238956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I love how you're incapable of wrapping your mind around such advanced concepts as <i>abstractions.</i> His hit rate is 100, his damage is 45. His enemy has 40 health and a 15% chance to hit him for zero damage.<br /> <br /> This paints the picture of someone too fast to defeat in single combat, able to block any hit, and tank any hit that he can't block, while dealing out one hit KOs.<br /> <br /> I hope that these concepts aren't completely beyond your ability to grasp, if you'd like, I can dumb the math down a little for you. Do you need me to explain basic percentiles?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Cut this sort of thing out if you want to keep posting here. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T07:10:02-07:00","id":1239294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239139#post1239139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, I've been in combat encounters where my character's inability to do much damage was a significant limiting factor.<br /> I wouldn't expect to be taken seriously if I said that I envisioned my strength 2 character as an elegant, graceful killing machine rather than a hulking brute and thus should determine raw damage with Dexterity instead of Strength without a charm purchase or merit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm... Your Dexterity already affects your damage as a result of the withering attack roll? So you are already getting that...<br /> <br /> So should the system not be taken seriously either?<br /> <br /> EDIT: So yeah, I even forgot to add this to the Dex God Stat list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 07-27-2018, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T07:25:21-07:00","id":1239300,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> <br /> You were the one who made dice pools comparisons, but then when they don't serve your purpose they are irrelevant? The fact is that a person with Dex 5 can easily equal whatever a Dex2/3 character with an Ability at 3 can, with the Ability at 1.<br /> <br /> 2 dice is a great advantage, and could easily determine success or failure.<br /> <br /> That point that system is full of abstractions is what invalidates this notion that a hit must connect due to dexterous accuracy.<br /> <br /> We are simply making the argument that a hit could also connect due to raw power. <br /> <br /> It is not as ludicrous as what people try to paint it as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T07:37:17-07:00","id":1239303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239216#post1239216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This literally has almost nothing to do with my point. My point was you do not need 5 dots of Dex to hit someone in combat. However, you're response was about Str replacing Dex. Okay, we'll discuss that if you want. Lunar's already do it, but I don't believe Solars or Dragonbloods need it. Though nothing really breaks if you give Solars/Dragonbloods a &quot;use Str instead of Dex for attacks&quot; charm. If that's what you want, well that's why we have the Golden Rule! You don't even need the Golden Rule though, the devs encourage charm development.</div> </div> </div> </div>Golden rule is useless for games that you don't run. Asking for an alternative to be baked into the rules means you don't have to argue every game with stubborn RAW STs, or people who insist that it's not broken, don't fix it, you can't attack with strength so you'd better have Dex 5.<br /> <br /> Also, for reals? I was in a game with a character with Dex 3, Strength 5, Stamina 5 and a heavy weapon. They were a <i>joke</i> compared to the PCs with Dex 5 and medium weapons. Not even a funny joke. It was a major reveal of a system failing: &quot;Fuck you for choosing strength over speed&quot; is still in effect. The result was a damn farce right out of Second Edition.<br /> <br /> And, bluntly, there had <i>better</i> be at least <i>some</i> monsters written to challenge people who optimize their characters for greater effect. I'm getting pretty sick of having to massively buff NPC statblocks so that they can be more than a speedbump for Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T08:04:24-07:00","id":1239312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239303#post1239303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, bluntly, there had <i>better</i> be at least <i>some</i> monsters written to challenge people who optimize their characters for greater effect. I'm getting pretty sick of having to massively buff NPC statblocks so that they can be more than a speedbump for Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially if you encourage characters to start with maximized stats to actually be able to access any of their decent supernal charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 07-27-2018, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T08:15:16-07:00","id":1239315,"title":"","content":"Honestly, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1183_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1183\" data-vbnamecard=\"1183\">Sandact6</a> you want to know why it's appropriate and fair and useful to have stat swaps for lunars? <br /> <br /> Because when I'm building a lunar character and I see all the awesome charms I want to take in Stamina or Strength or (etc.) I have to invest in those stats to meet charm prerequisites. If I invest in those stats that means I can't invest in other stats. I have limited resources. And buying attributes up later is <i>hella</i> expensive.<br /> <br /> The Devs wanted to put awesome stuff into <i>every</i> attribute. But Dex is still a god stat. So by allowing a character to swap out attributes, they can make dex NOT a god stat and thus a character is free to invest where they actually want to without facing potentially months or years of play where their character can't get the charms they actually wanted or where they are real danger of dying in combat because they didnt' invest enough in dex so their attack pools, parry <i>and</i> dodge are all shit. <br /> <br /> &quot;But wait Armyofwhispers&quot; you say! &quot;This is why I'm advocating that you can just swap out any attribute with a relevant stunt&quot; <br /> <br /> Problem is that this solution is way too freaking broad! This problem does not exist for Dragon Bloods and Solars. Nor would it exist for any ability splat. The investment to get to cool charms for a DB or a Solar is pennies compared to dollars when measured against the investment to raise attributes.<br /> <br /> Now you may not like swapping attributes as charm purchases. That's fine. There's simply no way it will work as a 'stunt it and it works whenever you want' or, like others have said in this thread, you may as well just have abilities and always assume you're adding +5 to the roll because your solution <i>breaks the system over its knee</i>. <br /> <br /> So I propose a different alternative: You could houserule that each caste of lunars gets an extra anima power that allows them to swap out their respective attributes as needed. IE Full moon can swap STR, DEX, and STA. Then you can safely strip out the charm purchases that so offend you without problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T08:27:32-07:00","id":1239317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239303#post1239303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Golden rule is useless for games that you don't run. Asking for an alternative to be baked into the rules means you don't have to argue every game with stubborn RAW STs, or people who insist that it's not broken, don't fix it, you can't attack with strength so you'd better have Dex 5.<br /> <br /> Also, for reals? I was in a game with a character with Dex 3, Strength 5, Stamina 5 and a heavy weapon. They were a <i>joke</i> compared to the PCs with Dex 5 and medium weapons. Not even a funny joke. It was a major reveal of a system failing: &quot;Fuck you for choosing strength over speed&quot; is still in effect. The result was a damn farce right out of Second Edition.<br /> <br /> And, bluntly, there had <i>better</i> be at least <i>some</i> monsters written to challenge people who optimize their characters for greater effect. I'm getting pretty sick of having to massively buff NPC statblocks so that they can be more than a speedbump for Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're buffing enemy stats and then complaining when characters without perfect optimization can't compete? Wow... just wow! You've already lost any credibility when discussing the mechanics, but let's do some math anyway:<br /> <br /> Let's say a solar character named Bob has a 3 Dex, and a 4 Melee, with no applicable specialization. We'll give Bob a medium non-artifact weapon, say a standard long sword. Bob is currently at 9 dice to attack. Now Bob's player being fairly new to stunting, only manages a 1-point stunt (+2 dice). So now Bob's rolling 11 dice. Bob also has use of the excellency for Melee, literally the least efficient way to get bonus dice for Solar Melee. However, Bob's worried about glowing in public, so he limits that to 3 motes. Bringing his total dice pool to 14. That's, mathematically speaking, about 7 successes on average. Do you know what 7 successes hits... Every single antagonist in the Core, Hundred Devil Night Parade, and Adversaries of the Righteous. This is a character that's not even remotely optimized. Bob isn't even pushing himself, he could clearly boost his dice pool more if he chose too. The point is, he doesn't need too. Bob is a perfectly valid character, unless he gets a ST who decides to break the RAW. At that point, it isn't Bob or the mechanics that are the issue, it's the ST!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T08:59:28-07:00","id":1239328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239300#post1239300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You were the one who made dice pools comparisons, but then when they don't serve your purpose they are irrelevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a comparison for a specific reason. That doesn't actually mean all numerical comparisons are relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 dice is a great advantage, and could easily determine success or failure. </div> </div> </div>It's a significant advantage in the system, sure, but if my character's life was on the line, I wouldn't trust two dice to carry the day by itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That point that system is full of abstractions is what invalidates this notion that a hit must connect due to dexterous accuracy. </div> </div> </div>Except it doesn't. Abstractions only mean that the way Exalted does isn't the only way to abstract it, not that Exalted is broken/wrong for abstracting it the way it does. Whether or not Exalted should abstract things differently requires a stronger case than, &quot;you can do it differently.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We are simply making the argument that a hit could also connect due to raw power. </div> </div> </div>Well not really. The case for Strength as the default close combat attack Attribute (that goes back to D&amp;D and all) isn't that raw power is accurate, but that in abstracting what &quot;strength&quot; is, things like muscle speed - and hence accuracy in hand-to-hand combat - are covered by the abstract concept of &quot;strength.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's, as I've said, where you put something in the abstraction. Strength based close combat defaults aren't about &quot;accurate&quot; raw power. It's about putting accuracy and raw power in the same abstract trait, just like foot-speed and hand-eye coordination are both in the same abstract trait; not inherently saying the two are the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is not as ludicrous as what people try to paint it as. </div> </div> </div>Having Strength be the default close combat Attribute isn't ludicrous.<br /> <br /> Insisting that your accuracy derives from raw power is actually ludicrous, even if it isn't ludicrous to abstract raw power and accuracy from the same trait.<br /> <br /> Insisting that Exalted is broken for not allowing Strength to be a close combat accuracy trait (which is the whole point of the thread) for free instead of gated behind Charms is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239303#post1239303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asking for an alternative to be baked into the rules means you don't have to argue every game with stubborn RAW STs, or people who insist that it's not broken, don't fix it, you can't attack with strength so you'd better have Dex 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or be a Grapple Solar, or a [whatever] Lunar, since you can make more Strength based attacks with your primary attacks as either Exalt.<br /> <br /> The thing is, it isn't broken. And you don't need Dex 5 to have fun with the game a a combat character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, for reals? I was in a game with a character with Dex 3, Strength 5, Stamina 5 and a heavy weapon. They were a <i>joke</i> compared to the PCs with Dex 5 and medium weapons. </div> </div> </div>As these forums have discussed, a lot, heavy vs medium weapons is a significant contributor here that can't be discounted. A normal medium weapons +2 accuracy and +2 Defense advantage over a normal heavy weapons +2 raw damage advantage makes heavy weapons a joke outside of very specific circumstances (esp. since most are two-handed).<br /> <br /> The weapon blocks are totally something you'll see plenty of support for something that should be fixed; and something that doesn't even screw with anything other than NPC stat blocks when it comes to the rest of the system. Because they're actually broken in that weapon choice is not up to style while heavy weapons are objectively horrible choices unless you're fighting low DV high soak enemies that aren't too low DV that the higher damage doesn't matter (esp. with the right tags) and/or too high soak for it to not matter anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, bluntly, there had <i>better</i> be at least <i>some</i> monsters written to challenge people who optimize their characters for greater effect. </div> </div> </div>Eh.<br /> <br /> Better to continue focusing on non-optimized antagonists. Lots of people don't play Exalted for optimization, so TPK NPC stat blocks are useless to them, and it's far easier to buff NPC stat blocks if your players are steamrolling them and not enjoying being so badass, than it is to nerf them if they're too strong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T09:11:06-07:00","id":1239330,"title":"","content":"The problem here, essentially, is when Bob's character feels like a chump because someone else has made a character with Dex 5, Melee 5, a speciality, and a medium weapon (so... 2 freebie points, that's it), who is rolling 13 dice without a stunt or motes.<br /> And then the ST has to start bringing out more powerful foes to challenge the more optimized character, and now Bob's struggling. Plus the other guy has Defence 7 while Bob has 3.<br /> <br /> I ran a game that had some pretty optimized characters, so the guy with Dex 4/Melee 5 and the girl with Dex 3/Thrown 3 looked pretty rubbish. And all the NPCs in the book were pretty crap, only by ambushing half the party while the others were away, with an alpha-strike, and bringing 100 war-gods, was even the Essence 6 Ahlat able to do serious damage... To one PC.<br /> <br /> I eventually stopped running the game partly because the only way I could remotely challenge the party was with NPCs with 30 charms I had to write myself. The antagonist section was useless.<br /> <br /> <br /> In short, the problem Fenrir's talking about is a real problem; the NPCs in the book are way too easy, and non-optimized characters do look pretty poor. And this is a little bit because of how god-statty Dex is, but it's mostly because optimising characters is way too easy.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the best way for an ST to fix these problems is to change character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-27-2018, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T09:19:54-07:00","id":1239334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239330#post1239330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then<b> the ST has to start bringing out more powerful foes to challenge the more optimized character</b>, and now Bob's struggling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why assume this? Is the ST required to create divine QCs with Bureaucracy/Sail dice pools in the twenties to challenge the Eclipse?<br /> <br /> By-the-book enemies stayed relevant to combats for the entire run of my Okeanos game. Adding a pair of extra hobgoblins to a fight adds to the challenge with <i>far</i> less risk of shutting out a player from contributing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-27-2018, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T09:30:12-07:00","id":1239337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239294#post1239294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... Your Dexterity already affects your damage as a result of the withering attack roll? So you are already getting that...<br /> <br /> So should the system not be taken seriously either?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on threshold successes over their defence.<br /> Do I seriously need to explain the difference between that and adding an attribute directly to your weapon damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T09:34:24-07:00","id":1239340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239317#post1239317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're buffing enemy stats and then complaining when characters without perfect optimization can't compete? Wow... just wow! You've already lost any credibility when discussing the mechanics, but let's do some math anyway:<br /> <br /> Let's say a solar character named Bob has a 3 Dex, and a 4 Melee, with no applicable specialization. We'll give Bob a medium non-artifact weapon, say a standard long sword. Bob is currently at 9 dice to attack. Now Bob's player being fairly new to stunting, only manages a 1-point stunt (+2 dice). So now Bob's rolling 11 dice. Bob also has use of the excellency for Melee, literally the least efficient way to get bonus dice for Solar Melee. However, Bob's worried about glowing in public, so he limits that to 3 motes. Bringing his total dice pool to 14. That's, mathematically speaking, about 7 successes on average. Do you know what 7 successes hits... Every single antagonist in the Core, Hundred Devil Night Parade, and Adversaries of the Righteous. This is a character that's not even remotely optimized. Bob isn't even pushing himself, he could clearly boost his dice pool more if he chose too. The point is, he doesn't need too. Bob is a perfectly valid character, unless he gets a ST who decides to break the RAW. At that point, it isn't Bob or the mechanics that are the issue, it's the ST!</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't the ST in that game, actually. I was an <i>observer, </i>watching it fall apart despite the enemies being straight from the corebook.<br /> <br /> Because, see, I'm not even talking about perfect optimization. I'm talking about <i>failing to take Dexterity at 5.</i> If I was talking about perfect optimization, I would be referring to how Solars can easily attack 3 times a turn, one of those casually being a Decisive Attack with 10+ initiative. Or how Solars can push their Evasion to 13+ and gain 5 initiative every time someone misses them. But I'm not talking about that. I'm talking about the sheer combat difference between a Medium Artifact Weapon+Dex 5, and Dex3+Heavy Weapon. The difference being a pathetic joke.<br /> <br /> If taking Dex 3, Strength 5 means you have to balance every encounter to have a defense score that can ever be hit by the heavy weapon user, that means the non-heavy weapon user will rapidly end the fight, unless you boost their soak insanely, which leads to this cascading series of patches and I'd really rather just be able to use the higher of Strength or Dex to aim my attacks without having to explain this problem to every storyteller from now until the end of time.<br /> <br /> Serious question: Do you ever actually play Exalted? Really play it? If so, how experienced is your group? Are you guys deliberately not optimizing? Or do people just sorta do whatever? Because in my experience, some players optimize, some do whatever, some sorta optimize, and some like to play people with weird ability spikes. If you have a Circle where everyone is optimizing, there are no problems, so if this is your experience, your reaction makes sense, you'd never have found a problem, but you also wouldn't be assuming I'm an idiot randomly buffing everything, because you would have seen for yourself what happens when someone combines Solar Dodge and Black Claw Style.<br /> <br /> If you play a group where people deliberately do not optimize, or who just sorta throw things together, you <i>also</i> would never have noticed the problem, and this is what I'm kinda assuming, but don't want to <i>just</i> assume, because your reaction makes a lot of sense. The game is very obviously designed to allow anyone to sorta throw stuff together and function.<br /> <br /> Stuff falls apart, though, when you have two people who are trying to be the best they can be, three people with little experience who just sorta throw whatever into line, and one person who just wanted to play a badass giant with low dex and high strength. Because if one PC is even remotely optimized while the others aren't, in the sense one player has 5/5/1 in their specialty and chose Charm combos that play together effectively, and the other players have whatever looks cool, this is <i>really hard to manage.</i> It's even harder if you have three people strategically combining Charms and stats, and three people <i>not</i> doing that.<br /> <br /> But, this isn't what I'm suggesting be addressed, because it's a much more complex failure state that can't easily be addressed, I don't think. The much easier failure state to address is &quot;One player took a heavy weapon and Dex 3, and now consistently fails to hit bosses, who tend to have 5 or 6 defense and are able to raise that&quot;. The Nephwrack can push itself to 8 defense pretty easily. Dex 3, Melee 4, Specialty (Grand Daiklave). That's 8 on Decisive. +5 from Excellency (these were Dragonblooded). That's 13. A max Excellency cannot hit the Nephwrack without being lucky. This, much like Bob, is a very &quot;just throw it together character&quot; who sounds cool.<br /> <br /> And, using just the corebook Charms, they cannot scratch the weakest of the powerful spirit boss enemies. This is something I consider to be a problem. And it's easily solved by saying &quot;Pick the higher of strength or dex to use in combat&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:03:53-07:00","id":1239351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239330#post1239330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem here, essentially, is when Bob's character feels like a chump because someone else has made a character with Dex 5, Melee 5, a speciality, and a medium weapon (so... 2 freebie points, that's it), who is rolling 13 dice without a stunt or motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... no.<br /> <br /> The problem here is basing the value of a character solely on combat pools.<br /> <br /> Having played &quot;Bob&quot; in this, I never felt like a chump, despite playing along side said 11 base pool character. Why? Because let the combat heavy have all the combat stuff. I was good enough at fighting to be an asset in a fight, while letting the player far more invested in kicking ass to the max shine in combat, and I had my investments in other things to let me shine.<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't just combat. Combat is a big part of Exalted, and by default you want to be at least at &quot;Bob&quot; levels so you can contribute to combat. But if you're not maxing out combat? You're probably maxing out something else. Which is good, because that way the group can do more than kill stuff, and characters have different things they can shine at doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, the best way for an ST to fix these problems is to change character creation. </div> </div> </div>Not... really sure how that fixes anything more than shifts stuff around and potentially stifles Charm selection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239340#post1239340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If taking Dex 3, Strength 5 means you have to balance every encounter to have a defense score that can ever be hit by the heavy weapon user,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just make heavy weapons less sucky.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it's easily solved by saying &quot;Pick the higher of strength or dex to use in combat&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Not it isn't. It just means you push people to take Strength 5 or Dexterity 5, instead of Dexterity 5, to maximize accuracy. It doesn't solve any of the issues with different players with different ideas of how to make a character, optimizing vs. not, and all that stuff. It doesn't fix the weapon blocks and tag assignments making specific choices of weapons clearly superior (along with the builds the best support them getting boosted for it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:08:18-07:00","id":1239355,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"800\" data-vbnamecard=\"800\">Fenrir666</a> You keep saying that the guy who consciously build a &quot;I hit really hard but have no accuracy&quot; character not being able to hit stuff consistently is a problem.<br /> <br /> But let's reverse that. Say we implement your idea of swapping out dex or str for attacks rolls Consider two characters, one with Dex primary, one with Str primary. Both using the same weapon, they have the same accuracy. But wait! Now it's the Dex user who's the chump because he's ALWAYS doing less damage! <br /> <br /> In Exalted, Dex and str are both combat attributes but it's a trade off for accuracy vs damage. Oh look, guess what, going for a heavier weapon is ALSO a trade off of accuracy vs damage. Your friends problem was that he simply went too far in the trade off. He doubled down the choice to sacrifice accuracy for damage so he can't hit anything. <br /> <br /> If anyone is at fault for his bad play experience (aside from the guy who went super high damage with no ability to hit anything) it's the ST for not pointing out that the build wouldn't really hit anything.<br /> <br /> tl/dr: your friend built a D&amp;D character in Exalted and was surprised when it failed to perform like a D&amp;D character. This should not be a surprise because <i>Exalted is not and has never been D&amp;D</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:23:27-07:00","id":1239360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239355#post1239355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"800\" data-vbnamecard=\"800\">Fenrir666</a> You keep saying that the guy who consciously build a &quot;I hit really hard but have no accuracy&quot; character not being able to hit stuff consistently is a problem.<br /> <br /> But let's reverse that. Say we implement your idea of swapping out dex or str for attacks rolls Consider two characters, one with Dex primary, one with Str primary. Both using the same weapon, they have the same accuracy. But wait! Now it's the Dex user who's the chump because he's ALWAYS doing less damage!<br /> <br /> In Exalted, Dex and str are both combat attributes but it's a trade off for accuracy vs damage. Oh look, guess what, going for a heavier weapon is ALSO a trade off of accuracy vs damage. Your friends problem was that he simply went too far in the trade off. He doubled down the choice to sacrifice accuracy for damage so he can't hit anything.<br /> <br /> If anyone is at fault for his bad play experience (aside from the guy who went super high damage with no ability to hit anything) it's the ST for not pointing out that the build wouldn't really hit anything.<br /> <br /> tl/dr: your friend built a D&amp;D character in Exalted and was surprised when it failed to perform like a D&amp;D character. This should not be a surprise because <i>Exalted is not and has never been D&amp;D</i></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Exalted shouldn't perform like a game that does it better because then Exalted would be like a game that does stuff better&quot;.<br /> <br /> such a compelling argument. The tradeoff of accuracy versus damage is ridiculously lopsided. Playing Strength 5, Dex 1 should be equally viable as Dex 5, Strength 1. Instead, what we actually get is Dex is a godstat and Strength can be casually dumped with no consequences. Which I do, consistently, because Strength really doesn't matter at all. If your only argument is Exalted's standard contempt for D&amp;D, you really don't have a good argument. Particularly when if it is actually a problem, swap the attfibute bonus around. If you attack with Strength, you add Dex. If you attack with Dex, you add Strength. Bam, <i>done.</i><br /> <br /> Or does D&amp;D do that too, and so must be avoided lest Exalted be like something <i>popular, ewwww?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:45:35-07:00","id":1239365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239337#post1239337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on threshold successes over their defence.<br /> Do I seriously need to explain the difference between that and adding an attribute directly to your weapon damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Dex is already figured into your raw damage calculation by virtue of it being part of the attack roll and the threshold successes of that attack roll os added to raw damage.<br /> <br /> Do I really need to explain that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:46:33-07:00","id":1239366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239360#post1239360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Exalted shouldn't perform like a game that does it better because then Exalted would be like a game that does stuff better&quot;.<br /> <br /> such a compelling argument. The tradeoff of accuracy versus damage is ridiculously lopsided. Playing Strength 5, Dex 1 should be equally viable as Dex 5, Strength 1. Instead, what we actually get is Dex is a godstat and Strength can be casually dumped with no consequences. Which I do, consistently, because Strength really doesn't matter at all. Particularly when if it is actually a problem, swap the attfibute bonus around. If you attack with Strength, you add Dex. If you attack with Dex, you add Strength. Bam, <i>done.</i><br /> <br /> Or does D&amp;D do that too, and so must be avoided lest Exalted be like something <i>popular, ewwww?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I want all characters to be exactly the same and the attributes to be meaningless&quot;<br /> <br /> See how that feels? Now how about you stop deliberately misrepresenting my arguments <br /> <br /> Now moving on to your actual points, leaving out the annoying sarcasm and belittling you seem so prone to.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239360#post1239360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tradeoff of accuracy versus damage is ridiculously lopsided. Playing Strength 5, Dex 1 should be equally viable as Dex 5, Strength 1. Instead, what we actually get is Dex is a godstat and Strength can be casually dumped with no consequences. Which I do, consistently, because Strength really doesn't matter at all. Particularly when if it is actually a problem, swap the attfibute bonus around. If you attack with Strength, you add Dex. If you attack with Dex, you add Strength. Bam, <i>done.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you have correctly identified that the ability to hit things is important when you want to be able to damage things. However, you draw the conclusion that that this is a bad thing which I find problematic. <br /> <br /> You have yet to actually explain why STR 5 DEX 1 <i>should </i>have exactly the same play experience as STR 1 DEX 5. I personally <i>like</i> that they're separate and distinct things in this system.<br /> <br /> You're also missing part of the point of my last post. The difference in stats wasn't the only issue. The difference in weapon types was as much or more to do with the combat disparity <br /> <br /> You can achieve the exact same thing that you're advocating for by making all the weapons have the same accuracy and damage stats. BUT WHY WOULD YOU WANT TO?<br /> <br /> To paraphrase you: If your only argument is that D&amp;D did it then you don't have a good argument.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:50:41-07:00","id":1239370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239328#post1239328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I made a comparison for a specific reason. That doesn't actually mean all numerical comparisons are relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is that even suppost to say?<br /> <br /> That you don't like my comparisons so they are not valid, but you like yours so they are?<br /> <br /> No reasoning or explanation offered, what is the point of even responding?<br /> ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239328#post1239328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a significant advantage in the system, sure, but if my character's life was on the line, I wouldn't trust two dice to carry the day by itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Except it doesn't. Abstractions only mean that the way Exalted does isn't the only way to abstract it, not that Exalted is broken/wrong for abstracting it the way it does. Whether or not Exalted should abstract things differently requires a stronger case than, &quot;you can do it differently.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well not really. The case for Strength as the default close combat attack Attribute (that goes back to D&amp;D and all) isn't that raw power is accurate, but that in abstracting what &quot;strength&quot; is, things like muscle speed - and hence accuracy in hand-to-hand combat - are covered by the abstract concept of &quot;strength.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's, as I've said, where you put something in the abstraction. Strength based close combat defaults aren't about &quot;accurate&quot; raw power. It's about putting accuracy and raw power in the same abstract trait, just like foot-speed and hand-eye coordination are both in the same abstract trait; not inherently saying the two are the same thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Having Strength be the default close combat Attribute isn't ludicrous.<br /> <br /> Insisting that your accuracy derives from raw power is actually ludicrous, even if it isn't ludicrous to abstract raw power and accuracy from the same trait.<br /> <br /> Insisting that Exalted is broken for not allowing Strength to be a close combat accuracy trait (which is the whole point of the thread) for free instead of gated behind Charms is ludicrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>All semantics and opinions with no real engament of the issue and no objective point stated.<br /> <br /> I don't even know why you quote while ranting about Exalted's system being broken, or saying accuracy is derived from raw power, when I said none of those things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 07-27-2018, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:54:26-07:00","id":1239372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239366#post1239366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I want all characters to be exactly the same and the attributes to be meaningless&quot;<br /> <br /> See how that feels? Now how about you stop deliberately misrepresenting my arguments<br /> <br /> Now moving on to your actual points, leaving out the annoying sarcasm and belittling you seem so prone to.<br /> <br /> Yes, you have correctly identified that the ability to hit things is important when you want to be able to damage things. However, you draw the conclusion that that this is a bad thing which I find problematic.<br /> <br /> You have yet to actually explain why STR 5 DEX 1 <i>should </i>have exactly the same play experience as STR 1 DEX 5. I personally <i>like</i> that they're separate and distinct things in this system.<br /> <br /> You're also missing part of the point of my last post. The difference in stats wasn't the only issue. The difference in weapon types was as much or more to do with the combat disparity<br /> <br /> You can achieve the exact same thing that you're advocating for by making all the weapons have the same accuracy and damage stats. BUT WHY WOULD YOU WANT TO?<br /> <br /> To paraphrase you: If your only argument is that D&amp;D did it then you don't have a good argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>My argument is that attempting to make them distinct makes one kinda crappy and the other amazing. Instead, make it purely a matter of aesthetics. I don't <i>want</i> a bunch of distinct mechanical options in attributes, because it leads to exactly this: Godstats and sucker's bets. <br /> <br /> And if you don't want people drawing false conclusions from your words, I'd suggest not assuming the people you're speaking to are idiots who failed to see an obvious solution like &quot;Exalted isn't D&amp;D&quot;. No shooting it's not D&amp;D, and in this case, this is a problem, because it leads to godstats and making some things objectively mechanically inferior.<br /> <br /> And, bluntly, yes, if the weapon statlines were as much of a problem as the dex/strength issue, I would want all weapons to be mechanically identical, only differing in fluff. Bluntly, as it stands light weapons are ridiculously better than heavy, it's just not enough to make it an actual problem, <i>yet. </i>But if you do the logical thing and take a high strength, high stamina, middling dex heavy weapon person, you get screwed.<br /> <br /> Fuck. That. Make Dex and Strength interchangeable, and let people play with the aesthetics they want without baking &quot;the tiny rapid fragile person with a knife is the inherently superior fighter to the hulking samurai in heavy armor with the tetsubo.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T11:22:55-07:00","id":1239377,"title":"","content":"I miss so much fun stuff at work.<br /> <br /> Getting home to address this will be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T11:27:21-07:00","id":1239378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239370#post1239370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is that even suppost to say?</div> </div> </div> </div>My use a numerical comparison doesn't meant that you tossing around numbers to show that you can proves anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That you don't like my comparisons so they are not valid, but you like yours so they are? </div> </div> </div>Your statements weren't a comparison and had no point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No reasoning or explanation offered, what is the point of even responding? </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you skip all the reasoning and explanation when I went into things...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All semantics and opinions with no real engament of the issue and no objective point stated. </div> </div> </div>The whole thread is ultimately about semantics (that is, how to define the words we're using the describe the game), so dismissing my arguments as semantics is a refusal to engage with the subject at hand on your part, not mine.<br /> <br /> And there is no purely objective issue to address on this tangent; and I'd argue no purely objective issue has even been raised yet regarding the core point of the thread, but that's not on you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't even know why you quote while ranting about Exalted's system being broken, or saying accuracy is derived from raw power, when I said none of those things. </div> </div> </div>Um...I have no idea what you're talking about with the whole &quot;Exalted's system being broken,&quot; part. And you actually did say that you were arguing for accuracy derived from raw power:<br /> <br /> &quot;We are simply making the argument that a hit could also connect due to raw power. &quot;<br /> <br /> Those are your words. Accuracy, &quot;hit could connect,&quot; derived from raw power, &quot;due to raw power.&quot; That's why I quoted you posting those words.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, maybe you should pay a bit more attention to what's being said when you're claiming you didn't say something I quoted you saying earlier today?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239372#post1239372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument is that attempting to make them distinct makes one kinda crappy and the other amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're actually both kinda crappy in combat, one's just easier to mitigate (both can be though).<br /> <br /> And, of course, &quot;kinda crappy&quot; as you're using it assumes the combat is the only thing that matters to the game. I can easily make a Strength 5/Dexterity 1 character that's very good at what they do, even if it's not combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead, make it purely a matter of aesthetics. I don't <i>want</i> a bunch of distinct mechanical options in attributes, because it leads to exactly this: Godstats and sucker's bets. </div> </div> </div>Then why even have them? Even in ST system variations with far less mechanical distinctions between the Attributes, the games put in at least enough to justify having nine of them. If there's no difference between two traits besides flavor when describing them, there's no point in having both of them. And that means we're getting way outside of a simple &quot;fix&quot; to the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...I'd suggest not assuming the people you're speaking to are idiots... </div> </div> </div>Nobody's called you an idiot. You're being plenty combative in your wordings, so either chill or accept some push back. Constantly accusing people of insulting you when they haven't doesn't actually do you any good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bluntly, as it stands light weapons are ridiculously better than heavy, it's just not enough to make it an actual problem, </div> </div> </div>No, medium weapons are ridiculously better than heavy. People have done the math on this repeatedly. Heavy weapons are never worth it compared to medium weapons.<br /> <br /> This is actually a significant problem. Your 5/3/5 build with a main hand light and off hand medium will make a Dex 5 heavy weapon user look bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Make Dex and Strength interchangeable, and let people play with the aesthetics they want without baking &quot;the tiny rapid fragile person with a knife is the inherently superior fighter to the hulking samurai in heavy armor with the tetsubo.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I feel like I'm getting ignored since I addressed why this doesn't actually work for what's intended.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the best fighter? 5/5/5 in physicals, and Wits 5 too. My hulking samurai with high Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina squishes your pure Dex build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T11:37:36-07:00","id":1239380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239372#post1239372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument is that attempting to make them distinct makes one kinda crappy and the other amazing. Instead, make it purely a matter of aesthetics. I don't <i>want</i> a bunch of distinct mechanical options in attributes, because it leads to exactly this: Godstats and sucker's bets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, why have attributes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> let people play with the aesthetics they want without baking &quot;the tiny rapid fragile person with a knife is the inherently superior fighter to the hulking samurai in heavy armor with the tetsubo.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I do want Str and Dex builds to have different disadvantages and advantages. I do want them to feel different. <br /> I also agree that Dex builds are generally better than Strength builds*, but I don't feel that an issue of game-balance needs to be eradicated by effectively eradicating stats. <br /> What I mean is, I'm okay with your concept that Strength should be buffed, and using it for attack rolls is a buff (though not the one I'd choose). I mean, I just don't agree with the principles behind your argument.<br /> <br /> *For Solars. I suspect not for Lunars, and not just because of Steel Paw or whatever. But we'll see.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On a separate note, could everyone try and present their points with a bit less hostility? Several (not just on one side) posters are getting rather negative and attack-y. I don't see the value in accusing other posters of being idiots/liars/etc just because they have a different opinion. Perhaps some are hostile in response to others, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T11:43:26-07:00","id":1239382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239351#post1239351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... no.<br /> <br /> The problem here is basing the value of a character solely on combat pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to combat characters. If the Dawn swordsman has Dex 5, Melee 5, and the Twilight doctor has Dex 3, Melee 3, that's fine. The issue is when you get, say, a guy playing an archer who's bad at optimisation and so his archer routinely does rubbish and gets beaten up, while someone else is playing a teacher who happens to be much better at combat, because he's better at optimisation.<br /> That was my point about character gen; if there's not such an optimised way to make characters, it doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> (This is one of the reasons I kind of want to run a Lunar game; I suspect that Lunar character gen will not vary so much in how well the PCs optimise as Solar character gen does)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or just make heavy weapons less sucky. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this probably is the easiest and simplest change. Because medium and small weapons are reasonably balanced against each other, but heavy weapons are definitely weaker (and, oddly, the best way to counteract this weakness is with a character who's really good at dodging. Which isn't something I associate with the genre-tropes of heavy weapon wielders).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T11:43:31-07:00","id":1239384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239365#post1239365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your Dex is already figured into your raw damage calculation by virtue of it being part of the attack roll and the threshold successes of that attack roll os added to raw damage.<br /> <br /> Do I really need to explain that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reductive and juvenile.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T11:56:08-07:00","id":1239389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239384#post1239384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reductive and juvenile.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you consider your own answer to my observation those things too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:04:23-07:00","id":1239392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239372#post1239372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument is that attempting to make them distinct makes one kinda crappy and the other amazing. Instead, make it purely a matter of aesthetics. I don't <i>want</i> a bunch of distinct mechanical options in attributes, because it leads to exactly this: Godstats and sucker's bets.</div> </div> </div> </div>And finally we're getting somewhere. <br /> <br /> Except that it's not Dex is the god stat, it's ACCURACY is the god stat. Dex feeds into that problem but being able to replace it with strength isn't a great answer. At least not as a system fix. Consider lunars. Their dice cap is [Attribute] unless you can stunt in another attribute. So like, describing their attack as using their awesome thews to crush an opponent into dust allows them to boost the roll by DEX+STR. It doesn't make as much thematic sense for a Solar to be able to 'use their mighty thews' to strike because the solar is all about their melee score, <i>not</i> their attributes. Same with DB. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239372#post1239372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you don't want people drawing false conclusions from your words, I'd suggest not assuming the people you're speaking to are idiots who failed to see an obvious solution like &quot;Exalted isn't D&amp;D&quot;. No shooting it's not D&amp;D, and in this case, this is a problem, because it leads to godstats and making some things objectively mechanically inferior.</div> </div> </div> </div>a) You started in on the personal attacks questioning intelligence, not me. I made no allusions to <i>anyone's </i>Intelligence at all. I used pointing out the obvious as a rhetorical tool to show how using D&amp;D as the reference for anything in Exalted is a weak argument to start because it's comparing apples to hand grenades. <br /> b)D&amp;D still has god stats. They went a long way to reducing that in 5th edition, but they really, absolutely, completely still have god stats. But even if it didn't you're still taking that one aspect of how D&amp;D approaches things and holding it up as an example of how awesome that is without in any way showing how it would actually work with the rest of Exalted play. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239372#post1239372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, bluntly, yes, if the weapon statlines were as much of a problem as the dex/strength issue, I would want all weapons to be mechanically identical, only differing in fluff. <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, Pump the brakes.<br /> <br /> You'd like to see a Grand Goremaul have the same stats as a rapier? <br /> <br /> Because, the difference in accuracy of light vs heavy is 4. The difference in damage is ALSO 4, but the other direction. This is literally the same as having STR 1 DEX 5 or STR 5 DEX 1.<br /> <br /> In fact, (ignoring the fact that heavy melee weapons require str 3) a DEX 5 STR 1 character wielding a Tetsubo is the exact same accuracy and damage as a STR 5, DEX 1 character wielding a club! If you're playing a DB, their excellency cap is the same either way!<br /> <br /> If you're comparing a 5/3 setup then the weapon choice is <i>by far</i> the worse problem but you seem to be completely rejecting that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239372#post1239372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bluntly, as it stands light weapons are ridiculously better than heavy, it's just not enough to make it an actual problem, <i>yet. </i>But if you do the logical thing and take a high strength, high stamina, middling dex heavy weapon person, you get screwed.<br /> <br /> Fuck. That. Make Dex and Strength interchangeable, and let people play with the aesthetics they want without baking &quot;the tiny rapid fragile person with a knife is the inherently superior fighter to the hulking samurai in heavy armor with the tetsubo.&quot;<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that this doesn't help! Being able to swap out 'middling Dex' for 'high strength' gets you 2 dice! TWO! If you're on average only missing by 1 success with a low accuracy character then I'd say the system is working perfectly fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:07:09-07:00","id":1239394,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> <br /> Why do you keep dodging the points and making long winded arguments about things that were never said? It is like you're quoting me to argue with a ghost and with yourself.<br /> <br /> I never said the system is broken, you were the one that quoted me to argue it wasn't. For what?<br /> <br /> Connecting a hit doesn't have to related to more accuracy. I can forgo trying to hit you on the nose to just throw a punch anywhere, that will connect and hurt due to my raw power.<br /> <br /> Rolling an attack with Dex can be described as circumventing defense and going for weak spots.<br /> <br /> Rolling with Str can be described as hurling the blow with as much power as possible, not caring where it lands.<br /> <br /> The system is abstract enough for it to don't matter for any kind of verissimilitude to break.<br /> <br /> \u200bTry paying more attention to what people that disagree with you are saying before replying, instead of trying to &quot;win&quot; or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:10:35-07:00","id":1239396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239394#post1239394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rolling with Str can be described as hurling the blow with as much power as possible, not caring where it lands.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that it's much like the clip posted a couple pages back and it only makes sense to hit if your opponent is standing still, letting it. Actual opponents who don't want to die will get out of the way of your wild, highly-telegraphed swings.<br /> <br /> So basically, exactly as the system currently works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:14:42-07:00","id":1239398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239396#post1239396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this is that it's much like the clip posted a couple pages back and it only makes sense to hit if your opponent is standing still, letting it. Actual opponents who don't want to die will get out of the way of your wild, highly-telegraphed swings.<br /> <br /> So basically, exactly as the system currently works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> What the opponent does in reaction to your move is mechanically defined as their Defense. It has noithing to do with your attack pool.<br /> <br /> Cannibal Wolf Boy is a Dodge monster, that's why he avoids getting hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 07-27-2018, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:18:24-07:00","id":1239400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239398#post1239398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really.<br /> <br /> What the opponent does in reaction to your move is mechanically defined as your Defense. It has noithing to do with your attack pool.<br /> <br /> Cannibal Wolf Boy is a Dodge monster, that's why he avoids getting hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, when someone is swinging wildly, and 'not caring where the blow lands&quot; then it's much easier to dodge those blows. IE Someone with less dodge can also get out of the way of them. IE <i>exactly as the system already stands</i><br /> <br /> If you want to describe how you can make an accurate strike using brute force, you're also going to have to explain how it's not easier to dodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:36:51-07:00","id":1239404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239400#post1239400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, when someone is swinging wildly, and 'not caring where the blow lands&quot; then it's much easier to dodge those blows. IE Someone with less dodge can also get out of the way of them. IE <i>exactly as the system already stands</i><br /> <br /> If you want to describe how you can make an accurate strike using brute force, you're also going to have to explain how it's not easier to dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are the one talking about swinging wildly, I didn't.<br /> <br /> I already described how I would justify rolling with Dex and Str.<br /> <br /> A roll with Dex is looking for a specific spot to hit, striving to hit a reduced vulnerable target.<br /> <br /> A roll with Str eschews a specific spot and makes the whole of the enemy the target, and it will hurt anyways because of the power behind the strike.<br /> <br /> It is not easier to dodge for the same reason that is easier to keep someone that wants to hit your face from hitting you than it is keeping a guy that just wants to hurt you from hitting you anywhere. It all just balances out on the abstractions, it is a too fine grained matter for it to have system relevance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:48:54-07:00","id":1239411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239389#post1239389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do you consider your own answer to my observation those things too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah so you really didn't understand and just wanted to throw the offer to explain things back in my face. Classy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T13:04:07-07:00","id":1239415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239411#post1239411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah so you really didn't understand and just wanted to throw the offer to explain things back in my face. Classy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No Lioness, your first statement in this chain was about how you don't expect to be taken seriously if you wanted to add Dex to your raw damage, making a parallel that people that argue for Str based attack pools shouldn't be taken seriously. I responded in a lighthy annoyed way, because I dislike the dismissiveness that is so usual around disagreement here.<br /> <br /> Then I pointed out to you that your Dex already is part of your raw damage. The more Dex you have, the more damage you will do, not only by dint of being able to hit more often, but also that whatever overage you get gets directly added to the damage of the attack.<br /> <br /> The fact is that what you tried to propose as an argument as to how to dismiss what is being discussed is already a part of the system.<br /> <br /> So I wanted to prod you into questioning yourself if you were going to dismiss the system, or were you going to back down and approach the discussion with other arguments?<br /> <br /> Then you chose to ignore the core point I brought up, nitpick that Dex is not added directly to the damage roll and finish up by implying that I was incapable of understanding something simple and that you needed to hold my hand and walk me through it.<br /> <br /> Finally, I just did the same to you, to see if you can look how you are acting yourself and stop this.<br /> <br /> How about we not be dismissive of the discussion and argue actual points that are being made?<br /> <br /> I'm all for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T13:15:28-07:00","id":1239419,"title":"","content":"I think that Lunars getting to use Strength instead of Dexterity for attacks via a charm is really cool. Charms-tech is supposed to hang off the system as it is currently written, and these new charms are doing exactly that in a way that make Lunars distinct from Solars and comparable enough in power that mixed games do not feel like an imbalanced farce. Which is the core of what the Exalted community asked of the Development/Writing team. So I see no reason to change that aspect to a universal system rule. Lunars should be allowed to have their things, can we please let Lunars have their things? Solars have Supernal, Dragonbloods have Hearths and Signature Charms. Let Lunars have Attribute Swapping and Shapeshifting!<br /> <br /> It is unfortunate that the system as written as resulted in a poor play experiences at tables other mine. That, I understand, can be frustrating.<br /> <br /> Back in the 2ed days there was a lot of :<br /> <br /> &quot;well my table isn't having problems&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well my table does and just because you don't see a problem doesn't mean the problem doesn't exist!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well you and your players are playing the game wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;How dare you say I am playing the game wrong?!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You wouldn't have problems if you were playing correctly&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;[insert pendantic rage filled argument]&quot;<br /> <br /> That is what this thread is very quickly devolved into. :/ People are even picking fights with Moderators. WTF?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T13:19:02-07:00","id":1239421,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1998_4.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1998\" data-vbnamecard=\"1998\">Keichiokami</a><br /> <br /> Solars can already swap the attribute of an attack dice pool... It is not an exclusive Lunar thing...<br /> <br /> And who is picking a fight with a Moderator? Or &quot;picking a fight&quot; at all?<br /> <br /> Lioness, when not speaking in red, is just another member of the community, like any one of us. And I believe she likes it that way, we shouldn't be stepping in eggshells when talking to her because of some special status.<br /> <br /> Calm down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 07-27-2018, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T13:46:52-07:00","id":1239429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239382#post1239382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to combat characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sorta. There's a lot of combat besides the Dawn attack Abilities. &quot;Bob&quot; that invests in Survival and goes Beast Master to toss a super-familiar at foes instead of themselves, or the Ride with a boost mount, or the Sorcery summoner, or the Sorcery artillery blaster, etc. All of these allow combat characters that don't get short changed despite not maxing out Dex + (insert Dawn attack Ability).<br /> <br /> Of course, on of those things that gets ignored a bit are things like the Ride specialist being one of the few situations where high Strength and low Dex can be pretty effective. Your mount's Speed bonus overcomes lower Dex's mobility issues - and you can not worry about heavy armor causing problems there - and you can use a lance one handed when mounted, allowing an off handed shield for the medium weapon parry, plus anything without the Reaching Tag means you get bonus accuracy and defense as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That was my point about character gen; if there's not such an optimised way to make characters, it doesn't really matter. </div> </div> </div>Unless you seriously restrict char-gen, I'm not sure how you accomplish this, especially while letting people take advantage of Supernals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (This is one of the reasons I kind of want to run a Lunar game; I suspect that Lunar character gen will not vary so much in how well the PCs optimise as Solar character gen does) </div> </div> </div>Or, at least from the previews I've seen, it just matters less because they have simple access to Charms that let them shift things around more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239394#post1239394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you keep dodging the points and making long winded arguments about things that were never said?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) What point did I dodge?<br /> <br /> 2) I directly demonstrated arguing against something you said... with quotes of you saying it. So... that's not really a compelling statement from you. If you're going to say I'm saying you're saying things you didn't say... you might want to actually show it instead of telling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never said the system is broken, you were the one that quoted me to argue it wasn't. For what? </div> </div> </div>You're arguing for a change to the system, I'm arguing against it... doesn't seem that complicated. For someone that was just complaining about semantics, it seems pretty weak to dismiss this because of the word &quot;broken&quot; being used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Connecting a hit doesn't have to related to more accuracy. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it does. The more likely you are to connect with a hit, the more accurate you are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can forgo trying to hit you on the nose to just throw a punch anywhere, that will connect and hurt due to my raw power. </div> </div> </div>Probably not. In fact, going back a bit? This approach is exactly how Foreman lost to Ali in the Rumble in the Jungle. Ali was careful to protect specific spots, while letting the extremely powerful Foreman hit him plenty in places that were good at absorbing the blows, this tired Foreman out, and let Ali get shots in that were more effective. This was the Rope-a-Dope. Let the powerful hitter waste all his energy throwing punches that connect but aren't effective, while you focus on single effective hits against the tired opponent's weakened defense.<br /> <br /> Accuracy matters. You can't just slam wildly and expect to hurt someone unless you're superhumanly strong. I've seen a man break three of his own fingers thinking he was being smart by sucker punching another man in the head, only to end up hitting one of the toughest spots on the skull and his hand bones lost. His raw power worked against him, because when his bones broke, all that power went into his own body instead of his opponent's. A mere three inches difference, and he probably would have shattered his target's orbital bone and potentially caused permanent damage to that eye.<br /> <br /> When a few inches can mean shattering your hand, or crushing your opponents eye... raw power just isn't enough.<br /> <br /> Again, if you want to say that Strength should include accuracy as well as raw power, that's different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The system is abstract enough for it to don't matter for any kind of verissimilitude to break. </div> </div> </div>Except, as noted, not caring where your blow hits makes it easier to defend against you, so it doesn't make sense that it would make you better at landing effective hits.<br /> <br /> There are ways you can have it make more sense - like Strength based attacks don't apply threshold successes to raw damage, which removes the doubling a bit as well as reflecting the wild blow landing whereever thing - but just allowing people to pick doesn't to it alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239398#post1239398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the opponent does in reaction to your move is mechanically defined as their Defense. It has noithing to do with your attack pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, speaking of paying attention to what people are saying? The point is, it doesn't make sense for two attackers to have equal pools against the same Defense, if one attack is descriptively easier to avoid than the other. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239404#post1239404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are the one talking about swinging wildly, I didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>You: &quot;...hurling the blow with as much power as possible, not caring where it lands.&quot; That's swinging wildly. You're talking about it. This is getting old.<br /> <br /> It's different from:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A roll with Str eschews a specific spot and makes the whole of the enemy the target, and it will hurt anyways because of the power behind the strike. </div> </div> </div>In phrasing in small but significant ways. But this phrasing runs into the issue of most things not being so simple to hurt as this. Some parts are hard, some parts are squishy, so treating the whole body as a target doesn't quite make sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T14:09:20-07:00","id":1239432,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> <br /> On connecting a hit: No it doesn't, you can just choose to broaden your target.<br /> <br /> And while yes, in the real world, hitting specific spots is what matters, you don't get better at it because you can do backflips. Like I said earlier, it all balances out in the end, the system doesn't make it harder if you want to hit someone in the nose or in the body, when in the real world it matters.<br /> <br /> If the hit connects on Str based attack pool, it could just be described as it having hit with such force that it hurt anyways. That is the point.<br /> <br /> On Str threshold successes: I was going to suggest the excat same thing in my post answering to Lioness, but I decided to hold back until someone showed they wanted to talk about the idea, instead of just dismissing it. And now that you are talking about it, yeah, I had the same exact thought and think it is pretty reasonable.<br /> <br /> On Defense and attack descriptions: I don't consider the a Str based attack descriptively easier to dodge, as further expanded on statement on a later post<br /> <br /> &quot;It is not easier to dodge for the same reason that is easier to keep someone that wants to hit your face from hitting you than it is keeping a guy that just wants to hurt you from hitting you anywhere. It all just balances out on the abstractions, it is a too fine grained matter for it to have system relevance.&quot;<br /> <br /> On wildly swinging: Wildly swinging for is swinging in a crazy way. What I described is swinging in a skilled, controlled way to produce the most power possible, you just care if you're hitting the chin or the chest. The description of where it lands and how much it hurts could be left to be based on the result of the damage roll. Which is how we do it at tables I play laready, not only for this game, but for any other that has rolled damage.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T14:59:22-07:00","id":1239443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239432#post1239432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On connecting a hit: No it doesn't, you can just choose to broaden your target.<br /> <br /> And while yes, in the real world, hitting specific spots is what matters, you don't get better at it because you can do backflips. Like I said earlier, it all balances out in the end, the system doesn't make it harder if you want to hit someone in the nose or in the body, when in the real world it matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>and an opponent can just redirect your wild swing more easily. Or get out of the way of it. It's easy to say &quot;broaden your target&quot; but that doesn't make your sword bigger. It just increases the randomness of your attack. If you're swinging to hit &quot;somewhere in this area&quot; then you're <i>not</i> in control of your weapon. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239432#post1239432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the hit connects on Str based attack pool, it could just be described as it having hit with such force that it hurt anyways. That is the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>But once again, you're completely ignoring the opponent in this fight. If you're letting him choose where that hit lands because he's faster than you then he can either take the hit better, redirect it better or get out of its way better.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239432#post1239432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Str threshold successes: I was going to suggest the excat same thing in my post answering to Lioness, but I decided to hold back until someone showed they wanted to talk about the idea, instead of just dismissing it. And now that you are talking about it, yeah, I had the same exact thought and think it is pretty reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is fine. But this is essentially saying &quot;I use my strength to have better control over my weapon and am able to guide it faster to where it needs to go. <i>That's </i>accuracy with strength. <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239432#post1239432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Defense and attack descriptions: I don't consider the a Str based attack descriptively easier to dodge, as further expanded on statement on a later post<br /> <br /> &quot;It is not easier to dodge for the same reason that is easier to keep someone that wants to hit your face from hitting you than it is keeping a guy that just wants to hurt you from hitting you anywhere. It all just balances out on the abstractions, it is a too fine grained matter for it to have system relevance.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the problem is that every single time you've described an attack it's in such a way that it would be inherently easier to dodge/parry. <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239432#post1239432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On wildly swinging: Wildly swinging for is swinging in a crazy way. What I described is swinging in a skilled, controlled way to produce the most power possible, you just care if you're hitting the chin or the chest. The description of where it lands and how much it hurts could be left to be based on the result of the damage roll. Which is how we do it at tables I play laready, not only for this game, but for any other that has rolled damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>What swinging wildly is not: Windmilling your arms until something connects or trying to keep an enemy away when he's just blinded you. That's just flailing.<br /> What swinging wildly is: Attacking someone with all your strength with no real intent to aim or do anything more than &quot;hit that guy&quot; <br /> <br /> This is not to be confused with &quot;shooting wildly&quot; which is a completely different thing.<br /> <br /> What you have described thus far has been swinging wildly. <br /> <br /> &quot;swinging in a skilled, controlled way to produce as much power as possible&quot; is literally what every single combatant is trying to do in every combat. This is not meaningfully describing strength vs dexterity in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T15:19:37-07:00","id":1239450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239415#post1239415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, I just did the same to you, to see if you can look how you are acting yourself and stop this.<br /> <br /> How about we not be dismissive of the discussion and argue actual points that are being made?<br /> <br /> I'm all for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because repeatedly posting in bad faith makes me inclined to engage with the discussion? <b>What? </b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:06:24-07:00","id":1239479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239432#post1239432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On connecting a hit: No it doesn't, you can just choose to broaden your target.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can't. The target is what the target is. You can choose to broaden the area you're going to focus on, but the decreases the odds of hitting if you get too broad.<br /> <br /> If I broaden the area I'm aiming for to &quot;anywhere within 1 yard of my foe,&quot; I can easily punch something in that space, but I'm drastically decreasing my odds of punching something that counts.<br /> <br /> Again, this is why the Rope-a-Dope worked. Just attacking &quot;anywhere on the body,&quot; makes it extremely easy to make sure your opponent puts something non-vital (or better very tough) in the way (aka parry). Ali effectively blocked a huge number of Foreman's punches (since they hit where Ali wanted them to hit, not where Foreman wanted to hit).<br /> <br /> If I have a shield, and you're swinging an axe at me with force but not accuracy, that axe is going to hit my shield, not me, because that's one of the reasons I have a shield in the first place. However broad you want to consider the target, the shield is going to occupy the vast majority of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And while yes, in the real world, hitting specific spots is what matters, you don't get better at it because you can do backflips. </div> </div> </div>Right, you buy Brawl, not Athletics.<br /> <br /> And, of course, you don't get better at hitting with a punch because you can crush a metal goblet with your hand. Attributes are broad. We've covered this. Every Attribute covers more than one thing. Bringing up things Dexterity does that don't directly impact landing attacks doesn't matter, because I can bring up things Strength does that don't directly impact landing attacks either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the hit connects on Str based attack pool, it could just be described as it having hit with such force that it hurt anyways. That is the point. </div> </div> </div>And it's a bad point, because that description will frequently not make sense (also just hitting doesn't mean you did any damage and all that, just that you get to see if you do). This gets worse in Exalted where you're going to end up fighting non-human opponents where your &quot;as long as I hit, it must be a spot that hurts&quot; thing gets more tortured in narration without overlapping with how you're saying Dexterity should be envisioned..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On Str threshold successes: I was going to suggest the excat same thing in my post answering to Lioness, but I decided to hold back until someone showed they wanted to talk about the idea, instead of just dismissing it. And now that you are talking about it, yeah, I had the same exact thought and think it is pretty reasonable. </div> </div> </div>So, here's the thing with it. I actually did this for a while in Revised WoD... and I stopped including it as a house rule because far too few playable character types could field enough Strength to make it enticing. Some players made characters that used it to start, but over time, as characters approach Strength 5/Dexterity 5 (and actually as long as they're equal) Dexterity is what combat focused characters used. It works for a little bit, letting Strength focused characters not feel as pressured to jump to high Dexterity ASAP, but as time passes, the appeal of threshold successes from attacking with Dexterity is too irresistible (esp. when you can't buy any more Strength anyway).<br /> <br /> Ultimately, you become a Dexterity based fighter, or you let your fighting skills stagnate, even with that house rule. It's not a bad thing for starting level play to help players not fall into optimization traps, but it doesn't actually make Strength and Dexterity on par over time.<br /> <br /> Also, it's worth noting that we're demonstrating how &quot;just let players pick Strength or Dexterity&quot; isn't a good rule by itself in the context of Exalted 3e as it is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 07-27-2018, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:12:25-07:00","id":1239482,"title":"","content":"I'm about to reply to another post but people let's please be civil here. At the end of the day we're talking about a pen and paper board game. There are better things to get angry over. Regardless of who you are in this debate if you find yourself becoming hot and typing nasty things, take a step away from the keyboard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239224#post1239224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn. I am getting some serious flashbacks to 2008 right now. O.O</div> </div> </div> </div>You and me both.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:35:25-07:00","id":1239491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239450#post1239450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because repeatedly posting in bad faith makes me inclined to engage with the discussion? <b>What? </b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so tired of this bad faith bullshit. <br /> <br /> Do you not have disagreements with your friends? Do you assume that someone that doesn't agree with you is automatically some evil asshole or something?<br /> <br /> You were the one that entered this discussion asking for people to not take others seriously.<br /> <br /> You came in with the patronizing attitude.<br /> <br /> And I am the one acting in bad faith here?<br /> <br /> I am not arguing in bad faith, I just happen to think differently than you. And I got a newsflash for you, it doesn't automatically make wrong or bad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:43:54-07:00","id":1239498,"title":"","content":"And all of you talking about how nonsensical a Str based attack pool is, you're just saying all the people that worked to create nWoD and now CofD lack any sense, because that system was proposed as the next step in Storyteller and it uses Str for close combat attack pools.<br /> <br /> I'm also going to bow out of this discussion, it soured for me with all this nonsensical crap being thrown around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T18:57:43-07:00","id":1239524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239491#post1239491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You were the one that entered this discussion asking for people to not take others seriously.<br /> <br /> You came in with the patronizing attitude.<br /> <br /> And I am the one acting in bad faith here?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you put it like that it does look like you were angry at me from the word go and had no interest in actual discussion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T19:11:58-07:00","id":1239529,"title":"","content":"So I was originally going to reply to Heavy Arms in one post before going to work, but it was longer than I thought. Since I was 2/3rds typing this I\u2019ll finish this before moving onto the mass response method. If you addressed these points later Heavy Arms I\u2019ll get to them later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the middleman can still be cool and/or valuable enough to warrant a cost of its own.<br /> <br /> By your logic, why shouldn't a Charm like Excellent Strike not just be part of a Solar's free Excellency, so they can get to Fire and Stone Strike, and One Weapon, Two Blows, without a middleman? Your logic isn't based on whether or not the effect is useful, just that it isn't 'special' enough. So why is Excellent Strike not something that's just default free for Solar Melee?<br /> <br /> Being able to parry with Stamina is already a &quot;cool thing&quot; you're buying a Charm to do. More Charms building off that, that do even more cool things, is how all Charms work: tress that build on a theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent Strike has a purpose being a charm even if its boring. Adding a success? Yea sure whatever. But the more important thing is rerolling 1s. You know how many Solar charms rely on 1s being rolled to trigger some sort of nasty effect? Excellent Strike bypasses those. Secondly it doesn't meet the requirements of being a feat tax: you take it or you're an idiot because your concept/build demands it to be essentially. You could ignore Excellent Strike completely or buy it and forget about it, it helps but won't be horribly damaging to your build otherwise.<br /> <br /> Attribute swappers do not do this. They are required for a character to have a dice pool worth a shit to use in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what? I remember people saying lots of stuff about 2e. Sometimes the people arguing that something with it wasn't broken were right.</div> </div> </div> </div>People were screaming at each other for more than a decade that 2e had problems with Paranoia combat. Again this isn't like paranoia combat or 3e Sail/Craft, but if we can make a fix that's relatively simple why not do it now and be done with it?<br /> <br /> Holden was one of those people who advocated that 2.0e had an essential problem in paranoia combat. There were (and still are!) groups of people who say it doesn't exist if you 'play the game right'. If a man says he's an owl then in that man's view he's an owl, but it doesn't stop everyone around him from thinking there's something fundamentally wrong.<br /> <br /> Want to know something really fun? Jon Chung pointed out ages ago that Solar Hero Style (and the rest of the 2e MA's) were largely shit on Solars because of the power difference. He made a Solar Hero Style revision that addressed these problems with the &quot;Hero&quot; keyword. This was officially done in 2.5e. This is the precursor to Mastery and Resonant effects.<br /> <br /> And he's a single person who claimed there was a problem DESPITE people saying that there was no problems with MA's because you take it for a flavor standpoint.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you're doing a piss poor job of advocating for it, because you're still just gong, &quot;this is dumb because I say so, and despite being said I need to actually justify this, I don't because... feat tax!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'll keep going. Until someone can provide me with some solid argument on why they're not counted as a feat tax and some new bastion of good charm design, I won't be convinced.<br /> <br /> Moral: Don't fix system problems with charms. Fix them with actual changes to the system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the same goes the other way. Just because you have a problem with it, doesn't mean others will. Your personal preferences are not adequate proof of a fundamental flaw in the system that needs to be fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully I have other people who posted in this topic who echo my own personal preferences to back me up on this.<br /> <br /> Secondly look at the owl example. You can be blind to a problem and never notice it, it doesn't mean others won't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who cares? Homebrew isn't official material that matters to how the books do things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honey all the people doing 3e are homebrewers. Every. Single. One. Homebrew is exactly how official books are made, its just given an official stamp by a company because the company have taken people who are capable of producing quality material.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't make any sense. I(A)M isn't a feat tax, it's a bad Charm that broke the mote economy... it's only effect was to reduce the mote cost of other Charms. &quot;Feat tax&quot; as you're using it, is a meaningless phrase that amounts to being, &quot;I don't like it but I don't want to have to actually explain why in a fully thought out fashion!&quot;<br /> <br /> And I directly addressed I(A)M in detail, which you're skipping, which only reaffirms you don't have a reason beyond wanting the devs to make your preferences the official rules instead of actually caring about improving the game for as many people as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IAM is exactly a feat tax. Have you seen the dice pools of other late game enemies? You\u2019ll be slaughtered without it. The fact that it broke mote economy and separated literally everyone into two tiers (Whose who have IAM and those who do not) amounts to being a feat tax.<br /> <br /> Secondly I did address what a feat tax is, multiple times. Something that\u2019s required to be taken in order to be remotely comparable to anyone else. If there was one Solar Melee charm that was so good that other builds in the game could be warped around, \u201cThose who have that charm and those who do not\u201d that is a feat tax.<br /> <br /> Lastly please do not put words into my mouth like that. I only want to bring the game to as best of a state as possible that is enjoyable to as many people as possible while still remaining true to the core of the game. If I see something like, then I shall echo it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is fundamentally just a matter of perspective. If my concept includes &quot;wrestling giant monsters,&quot; there's a specific Brawl Charm my Solar needs to buy. Does that make it no longer a fun Charm because I designed a character specifically around doing that awesome thing?<br /> <br /> Yes, not every Charm is equally, &quot;get this or you're stupid,&quot; but the majority of Charms relevant to whatever your concept is, are ones you want to buy. So this doesn't work as a clarification; how many Essence 1 Solar Charms aren't &quot;get this or you are stupid&quot; if you want to be good at that Ability? How many of them are bread and butter Charms that are more about functioning at higher level, than they are flashy effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to wrestle giant monsters? There are charms specifically to make you do that because not many people in the setting or other games can do the same. You want to make charms to wrestle well? There are charms that do that and are honestly much better than any other systems out there for using grappling.<br /> <br /> But do you know what do you know what there are often not charms of?<br /> <br /> Charms that make your character remotely feasible. In 2.Xe this was IMA and excellencies. If you did not have it then you were effectively a non-entity beyond a certain point in the game unless you were doing something like mortal only, serious kiddie gloves, or serious homebrew. If there is something wrong with this, then something is fucked and things need to change.<br /> <br /> You know the last things that had such an outcry? 3e Craft (Which Vance said revamped rules are incoming), 2.0e paranoia combat and 2e Martial arts. The developers tried to repair the system using band-aid effects in 2.5e *but you cannot solve a root problem with charms*. It needs to be fixed at the root.<br /> <br /> In fact let me ask you this. In DnD 4e despite its careful mathematics Weapon Focus feats (Feats that gave +X to hit and another that gave +X to damage) where baked into the math of the game. Attempting to play a character later on without those has a handicap compared to others that do, starting small and eventually being significant. Should players be charged/forced to take these concepts not to fall behind in the game due to an oversight or mistake on the developers part? Or do you disagree with the idea that people given them out for free because most players want to do cooler things like do an 10 square burst area aggro that rains divine wrath on enemies who dare attack your allies?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You saw me say &quot;Celestial&quot; there, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was leading into the next point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You still need to buy them, which you're saying is bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am against pointless purchases, not for excellencies as a whole. If DB Excellencies only added dice? Yea I\u2019d complain against that and say they need it for free. But when compared to something like the Brawl Excellencies or Melee excellencies? With effects good enough that they\u2019re not \u2018lol DB\u2019s\u2019 but good enough to the point other splats want them? That is worth is a purchase. That makes you feel like you\u2019re going to be doing something with them.<br /> <br /> For Solars and Lunars? Which excellencies will be just buying dice? Yes, those are crap. They\u2019re functional but boring and dull. The same way letting you have the \u2018honor\u2019 of letting you use Strength for attack pools. The only reason I don\u2019t go after the Solar grappling charm is because it does have other effects on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Above contains no objective flaw demonstrated in the system. Repeatedly saying it's there when you haven't actually demonstrated it's there doesn't mean it's there.</div> </div> </div> </div>See the owl example. People have had this problem other than me. Other than people in this thread. It exists whenever you want to believe it or not. I said the same thing to people who talked about Martial Arts having no problems and Paranoia combat no existing in 2.Xe despite these being very real things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't know what I &quot;think.&quot; And I didn't call it fragile, I simply said that the Charms being based on Attributes and Abilities necessitates a heavier hand on Attribute and Ability default assignments than a game where powers don't have default links to traits like that. This is actually less about it being fragile, and more about that big concern of yours: newbie traps. If you make Attribute assignment more flexible, you make it harder to avoid creating Charms that screw newbies that didn't invest in Attribute B because they thought they only had to worry about Attribute A to be effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>First that link isn\u2019t as tight as you think in 3e. It was in 2e massively, but not here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly it doesn't matter if I make something new called Zorgs to the system. Point is powers from nearly any RPG are rule exceptions. They let you do something contrary to the standard rules. Often these are neat things, other times they\u2019re powerful things, other times they\u2019re dumb because they\u2019re \u201cGet this or you\u2019re stupid\u201d powers.<br /> <br /> What you\u2019re saying about attribute assignment makes no sense. Right now a person is screwed if they get something like Strength 5 Dexterity 1 or 2. Opening up the attribute powers in this sense doesn\u2019t screw people because investing in Attribute B makes Attribute A more effect. In fact you don\u2019t need to make many changes to the current charmsets as a whole for this to be effective.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think your own ego is proof of your knowledge or whether or not you're correct on any specific issue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Crown\u2019s heavy, what can I say.<br /> <br /> Heavyarms my ego is jack shit. I only know one or two people who are harsher on my work than myself. The constant self-reflection at your own self works and the ability to go, \u201c\u2026They\u2019re good, but I can do better.\u201d<br /> <br /> The only way I can get better is learning and devouring anything and everything I can. About the setting, about the mechanics, and how everything works.<br /> <br /> I would not make such statements if I couldn\u2019t back them up. If there is someone who can point out otherwise I will concede, but right now I\u2019m not at that point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. I never asserted that the system isn't broken because you can fix it. I said that you having a preference that's different from the primary design of the game, and house ruling the game to fit the preference, isn't proof that the system is broken.<br /> <br /> You're just tossing out buzzwords to paper over you haven't demonstrated a break in the system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> See the owl example Heavy Arms. Just because you refuse to listen to something doesn\u2019t mean the problem isn\u2019t there. If I\u2019m paying money for a product, then I would like the best and well-polished product I can get without needing to fix things myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does this prove anything about your points? It just proves that combat is a lot more complicated than maxing out your to-hit dice-pool.<br /> <br /> Your assertion here also further demonstrates your poor argumentation as you ignore how Abilities factor into these things. Mobility is not just how much Dex you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know because for years in both 2e and even 3e usually the best way to gauge encounters is by dice pools. How high are the pools and defenses from enemy to enemy if you want to make the players mechanically sweat. Combat is more complicated than dice pools, but it\u2019s a damn good starting metric that\u2019s universal across nearly any character, mortal to exalt to cosmic exalted.<br /> <br /> In this system? Yes mobility is exactly how much dex an on foot character has. You can have a Strength 5, Dex 1 Athletics 5 character and a Strength 1, Dexterity 5 Athletics 5 character, the latter is going to be better exponentially better in nearly every area outside of feats of Strength. It doesn\u2019t matter if you have speed charms too because because on average that higher dex character will be faster *because many charms work better with higher base stat pools*.<br /> <br /> The Strength 5 character can use a mount. Great! He\u2019s probably just as fast or on par with the Dexterity Athletics use AND can hit harder! \u2026When he actually hits because his accuracy is still Dexterity, oof.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Facts not in evidence.<br /> <br /> Also, listing off your bone fides doesn't mean anything if you're not applying them in a useful fashion. Someone with 1% of the experience you're claiming would look at the push back in this thread and consider that it's more likely they failed to adequately communicate their base assertions than everyone else being wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>What evidence do you want? A paper dedicated to exploring the differences between using Dexterity or Strength for accuracy? Isn\u2019t the sour expression of other players who had a similar problem not enough for you? Other games not doing similar things not enough for you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239206#post1239206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, the good old, &quot;I'm right, so I'm allowed to be an ass, but everyone else has to treat me like the Queen or they get dismissed,&quot; bullcrap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respect is a two way street. If people are going to hide behind insults rather than contribute anything of merit, they can present their point or move on.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T19:19:47-07:00","id":1239530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239340#post1239340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't the ST in that game, actually. I was an <i>observer,</i> watching it fall apart despite the enemies being straight from the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I just used math to prove characters don't need a Dex of 5 to hit literally every single antagonist listed in the corebook. With the limited information I have on the game you observed, my assessment would be either the players had a simple run of bad luck with the dice, or didn't understand how to properly augment their rolls. The attack benefits provided by a Dex 5 over a Dex 3 character is 2 dice, roughly equating to 1 success. When you start accounting for stunts and charms, 1 success is a very small margin of difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239340#post1239340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, see, I'm not even talking about perfect optimization. I'm talking about <i>failing to take Dexterity at 5.</i> If I was talking about perfect optimization, I would be referring to how Solars can easily attack 3 times a turn, one of those casually being a Decisive Attack with 10+ initiative. Or how Solars can push their Evasion to 13+ and gain 5 initiative every time someone misses them. But I'm not talking about that. I'm talking about the sheer combat difference between a Medium Artifact Weapon+Dex 5, and Dex3+Heavy Weapon. The difference being a pathetic joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to ignore your comments on &quot;perfect-optimization&quot; because it isn't what we're discussing, as you yourself pointed out. The math is done, you can absolutely compete against every antagonist in the corebook with a Dex of 3. If Bob's wants to use a heavy weapon, he'll need to bolster his attack a bit more. There are numerous ways to do this without taking a Dex of 5. He could pick up dice trick charm or two, or take an appropriate specialization, invest more essence in his excellency during the attack, boost his Melee stat, etc. In your example of characters with: Dex 5 + medium artifact weapon (we'll call him Tim) vs Dex 3 + heavy weapon (lets stick with Bob), I hope you mean a heavy artifact weapon? Otherwise you're getting into question of Tim having spent more resources (ie. merits and XP) on combat capability then Bob did. In which case, Tim should absolutely have the advantage!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239340#post1239340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If taking Dex 3, Strength 5 means you have to balance every encounter to have a defense score that can ever be hit by the heavy weapon user, that means the non-heavy weapon user will rapidly end the fight, unless you boost their soak insanely, which leads to this cascading series of patches and I'd really rather just be able to use the higher of Strength or Dex to aim my attacks without having to explain this problem to every storyteller from now until the end of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you balancing? Unless the laws of probability and physics work differently at your table then mine, Bob with his Str 5, Dex 3, heavy weapon, can hit every opponent listed to date. If you like, we can hop on Discord and run through the scenario with several different opponents? We're not discussing subbing Str for Dex. I stated from the beginning that I was neutral on that debate. On one hand, I see reducing the reliance on Dex as a good thing, as well as making Str builds more viable. On the other, using Str for both attack and damage is literally doubling it's effectiveness, making it the new &quot;god stat&quot; for combat. Both sides have compelling arguments, and neither side has presented an effective alternative that I've seen. I unconvinced a baseline change allowing everyone to use Str over Dex at will is the best solution, and thus I remain neutral.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239340#post1239340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serious question: Do you ever actually play Exalted? Really play it? If so, how experienced is your group? Are you guys deliberately not optimizing? Or do people just sorta do whatever? Because in my experience, some players optimize, some do whatever, some sorta optimize, and some like to play people with weird ability spikes. If you have a Circle where everyone is optimizing, there are no problems, so if this is your experience, your reaction makes sense, you'd never have found a problem, but you also wouldn't be assuming I'm an idiot randomly buffing everything, because you would have seen for yourself what happens when someone combines Solar Dodge and Black Claw Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been playing Exalted since 1st edition. I can't even recall how many games I've been a part of, or was the ST for. I've played with new players, and with veterans of the system. I can sit here, and honestly tell you my in-game experience with the system would have to be measured in hundreds of hours (possibly 1000+). The current game I'm running will be hitting the 20th session next week. <i>For my players watching the forums, keep it up guys, you always keep me entertained as a ST!</i> So it's safe to say, I'm familiar with both the positive and negative aspects of all three editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239340#post1239340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, this isn't what I'm suggesting be addressed, because it's a much more complex failure state that can't easily be addressed, I don't think. The much easier failure state to address is &quot;One player took a heavy weapon and Dex 3, and now consistently fails to hit bosses, who tend to have 5 or 6 defense and are able to raise that&quot;. The Nephwrack can push itself to 8 defense pretty easily. Dex 3, Melee 4, Specialty (Grand Daiklave). That's 8 on Decisive. +5 from Excellency (these were Dragonblooded). That's 13. A max Excellency cannot hit the Nephwrack without being lucky. This, much like Bob, is a very &quot;just throw it together character&quot; who sounds cool.<br /> <br /> And, using just the corebook Charms, they cannot scratch the weakest of the powerful spirit boss enemies. This is something I consider to be a problem. And it's easily solved by saying &quot;Pick the higher of strength or dex to use in combat&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question: Did this Dragonblood (Dex 3, Melee 4, Specialty: Grand Daiklave) forget how to stunt? If he's a combat character, does he have any dice trick charms? I can keep going if you like? Could he not delay his decisive attack until his buddies added some onslaught penalties? Did he forget Willpower adds 1 success? It seems to me, this Dragonbloods player is either willingly refusing to use all his tools, or isn't aware of them to begin with. The former is entirely on the player, and he has no reason to complain. If it's the latter, I'd have a conversation with his ST because he's clearly not doing his job.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:57:25-07:00","id":1239583,"title":"","content":"I think this covers my points. The rest of it just seemed to be repeated multiple times in the thread.<br /> <br /> <b>#67 TalosX </b><br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s why we have the golden rule!\u201d<br /> <br /> Rule 0 fallacy. Do you need a definition? It supposes something isn't broken if it can be fixed. If the rule is not broken, it shouldn't <i>need</i> to be fixed.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019m saying is that a rule is broken/not working therefore it needs to be fixed. Attempting to fix such things with band-aid charms will never work, only mask the problem. It doesn\u2019t matter if they encourage charm development. I encourage it as well, but the charms will work better on a system with base alterations.<br /> <br /> &gt;The enemies shown so far show that you don\u2019t need a maxed out pool!<br /> <br /> Do you know why this is the case Talos? Its for people who don\u2019t optimize (definition below) for combat have a chance. The people who do optimize? They use them to wipe their ass in combat. This is great for people who just want a pure power fantasy with nothing capable of remotely challenging them. You want an isekai power trip? Go ahead, others like to have more tactical combat choices.<br /> <br /> You want an example of high end enemies? Viator of Nullspace in 2e. This thing wasn\u2019t made like a deathlord, you didn\u2019t need broken charms to beat it. But if you didn\u2019t know how the system worked by the time you fought it? Then holy crap you were going to be in hell. Hell is a nice place to be compared to leaping into shark infested waters covered in blood.<br /> <br /> You know why people want these enemies? There are very few people who have the time, skill, or motivation to make something like an end game enemy that can engage an entire group of Exalts. It isn\u2019t as simple as tweaking some numbers. Viator of Nullspace was an amazingly designed enemy because not only where his base stats and charms powerful but also had a backdoor of being able to use the entire spirit charmset if you needed additional power. There are some people who are capable of making the Lost Primordial for their players to fight against in their game. MadMaddy, Jon Chung, Plague of Hats, really most people who dig in have a shot at this. They don't need such things statted up because they're more than capable of doing it themselves. What they'd like are a few enemies who are capable of proving to be beyond a blip to a certain other crowd, which some were (Such as the Arete's in 2e)<br /> <br /> Optimization: In this context it means going the best you can in combat by making smart choices in build and powers. This isn\u2019t minmaxing where you sacrifice everything to kill everything but doing the best you can do with the tools given to you. 90% of the time this is people with Dexterity 5, Ability 5, specialty, and a relevant artifact weapon/good MA tactic/Brawl.<br /> <br /> <b>#74 \u2013 armyofwhispers</b><br /> <br /> OK, but wouldn\u2019t you like to have an extra charm or two for something you\u2019d really like for your character instead? Because that\u2019s what you can have if you don\u2019t get those filler charms. Every stat can still have awesome stuff, just less dull stuff now. In fact, since in a hypothetical example where you can use Strength to attack and parry to defend by default you don\u2019t need to spend tons of resources and months of experience to get something you can do by default! You can spend it on fun charms that support your character and his concept!<br /> <br /> But armyofwhispers! I\u2019m not advocating you can do this with a stunt! I\u2019m saying you can do this with a base system change!<br /> <br /> The change is supposed to be broad, effecting everything from not just Dragonblooded, but MORTALS and up. The problem doesn\u2019t exist for Dragonblooded and Solars, but everyone who uses PC rules. The fact that charms are pennies for dollars when compared to attribute raising is exactly *why* making an alternate attack stat would be a good idea, because they we could have more diversity in builds!<br /> <br /> As for saying it will not work? Have you tested this yourself? Have you listened to the others in this thread who have a differing viewpoint aside from your own and deeply thinking about it? Or just immediately thinking about it and going \u201cNa, too OP.\u201d Right now you\u2019re acting like you\u2019re doing the latter. I can tell you right now that after attempting to learn how the base system works and how charms work? It won\u2019t break the system over its knee. It will encourage more 5\u2019s in certain attributes yes, it\u2019d be like DnD 4e where putting a 16 or an 18 in your main class is a really good idea. Right now 3e is set up that taking Dex 2 is like taking a 14 in that stat. You can do it but damn you\u2019re going to feel some sting down the road.<br /> <br /> As for your houserule? Cool, go for it. People are going to swap their stats around so they get 5 in their defense/attacking stat. I question why it needs to exist.<br /> <br /> <b>#76 Heavy Arms</b><br /> <br /> Two base dice difference isn\u2019t that much of a gap you\u2019re right. But when it comes to Solar excellencies? The difference is very small. A dice gap of 3 dice is really edging it, going one over it makes it hard for players. This is because you can double your dice pool with excellencies, and if you\u2019re fighting an enemy that is deserving of something like that they\u2019re likely going to have some sort of defensive trick (EX: Stat buff) on them too. Three defense is much harder for dicepools to crack reliability without luck.<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t say Ex3 is broken for not using this fix. Defective is a better word. Exalted 2.Xe was broken. It had fundamental problems at the best including many problems for using Strength as Accuracy in that. If any player wanted that I\u2019d need to watch their build closely like a hawk to make sure cheese like Tyrant Lizard\u2019s are attempted, applying it to enemies is a waking nightmare as you\u2019d need to restat everything.<br /> <br /> Also grappling? Yay, the one single build I can do. I want to make a boxer instead? A raging barbarian? Oh right, I\u2019m told to get fucked. Oh well ballerina conan it is. As for if people need Dex 5, see TalosX\u2019s response below.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll side with you on the heavy weapons and non-optimized monsters. Heavy weapons only have a niche in clash builds which dual light weapons are better at (I love them so anyways) while enemies made for non-optimized players are good because those are what brings lifeblood into the game. Such people will need pre-statted enemies capable of engaging their friends who likely don\u2019t know much about the game. When they become more experienced, they can learn to make enemies more suitable for their group.<br /> <br /> You know what else brings lifeblood in? Removing trap options.<br /> <br /> <b>#75 TalosX</b> \u2013 If all your enemies are going to have 7 defense you\u2019ll have some really aggravated players. Even 6 is high at times. They\u2019re best saved for defense tanks. As TheCountAlucard said in #78, there are different ways to increase difficulty in encounters.<br /> <br /> But do you know when Bob isn\u2019t valid? It\u2019s when everyone in the group are playing 5/5 attack pools and he is not. They\u2019re going to have a fairly moderate advantage over Bob without needing to spend magic. If they go all out that means a potential six extra dice or +3 defense more than what Bob can bring.<br /> <br /> And if the other players are bored because the ST is designing encounters for Bob this is a problem. Either the other players are going to find encounters very easy or Bob will find them very difficult. This is the reason when I made my Monster guide I made the EX-Hard buffs. Bob groups can play in their game where optimization isn\u2019t as strong. Players who get bored of Bob group enemies can use EX-Hard for a little bit more challenge.<br /> <br /> &gt;\u201dBut that means you\u2019re saying they\u2019re not good enough!\u201d<br /> <br /> No, I\u2019m saying there are different groups and playstyles. What is fun for one group will bore another to sleep.<br /> <br /> <b>#77 The Wizard of Oz</b> \u2013 I don\u2019t blame you. Making enemies to challenge a circle of anything is hard simply due to the numbers advantage PC\u2019s have. In 2e this was ironically easier, but then you had all the issues that dealt with 2e. Enemies for long term characters are harder and more of a burden on the ST either by enemy complication or raw character count.<br /> <br /> <b>#81 Heavy Arms</b> \u2013 If you\u2019re one of the types that want to sit out of combat, then you don\u2019t need to worry.<br /> <br /> If you want to remotely take part in combat done the line? Its important.<br /> <br /> <b>#82 armyofwhispers</b> \u2013 The Dex character still has some pretty big advantages. He can go into dodge and disengage at will. If he\u2019s also specced into Athletics then the chances of the melee guy ever catching him are moot. You lose four damage, but without charms your defense might as well be infinite as your opponent cannot ever attack you.<br /> <br /> Heavy weapons, not touching that shit. Different topic.<br /> <br /> But claiming a new player is at fault for wanting to make a tried, tested and commonly played trope? That\u2019s called newbie hazing. It\u2019s a practice where we laugh at people who make horrible builds through no fault of their own.<br /> <br /> Also Exalted has been DnD. Vance made the Exalted into DnD 3.5e classes a while back, so if you want you can use the chosen system by Lord Gary Gygax, may he forever bless our saving throws amen, to play Exalted in a brand-new light!<br /> <br /> But god forbid characters be similar. I mean its not as if in other games I see characters who are interested spec into combat builds they like right? I mean its not as if we see Wizards aim for 16-18 INT all the time, Clerics with Wisdom, Rogues with Dexterity and Barbarians with Strength right?<br /> <br /> Oh\u2026Wait.<br /> <br /> <b>#102 Keichiokami</b> - Lunars can have lots of things. I just feel some things should be universal.<br /> <br /> You are however EXACTLY spot on about what saying about the 2e days. People used their own subjective and personal experience to gauge things as a whole. I tried to avoid this by over the ages asking and talking to other ST\u2019s about their wants and experiences with the system. How they do things well and various traps they fall into (either being new to GM\u2019ing or new to the system). Strength not being used for attack was one of them. It was minor compared to everything else (really STR to hit/defend was one 2.Xe\u2019s least important issues) but still there to annoy people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T00:50:05-07:00","id":1239594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239529#post1239529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Respect is a two way street. If people are going to hide behind insults rather than contribute anything of merit, they can present their point or move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great then stop talking, because your giant posts are 99.9% condescending asshole that don't contribute anything of merit, and 0.01% patting people on the back for agreeing with you.<br /> <br /> The respect you've shown me is, &quot;How dare you say I need to show my work! I'm going to condescend to you for being so stupid as to suggest I have to stoop to such things to anyone not on my kingly level of Exalted.&quot; So here's the two way street:<br /> <br /> You're a fraud. Jon Chung? Holden? They happily showed their work. They shoved their work down your throat whether you wanted to hear it or not, because they cared about showing that they knew what they were saying and not relying on reputation or experience to be taken seriously. You've spent 8 pages dodging showing your work. So the claim you can? I don't believe it, and I don't respect your claim you can.<br /> <br /> If you think you're being &quot;facetious&quot; or &quot;cute&quot; or &quot;funny&quot; though shit, you suck at it and it makes you sound more like an asshole and less like someone that cares about a calm civil discussion. You only want civility when it shuts up people calling you out because you can't back it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T02:27:25-07:00","id":1239610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239594#post1239594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great then stop talking, because your giant posts are 99.9% condescending asshole that don't contribute anything of merit, and 0.01% patting people on the back for agreeing with you.<br /> <br /> The respect you've shown me is, &quot;How dare you say I need to show my work! I'm going to condescend to you for being so stupid as to suggest I have to stoop to such things to anyone not on my kingly level of Exalted.&quot; So here's the two way street:<br /> <br /> You're a fraud. Jon Chung? Holden? They happily showed their work. They shoved their work down your throat whether you wanted to hear it or not, because they cared about showing that they knew what they were saying and not relying on reputation or experience to be taken seriously. You've spent 8 pages dodging showing your work. So the claim you can? I don't believe it, and I don't respect your claim you can.<br /> <br /> If you think you're being &quot;facetious&quot; or &quot;cute&quot; or &quot;funny&quot; though shit, you suck at it and it makes you sound more like an asshole and less like someone that cares about a calm civil discussion. You only want civility when it shuts up people calling you out because you can't back it up.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Okay I feel this crosses over into a personal attack, take a warning and reconsider your approach. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T02:46:21-07:00","id":1239612,"title":"","content":"You want evidence to back this up? Fine. We\u2019ll use <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/10e32\" target=\"_blank\">https://anydice.com/program/10e32</a> . We\u2019re going to calculate hit percentages.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s take an example of Bob and Chad. Bob has a character that\u2019s Strength 5, Dexterity 3 and Melee 3. Chad has a Strength 2, Dexterity 5 and Melee 5 fighter. Let\u2019s assume they\u2019re using a medium mundane weapon for accuracy of +2 and defense of +1. Final dicepools of 8 for Bob and 12 for Chad. Overall these are not abnormal builds that I\u2019ve seen for many people and both are Solars. Let\u2019s say Bob is Physical Primary and Chad is Physical secondary. No stunts are used during this process.<br /> <br /> <b>Test 1</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bob</b><br /> <br /> Bob can strike anyone with 4 defense for an average of 58.01% chance of hitting. With a 3m excellency he can hit an 81.18% average and with a 6m excellency he can roll 14 to hit with with a 92.65%. The returns diminish a lot after a certain point, so lets assume 3m is the sweet spot.<br /> <br /> If he wants to stand a chance of hitting a Nephwrack however at defense of 7 then his chance of hitting is at 9.97%. Really don\u2019t want to wait for that natural 20 to kick in to have a shot at hitting.<br /> <br /> But wait, we have excellencies for this case. He wants to spent 3m in order not to flare up a stage. A 3m excellency has a 31.34% chance of hitting. This is a big leap but not ideal.<br /> <br /> So he goes full in and strikes at with a full excellency. 6m for 6 dice, total of 14. This gives roughly 50/50 odds of hitting for a total chance of 56.11%. 50/50 chance if he goes all in.<br /> <br /> Wanna make a decisive attack? Cool! Let\u2019s say Bob has an artbitary amount of initiative needed to OHKO the Nephwrack. So now when we make the decisive attack? Your accuracy is now meaningless! 2.73% chance of hitting without any resources! You\u2019ll need a miracle for that one. But this is a decisive, we want to be cool and show off killing this evil monster that has taken a children\u2019s heart for evil schemes. So we add +3 dice and get\u2026 16.03% chance to hit. Even a decisive attack full of Bob\u2019s pain and sorrow contain only a 39.75% chance to actually end the battle.<br /> <br /> <b>Chad</b><br /> <br /> Chad has a much higher base dicepool. Hitting someone with 4 defense on average for him? That\u2019s an 86.07% chance. <i>That\u2019s already better than what Bob is doing spending resources on hitting his target</i>. If he\u2019s spend 3m for 15 dice he\u2019s rolling for 94.75%. This is like a Dragonball Z battle here. Chad can already hit his opponent at only a third of his power.<br /> <br /> The Nephwrack has a 39.75% chance of being hit. Roughly a little better than a third of a chance at hitting but if you\u2019re in tense combat you might not want to take those odds. So we\u2019ll beef it up bit. Chad can spend 3m and gain 63.47% chance to hit. <i>Three dice have given us nearly a +30% boost in hit chance.</i><br /> <br /> Futhermore Chad can go full anime and unleash his full power, 10m for 10 dice to get a 93.02% chance of hitting the Nephwrack. Barring horrible luck this will hit. Hell, just matching Bob\u2019s 6 additional dice still affords him an 80.70% chance to hit. 25% to 30% more than what Bob can do at his best.<br /> <br /> When Chad gains enough initiative to make his decisive attack? He barely feels it in the long run. A base decisive gives him a 23.28% chance of hitting. This is low but still already 10 times better than Bob. If Chad uses a third of his power because the Nephwrack dared to sully Chad\u2019s fine robes when the child\u2019s heart was torn out then he has a 48.12% chance of hitting with 13 dice. If he invokes the Forbidden Technique of his People to add +10 dice with all his might? He has an 88.14% chance of hitting the Nephwrack.<br /> <br /> <b>Result 1</b><br /> <br /> This is what I meant by dicepools being important. Even a +3 dice difference can be fairly large at overcoming the odds. Bob trying his best can only manage a roughly 50/50 chance of hitting. Chad on the other hand will have no such problems at all hitting. Do you know what this roughly means?<br /> <br /> First, the +3 damage that Bob would get over Chad is pointless. All the damage in the world doesn\u2019t matter if you can\u2019t hit your opponent for shit. Bob will need to blow his resources just for a 50/50 chance to hit a Nephwrack with his main bonus being +3 damage over Chad.<br /> <br /> Chad meanwhile is laughing to the bank. He can actually hit his target for less resources. Resources that can be spent on things like damage enhancing charms that RAPIDLY close the gap in damage far faster than merely having +3 additional strength will.<br /> <br /> If Bob wants to fix this drastic mistake? He\u2019ll need 8 XP for DEX 3. Not bad. 12 XP for Dex 4? Eh\u2026 A bit painful. 16 XP for Dex 5? Well shit there are two evocations Bob wanted gone down the toilet. Bob knew he was going to have to raise his Melee ability eventually, but damn man. He made physical his strongest attribute group and he\u2019s getting trounced by Chad who only dabbles in it.<br /> <br /> Chad meanwhile doesn\u2019t need to worry about this. He can buy those fancy new evocations he wanted with all that spare XP and not worry about his build.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t use flat of BP builds either. The principle holds the same that Chad is going to be able to buy the stuff he wanted and Bob is going to play catch up. The only time this doesn\u2019t hold true is if you\u2019re using flat XP with attributes costing 4 XP and charms 8 XP in which holy shit you got a pretty good steal there. Short term it will be felt but no one will feel it at like 150 XP in.<br /> <br /> <b>Test 2</b><br /> <br /> Let\u2019s make another test. Same characters, only this time Strength is allowed to be used to calculate Melee attack pools. Bob now has a base pool of 10, Chad has 12. Since Chad\u2019s results are going to be the same, we\u2019ll just do Bob.<br /> <br /> <b>Bob</b><br /> <br /> When attacking a defense 4 soldier? Wow, two dice of difference means that his chance of hitting has shot up nearly +20% to 74.96%! Bob doesn\u2019t need to blow resources to have a decent chance of hitting a battle ready troop. He can blow 3m to get 3 dice and get a 89.82% chance of hitting and nearly assure it, but since this is Exalted and not X-COM UFO Defense this means he\u2019ll likely hit.<br /> <br /> That scary Nephwrack? OK you\u2019re still a bit of a pain in the ass, but now at least Bob has a 23.28 chance of hitting him. If you\u2019re desperate then at least you won\u2019t be praying to RNGesus in your time of greatest need, though it does help. If Bob wants to add +3 dice for 3m? Oh shit, his chances of success have nearly <i>doubled</i>! He\u2019s at a 48.11% chance of hitting! Nearly a 50/50 chance of hitting! Attacking with all of his rage and sorrow lets him hit at a 70.06% chance! Another increase of nearly +20%! This isn\u2019t assured, but its at least reliable and would make for a tense fight to keep Bob on his toes.<br /> <br /> Time for a decisive? Well our accuracy is 8 now. A base attack still only has a 9.97% chance. Easier to roll a single d10 and hope for that 10 and nearly just as accurate. Adding +3 dice for 3m? Roughly 20% increase again for 31.34% chance of hitting. Good, but still risky odds. Going full blast? 56.11%. Oh shit. The tension\u2019s on now. Is Bob going to take revenge for the fallen child or is the Nephwrack going to get away?<br /> <br /> But wait! Since his attack pool is Strength + Melee he can add more dice! He can double his dice pool! 70.06% chance to hit that Nephwrack! BAM SON! Bob is more than likely going to vanish that monster and redeem the child.<br /> <br /> <b>Result 2</b><br /> <br /> Oh shit! Bob\u2019s character archtype just became a lot more viable because he can <i>actually hit things!</i> Even better charms such as Fire and Stones Strike hit like a nuke for him while being a (relatively) minor benefit for Chad. Chad is still going to still be better at hitting things period yes because more dice, Bob isn\u2019t falling behind as badly as he was before. With a relatively common newbie build he can still contribute heavily in combat and feel like the big damn hero that Exalted is supposed to make him out to be.<br /> <br /> His Melee score is 3, still behind Chad\u2019s. It costs him about 5 + 7 = 12 XP to increase Melee to 5. A bit of change but not overly taxing. In fact he\u2019s now on the same level as Chad in terms of attacking. Sure Chad is way more mobile than Bob, but Bob feels the tradeoff is not terrible because he can hit that little bit extra harder. Not enough to make a gamebreaking difference using charms, so both Bob and Chad play roughly at the same level. Plus he can use his high strength to grab Athletics and play the strongman! Awesome!<br /> <br /> <b>Final Result</b><br /> <br /> Allowing Bob to use his strength to hit actually allowed him to compete with the character idea he was envisioning. This is a noticeably better result than disappointment from being newbie hazed and overall happier.<br /> <br /> For damage? Charms are usually capable of overcoming that gap far more rapidly than just raw strength increases. You get some side benefits (Longer grappling times, Fire and Stones increasing in potency), but these are going to be side benefits. You'll be losing a lot of mobility on foot still. Most newbies who opt for this sort of build probably figure they're not going to be using dodge much.<br /> <br /> So mathematics wise? Yes it does work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 07-28-2018, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T05:52:02-07:00","id":1239643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239612#post1239612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want evidence to back this up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I want the full work shown (not of the math behind the hit percentages) of your logic. Evidence is a good start though. I'll get back to this to address the examples first.<br /> <br /> <br /> A few general points:<br /> <br /> 1) More dice is better wasn't in contention, so most of the examples don't really move the ball forward. It's just &quot;more dice is better.&quot; I'm pretty sure everyone here agreed that this was a mathematical truth of the game, and that allowing free choice of Strength or Dexterity would be an avenue for some character to have more dice, thus preform better on hit percentages.<br /> <br /> 2) The Nephwracks really don't demonstrate much, because hit percentages aren't everything. I'm pretty sure nobody is going to accidentally make a starting level Solar that could hope to actually solo kill a Nephwrack with Melee; I'm not sure how well one of us could build as optimal an anti-Nephrwrack character as possible knowing one's stats from the core book that would still be able to Melee kill one. Bob and Chad both die against one pretty clearly despite being Solars, because Bob can't hit often, and Chad can't hit hard enough; the Nephwrack can stalemate either of them until they run out of motes (assuming they have the stats to resist Clinging Shadow Miasma and Dawn of the Dead Stars), and then wear them down and kill them.<br /> <br /> 3) Choosing Solars also skews things away from examples that are going to matter across the board. If you're saying this needs to be a mortals level rule, getting into Solar Charms is a distraction from the point. Mortal Bob and Chad vs. the Battle Ready Troops/Medium Infantry stat block are both going to easily win. Bob will probably take longer to get the job done, but the math is totally in his favor to win. The +2 dice for Mortal Bob using Strength instead is just going to speed it up a little.<br /> <br /> 4) And, of course the bane of white rooms is so much of this doesn't apply in real play where you have other characters involved. This doesn't address things like Bob still being able to add Onslaught penalties to a tough baddie for Chad to smash even better, which is something the game is supposed to include. Not being able to deliver the big hits doesn't mean you're sitting out of combat, there are support things you can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Bob wants to fix this drastic mistake? He\u2019ll need 8 XP for DEX 3. Not bad. 12 XP for Dex 4? Eh\u2026 A bit painful. 16 XP for Dex 5? Well shit there are two evocations Bob wanted gone down the toilet. Bob knew he was going to have to raise his Melee ability eventually, but damn man. He made physical his strongest attribute group and he\u2019s getting trounced by Chad who only dabbles in it. </div> </div> </div>This is a very different issue to me, much like heavy weapons sucking. I'm not a fan of Exalted's XP system in the slightest. And we both seem to agree that moving to a flat XP addresses this particular concern without the Attribute swapping issue coming into play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wow, two dice of difference means that his chance of hitting has shot up nearly +20% to 74.96%! </div> </div> </div>And Bob could have just switched to a light weapon for the same effect (or light main hand, medium off hand), since his base damage is more than high enough against 8 soak. Equipment is not my favorite thing here, but Bob's concept isn't specifically tied to a weapon (if so he'd have a specialty for it and +1 die), so the more beneficial shield + short sword combo, or a whip for that sweet sweet grappling tag that actually synergizes more with his stats does make a difference here.<br /> <br /> The goal though, is to make Strength 5/Dex 3 more fun, and as such the current weapon rules, as flawed as they are do accomplish this fairly well in terms of allowing Bob to reliably hit in combat if he takes weapons that suit his stats. How the weapon synergies work is is.... questionable, but that's a lot down to equipment design, not which Attributes you can use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Allowing Bob to use his strength to hit actually allowed him to compete with the character idea he was envisioning. This is a noticeably better result than disappointment from being newbie hazed and overall happier. </div> </div> </div>This is where the &quot;show your work&quot; really needs to be applied though. This is the gap where you're not presenting the argument.<br /> <br /> How is this not the character as envisioned? He wasn't built as a pinnacle of combat, he was built to be really good by mortal standards with some extra oomph to carry him through fights with mortals, but wasn't built to easily take on the bigger nasties of the setting without significant outlay of resources and/or help. Regardless of the Strength vs. Dexterity, he's only got Melee 3, that's &quot;awesome for a mortal, OK-ish for an Exalted&quot; which is exactly how he preforms. <br /> <br /> He's also getting &quot;hazed&quot; by things like forced sub-optimal equipment choices. I'm fairly confident that mortal Bob with a whip and the RAW is going to feel a lot less &quot;hazed&quot; than mortal Bob with a chopping sword that can attack with Strength instead. The first might not be the best fighter, but when he lands that Grapple... he can do a lot, where Chopping Bob is just more dice that make him slightly less behind Chad.<br /> <br /> What you're not answering here, is where does this go from, &quot;this is a house rule some people might enjoy,&quot; to, &quot;this is a rule that should be changed across the board.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can make Bob builds that pass the tests of beating up on Battle Ready Soldiers without needing to switch to Strength. There is an unfounded assumption that Bob was build to be a top dog combatant despite not being built that way that isn't addressed in making his better automatically. There's even an unfounded assumption that Chad's physical secondary assignment means he's &quot;dabbling&quot; when he's the one with Melee 5 (which is half of his advantage over Bob in your examples).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Charms are usually capable of overcoming that gap far more rapidly than just raw strength increases. </div> </div> </div>Why isn't this an argument for Strength doing more on the raw damage side of things? Why is it OK for Charms to fix this? Not that I think it's a good rule, but wouldn't having raw damage be Strength x 2 + Weapon damage make Bobs way more effective than increasing their accuracy? <br /> <br /> As it stands, to quote earlier, &quot;Accuracy is the god-stat.&quot; Hitting matters the most, because soak and damage are current set so that same class of weapon vs same class of armor leaves you a few dice over your minimum damage anyway, with Strength and Stamina cancelling each other. There is no reasonable trade off of accuracy for damage that's worth it. Letting people attack with Strength doesn't change that. Having Strength do more to create high raw damage that's worth not hitting as frequently would, and would make Bob's more fun too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'll be losing a lot of mobility on foot still. </div> </div> </div>Depends entirely an how you're invested though. Dex 3/Athletics 5 beats Dex 5/Athletics 1 on this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most newbies who opt for this sort of build probably figure they're not going to be using dodge much. </div> </div> </div>True... but seems another side tangent where Dodge's non-Evasion uses aren't called out adequately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So mathematics wise? Yes it does work. </div> </div> </div>It makes Bob has more dice, yes.<br /> <br /> It doesn't demonstrate an actual problem (why is having 6 dice to hit and not hitting every a bad thing?), nor does it demonstrate that this is the proper fix for the problem of Bobs not necessarily being as fun in combat as they should be (aka why should Strength just copy Dexterity instead of doing something else?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T13:18:12-07:00","id":1239778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I want the full work shown (not of the math behind the hit percentages) of your logic. Evidence is a good start though. I'll get back to this to address the examples first.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want that then please specifically say what you want me to address. Most of my point about using Strength to hit is largely a dice pool one and to show how dice are important when planning. If you want me to expand upon it then I\u2019ll gladly do so. Otherwise we\u2019ll go back to talking past each other more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) More dice is better wasn't in contention, so most of the examples don't really move the ball forward. It's just &quot;more dice is better.&quot; I'm pretty sure everyone here agreed that this was a mathematical truth of the game, and that allowing free choice of Strength or Dexterity would be an avenue for some character to have more dice, thus preform better on hit percentages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is one reason why I believe it should be a default rule. It allows more flexibility in starting build variations even for newbies. I\u2019ll address why the base dice is so important later.<br /> <br /> Also more dice is better <i>to a certain point</i>. That part is important. At some point the gap between Bob and Chad narrows to a point where you get diminishing returns. Chad can make his 80% go up to 93% but would that be worth the 4 additional motes? That\u2019s for a player to decide. Unless you\u2019re attempting to do something with that generally you might be better off with damage enhancers in case you do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The Nephwracks really don't demonstrate much, because hit percentages aren't everything. I'm pretty sure nobody is going to accidentally make a starting level Solar that could hope to actually solo kill a Nephwrack with Melee; I'm not sure how well one of us could build as optimal an anti-Nephrwrack character as possible knowing one's stats from the core book that would still be able to Melee kill one. Bob and Chad both die against one pretty clearly despite being Solars, because Bob can't hit often, and Chad can't hit hard enough; the Nephwrack can stalemate either of them until they run out of motes (assuming they have the stats to resist Clinging Shadow Miasma and Dawn of the Dead Stars), and then wear them down and kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I randomly choose an enemy from the book that could be something a new ST would pick for a group challenge new or experienced ST alike. The important part isn\u2019t the rest of the Nephwracks stats, its his actual defense pool. How hard he is to hit. My point was it doesn\u2019t matter what the rest of his combat stats are if you can\u2019t actually hit and do anything to him in the first place. This would be important if an enemy had difficulty reaching something like defense 7, but for a Nephwrack won\u2019t break sweat doing so.<br /> <br /> In a more fleshed out example the Nephwracks other abilities will come into play. But for planning encounters like this? Base dice pools actually do matter. If they\u2019re going to have trouble at a base then things are only going to get a lot worse when magic is added. You can say things like design encounters to take that into account but now we have a problem: The ST needs to make encounters for both Bob and Chad. This is like oil and water. You could probably force the two to mix but that is pretty difficult. You can plan events in the battle that would give more situational dice to hit? Sure, but if you\u2019re planning an encounter where an event needs to happen before the boss you\u2019re fighting becomes enjoyable rather than a slog? You need to take a step back, something bad happened along the way. Unless you\u2019re fighting a final boss (or forgot a McGuffin the ST told you an enemy was weak to) or new to GM\u2019ing then I don\u2019t see why you\u2019d do this intentionally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Choosing Solars also skews things away from examples that are going to matter across the board. If you're saying this needs to be a mortals level rule, getting into Solar Charms is a distraction from the point. Mortal Bob and Chad vs. the Battle Ready Troops/Medium Infantry stat block are both going to easily win. Bob will probably take longer to get the job done, but the math is totally in his favor to win. The +2 dice for Mortal Bob using Strength instead is just going to speed it up a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>No the mortal dicepools are important because if things are messed up on that level it ripples throughout the entire game. This is one thing Holden and Morke meant by making mortals important in the system narratively and mechanically. Yes, mechanically too. In 2.Xe a mortal versus a supernal creature? It usually didn\u2019t matter what his weapon was, unless you\u2019re fighting glass cannons you\u2019re either going to be 1 damage once in a blue moon when you hit or never hit because of the bloated dicepools in that edition. In Third Edition? Any mortal can hurt any supernal creature in theory. If his initiative is high enough, he can pose a threat to your health levels. Supernatural creatures now at least need to sweat a tiny bit if a mortal wants to attack them, pump your defense stat or hope you have some sort of anti-decisive methods.<br /> <br /> Chad and Bob would finish the soldier off eventually as mortals or Solars pretending to be mortals (no charms), but Chad is going to have such an advantage that its not even funny. A nearly 30% difference? That\u2019s a difference between flipping a coin and a near certain hit. Bob might struggle a bit with him, Chad is likely going blow through him. Bob is really going to be praying his damage dice turns up as successes when he does hit as that\u2019s important. Chad isn\u2019t going to be doing as much damage but he\u2019s going to be a much better position if hit because he\u2019s more than likely going to hit more, therefore more damage, therefore more initiative to pad his character if hit by withering or more quickly build up to a decisive. Hell, if anything Chad\u2019s number advantage potentially allows a chance for better damage on average because Exalted uses threshold successes for withering damage.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/247548999718928384/472753320944074763/unknown.png\" target=\"_blank\">Don\u2019t take my word for it. Here\u2019s the proof</a>. (Ignore the rest of the table, that\u2019s for a special rules hack homebrew. Look at the threshold successes). On average Bob is going to be hitting at threshold or maybe with an additional success most of the time. Chad is going to hit with 2 threshold on average, possibly 3. That\u2019s to Lumi from the Exalted Discord for that information<br /> <br /> +2 dice for Bob means the difference of coin flipping or reliably hitting in the same realm as Chad. It\u2019s not a \u201cbit\u201d faster. It\u2019s a lot faster and a lot less painful. This is one reason why a +2 dice bonus to stunting is in the game. It\u2019s a crutch to let people with lower dicepools do stuff, which is good as we don\u2019t want to go back to the 2.Xe version where if you didn\u2019t have 8 dice in a pool minimum then don\u2019t bother (For Dragonblooded they also needed to have a +3 specialty or not bother).<br /> <br /> This is why I say base dice pools are so important when talking to new people. A difference of +3 dice might not seem like a lot but its pretty significant. Any more than that and other players are going to struggle to keep up in most circumstances.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) And, of course the bane of white rooms is so much of this doesn't apply in real play where you have other characters involved. This doesn't address things like Bob still being able to add Onslaught penalties to a tough baddie for Chad to smash even better, which is something the game is supposed to include. Not being able to deliver the big hits doesn't mean you're sitting out of combat, there are support things you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your base math is fucked from the get go then it will be downhill from there. It gives a limitus test for your encounters, how your matchup is going to go just by looking at it rather than playing it out (Which unless you can see the future, is important for encounter design). Onslaught penalties are a thing yes but what if Chad needs to head off and deal with incoming zombie reinforcements? What if he\u2019s telling Bob to wait as his silk clothes got dirty and he needs to clean them? Bob is going to struggle to hold that line. If the reverse is true? Chad laughs as he\u2019ll easily deal with the Nephwrack.<br /> <br /> But also brings up my other point: Bob is likely wanting to fight this thing as his character concept! Even if you ignore fluff examples, just by looking at stats we could assume \u201cOK he\u2019s physical primary and attack ability 3. Melee 3 is likely what he heard from the book/others that such a thing is above average skill in the game world while Strength 5 makes him one of the most impressive beefcakes in the world.\u201d Unless he says otherwise, Bob is in this character to fight.<br /> <br /> Do you know how bad it would be for Bob to go through a Test 1 scenario and talk to the frustrated ST after?<br /> <br /> ST: \u201cOh sorry, I didn\u2019t realize. I was assuming Chad would\u2019ve fought the Nephwrack while you used Feats of Strength to hold up a crashing building.\u201d<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a boot to the balls. That\u2019s saying you\u2019re character is second fiddle to Chad when it comes to combat, a person who while knows the game is treating combat as a largely side thing. You need to give players the freedom to do what they want, and if there are less traps to deal with for both new ST\u2019s and players to deal with? The better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very different issue to me, much like heavy weapons sucking. I'm not a fan of Exalted's XP system in the slightest. And we both seem to agree that moving to a flat XP addresses this particular concern without the Attribute swapping issue coming into play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I considering something like a birth defect of sorts. A lot of birth defects can happen by themselves but tend to amplify or worsen each other. Spina Bifida is an example of this. It can occur by itself, but if you do have it you could have other mental health issues that go along with it. If you\u2019re really unlucky this could trigger a domino effect.<br /> <br /> One thing can lead into another thing that is worse. You can fix the worse thing sure, but even then you\u2019d still be left with the other problem.<br /> <br /> (Also as I said, you can swap out to nearly XP system you want, you\u2019ll still have this problem).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Bob could have just switched to a light weapon for the same effect (or light main hand, medium off hand), since his base damage is more than high enough against 8 soak. Equipment is not my favorite thing here, but Bob's concept isn't specifically tied to a weapon (if so he'd have a specialty for it and +1 die), so the more beneficial shield + short sword combo, or a whip for that sweet sweet grappling tag that actually synergizes more with his stats does make a difference here.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Nephwrack could\u2019ve had a magic spell to increase his parry by another +1. Maybe Bob is using his Father\u2019s sword? Maybe he wants a sword to go along with his big he-man type character and sees knifes as toothpicks? Who knows. My point was to illustrate dice pools and how they\u2019re important.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The goal though, is to make Strength 5/Dex 3 more fun, and as such the current weapon rules, as flawed as they are do accomplish this fairly well in terms of allowing Bob to reliably hit in combat if he takes weapons that suit his stats. How the weapon synergies work is is.... questionable, but that's a lot down to equipment design, not which Attributes you can use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t shift the goalposts. As I said doing damage wasn\u2019t the point here, because if you can\u2019t hit then all the damage in the world isn\u2019t going to do jack. Do you want a weapon that hits once out of a hundred times but does a 100 withering damage if it hits or do you want a weapon that hits 100/100 times and only does one damage each? With the way 3e works you\u2019re going to want the latter. It will pad your initiative, it will save you from crash, and it will actually allow you build up decisive attacks that deal damage a lot sooner. If you want to talk about weapons then take it somewhere else.<br /> <br /> If we can bring player\u2019s averages overall closer by letting them attack with Strength by default, why not do this?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is where the &quot;show your work&quot; really needs to be applied though. This is the gap where you're not presenting the argument.<br /> <br /> How is this not the character as envisioned? He wasn't built as a pinnacle of combat, he was built to be really good by mortal standards with some extra oomph to carry him through fights with mortals, but wasn't built to easily take on the bigger nasties of the setting without significant outlay of resources and/or help. Regardless of the Strength vs. Dexterity, he's only got Melee 3, that's &quot;awesome for a mortal, OK-ish for an Exalted&quot; which is exactly how he preforms.<br /> <br /> He's also getting &quot;hazed&quot; by things like forced sub-optimal equipment choices. I'm fairly confident that mortal Bob with a whip and the RAW is going to feel a lot less &quot;hazed&quot; than mortal Bob with a chopping sword that can attack with Strength instead. The first might not be the best fighter, but when he lands that Grapple... he can do a lot, where Chopping Bob is just more dice that make him slightly less behind Chad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not addressing weapon accuracy or damage. I am addressing base dicepools and how those apply to base difficulties. With weapon accuracy you are making a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hfil34ayaEU\" target=\"_blank\">strawman</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're not answering here, is where does this go from, &quot;this is a house rule some people might enjoy,&quot; to, &quot;this is a rule that should be changed across the board.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can make Bob builds that pass the tests of beating up on Battle Ready Soldiers without needing to switch to Strength. There is an unfounded assumption that Bob was build to be a top dog combatant despite not being built that way that isn't addressed in making his better automatically. There's even an unfounded assumption that Chad's physical secondary assignment means he's &quot;dabbling&quot; when he's the one with Melee 5 (which is half of his advantage over Bob in your examples).</div> </div> </div> </div>You know why I used excellencies and Melee in this example? Anything Bob can do Chad is likely going to do just as well if not better because his base dicepool is better. Excellent Strike will give a better return, Rising Sun Slash is going to proc a HELL of a lot harder with Chad, when Chad uses Fire and Stones he\u2019s likely to hit and do that bit of additional damage compared to Bob who wastes 5m and gets nothing if he misses (and the chances are against him).<br /> <br /> I can likely make builds for Bob that will allow him to fight against the Nephwrack better too. But when we get into the realm of certain splat charms, evocations, martial arts and more? Things become a lot more complicated. Those kinds of encounters really need to be tailor made to a specific character, and if Bob and Chad are nearly oil and water? That is going to much, much harder as you need to start from two bases rather than one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why isn't this an argument for Strength doing more on the raw damage side of things? Why is it OK for Charms to fix this? Not that I think it's a good rule, but wouldn't having raw damage be Strength x 2 + Weapon damage make Bobs way more effective than increasing their accuracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>That little change is going to affect the system a bit more. You can do so, but some of the damage-armour ratio might be messed up in that circumstance. Using Strength to hit is less intrusive (That being how much of the game needs to change when a new rule, homebrew or otherwise, is introduced. If I was in 2e saying that all attacks now have a +1 raw damage boost across the board is not major. 2.5e banning Essence Ping was far more intrusive and made Adorjan Infernals cry).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it stands, to quote earlier, &quot;Accuracy is the god-stat.&quot; Hitting matters the most, because soak and damage are current set so that same class of weapon vs same class of armor leaves you a few dice over your minimum damage anyway, with Strength and Stamina cancelling each other. There is no reasonable trade off of accuracy for damage that's worth it. Letting people attack with Strength doesn't change that. Having Strength do more to create high raw damage that's worth not hitting as frequently would and would make Bob's more fun too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Giving people the ability to attack using Strength in Brawl/Melee gives them a few more dice on average for damage yes. I consider that a fair trade off. You\u2019re trading raw offense for less defense and utility. Even if we do this rule I\u2019m not advocating making Strength only for attack. That\u2019s dumb. I\u2019m saying to let it be higher of Strength or Dexterity. In this case Dexterity can be used to hit, to defend, SPEED (very important), Dodge, Stealth, Archery/thrown accuracy (I do not think letting Strength be used to hit in these as the normal is OK) and most non-FoS charms in the Athletics tree (a majority).<br /> <br /> Strength? They get on average a bit more damage to each attack, better grapples (for rounds of control and slamming), Feats of Strength, and Strength+Socialize. Grapples need builds based around them specifically so if you want melee they\u2019re out. Feats of Strength are useful, but they\u2019re not omni-applicable as Dexterity still is. Overall you will get a better a better deal with Dexterity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends entirely an how you're invested though. Dex 3/Athletics 5 beats Dex 5/Athletics 1 on this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, because of higher dice pools. But if you\u2019re Melee/Brawl based you might want a bit of investment in Athletics even stat wise for mobility. Universally true for everyone in the system with the way how movement works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True... but seems another side tangent where Dodge's non-Evasion uses aren't called out adequately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Semi sorta. First is that anyone who looks at the Dodge ability are going to logically assume \u201cOh, this must be used for dodging in some fashion\u201d. If the player or ST know that disengaging as a mechanic exists and that it uses dodge and that to move out of close range from someone opposing, you that you need to use Disengage? I think the book does a good job of saying this. It doesn\u2019t tell the averages, but it does tell you that you need this pool to disengage.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re making a he-man type character who takes on any challenger? You\u2019re probably going to dump it. Many, many melee specialists do this from 2e to 3e.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239643#post1239643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes Bob has more dice, yes.<br /> <br /> It doesn't demonstrate an actual problem (why is having 6 dice to hit and not hitting every a bad thing?), nor does it demonstrate that this is the proper fix for the problem of Bobs not necessarily being as fun in combat as they should be (aka why should Strength just copy Dexterity instead of doing something else?).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having 6 dice to hit is a bad thing when you literally have a one in ten chance of hitting a target? How about when you have 50/50 chance when you\u2019re trying your absolute best? This doesn\u2019t make you feel in control of the narrative or character, and when that happens it creates a feeling of powerlessness. This doesn\u2019t make a character feel powerful, it makes what they do completely random.<br /> In DnD 4e you can get Leaders to buff your attack or a method to make them burst for an instant to REALLY dig into an enemy. You don\u2019t need to dig really deep or hard into this. The math of the system makes it so that you can boost your chance of hitting a target you have a pretty good chance of doing so, even if it was 50/50 originally. So long as primary attribute is minimum 16 or ideally 18 then you\u2019re going to be just fine. The default to attack your opponent with melee attacks is only one attribute of +STR, but your class gives you the ability to swap this to another attribute for free.<br /> <br /> In Exalted excellencies are often the most efficient and common dice adders. Unlike DnD and other systems it does not have alternate stats for going down different paths by default. You pick Dexterity or you\u2019re hazed. That Nephwrack you wanted to take a heroic chance against? You have little to no control over that. You feel like you\u2019re playing a game to the whims of fate. Unlike DnD 4e aside from using onslaught there are not as many options Chad can use outside of directly applying onslaught. Empowering Shout if we really want to be generous, but it still leads to the same problem. Bob needs Chad in order to fulfill his character concept of being the strong he-man he likely wanted, the opposite is not true. This is like playing DnD 4e and having a minmaxed Barbarian multiclassed fighter in your game, as for a major portion of the game those things can often a lot things all by themselves for a long part of the game itself (Maybe it was errata\u2019d? The point is it still existed)<br /> <br /> Strength is being thrown a bone in 3e by expanding it. As an attribute its not nearly as valuable as the others are. Stamina is good, Stamina gives soak and boosts resistance pools, these are very handy as this is how not to die to poison or illness. It gives some additional soak which reduces raw withering damage. Strength meanwhile has Feats of Strength and\u2026 that\u2019s really it? The raw damage is there but is eclipsed by damage from charms. For gods sake Fists of Iron lets you ignore (Essence + Intimacy) soak for 1m. That\u2019s a potential +5 damage immediately <i>for a single mote!</i> You\u2019d need five extra dots of strength to match what a Strength 1 brawl user can do! How the hell is a person new to the game going to feel with the nerdy Twilight can punch through armour better than his he-man swordsman can? He\u2019s going to feel like a sucker!<br /> <br /> Why should Strength copy Dexterity when it comes to attacking with Brawl/Melee? As I said before, <i>to reduce trap options and make it so each player can have an enjoyable time with their build</i> <i>as the envision it</i>. Bob doesn't feel like his he-man fighter should be a ballerina, why should he be forced to pick between being functional or playing the concept he wants?<br /> <br /> The reason why Lunars getting these attribute swappers? Their excellency. Rather than having a universal DEX+ATT dicepool for attacking, they can vary it up with things like STR+CHA, DEX+INT, or parry with STA+APP. Cool. That\u2019s a good idea. My point is why don\u2019t we go deeper and tackle the root issue with this rather than treating a surface problem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T17:17:27-07:00","id":1239847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239778#post1239778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want that then please specifically say what you want me to address.</div> </div> </div> </div>This statement is not good for the civility of the discussion. If I say, &quot;I'll get to it later in the post,&quot; don't complain that it's not in the section you're quoting. It's rude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of my point about using Strength to hit is largely a dice pool one and to show how dice are important when planning. </div> </div> </div>Which is why it remains a preference as you're constructing it, not a flaw that needs errata. There isn't a flaw in the system with PCs being able to get high dice-pools there's just a less broad method of doing so than you'd like, and free Strength/Dexterity switching for close combat attacks doesn't guarantee builds that resolve the planning issues you bring up. A Strength 2/Dexterity 3/Ability 3 character in a group with multiple 5/3 or 3/5 + 5s in their Ability characters remains a planning issue, and actually gets worse because you have more traits contributing to the dice-pool you're planning around to track.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I randomly choose an enemy from the book that could be something a new ST would pick for a group challenge new or experienced ST alike. </div> </div> </div>But the examples don't take into account &quot;pick for a group challenge,&quot; at all. Bob, in a group, isn't going to be facing the Nephrwrack (or whatever non-Legendary Size higher end solo enemy) at full Parry/Evasion, because the Chads are going to be going first most of the time, and bringing defense down to levels easier for Bob to handle.<br /> <br /> Something that's going to give a circle of Solars a decent fight doesn't really prove much in a one-on-one fight besides &quot;it has high enough stats to make that a questionable thing to throw at a new character.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The important part isn\u2019t the rest of the Nephwracks stats, its his actual defense pool. </div> </div> </div>Then the important part shouldn't be Bob or Chad's other stuff either; including Charms. And considering a Nephwrack can inflict -9 dice to hit it with two Charms that are scene length if you can't counter them (directly or other ways)... that's as important to his defense as Excellencies are to the other's offense. -9 to hit is a huge impact on &quot;how hard a Nephwrack is to hit&quot; even if it isn't expressed in boosted defense (because it's three different -3 penalties that can all be overcome separately).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But for planning encounters like this? Base dice pools actually do matter. </div> </div> </div>Sure. But lots of things matter. Onslaught negation matters a ton in planning encounters because something with them forces each PC to deal with its defense more directly, while one's without are easier on a mixed group where the more optimized characters will knock down high DVs, letting the lower dice-pool characters get hits in.<br /> <br /> This is why &quot;it's just about dice-pools,&quot; really isn't a sufficient logical basis for making this a universal rule: dice-pools aren't the only thing that matters, and such a rule needs to be examined in full context, not just if it has an impact on one aspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ST needs to make encounters for both Bob and Chad. This is like oil and water. </div> </div> </div>Only if you insist on dice-pools being the sole metric. You're artificially forcing Bob to measure up to Chad, by forcing Bob to fight like Chad, instead of the two fighting smart together and playing to each other's strengths.<br /> <br /> For all the talk about expanding options, it's still keeping Accuracy as all that matters.<br /> <br /> Though if we were talking about something like the Distract Gambit allowing different hit dice-pools? You'd sell me easily on that. Because &quot;I threaten the enemy to distract them,&quot; relying on hitting with Dexterity + Ability first is strange as a specific rule since it means your ability to be threatening doesn't actually matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No the mortal dicepools are important because if things are messed up on that level it ripples throughout the entire game. </div> </div> </div>Right, which is why I said making the examples Solars distracts from the core of your argument. Things should be evident at mortal levels, not when you start getting into Solar Charms. You're skipping showing that things are &quot;messed up&quot; on that level when you jump right into Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chad and Bob would finish the soldier off eventually as mortals or Solars pretending to be mortals (no charms), but Chad is going to have such an advantage that its not even funny. </div> </div> </div>But Bob can close the gap, eliminate it, and even overcome that advantage with the tools in the system as it stands. Bob doesn't <b>need</b> your proposed rule to do so. You've simply set the terms of the example to deny those.<br /> <br /> If Bob can close the gap without your house rule, where is the objective flaw in the system that it addresses?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, if anything Chad\u2019s number advantage potentially allows a chance for better damage on average because Exalted uses threshold successes for withering damage </div> </div> </div>Chad does more damage on average by hitting more frequently. The math on the thresholds leave Bob with the edge on average post-soak damage per hit. Not by much, but those are the numbers presented. That's even backed up by your link. Chard's +2 damage from thresholds is less than Bobs +3 higher base damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is why I say base dice pools are so important when talking to new people. </div> </div> </div>Nobody is saying otherwise. We're saying we don't need another default avenue of improving them. Bob with Melee 5 and a specialty closes the gap with Chad to 1 without needing to use Strength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your base math is fucked from the get go then it will be downhill from there. </div> </div> </div>As far as I can tell, the base math isn't fucked. The Bob and Chad examples are working entirely as the game says they should as much as can be assessed in constrained white-room examples.<br /> <br /> [quote...but what if Chad needs to head off and deal with incoming zombie reinforcements? What if he\u2019s telling Bob to wait as his silk clothes got dirty and he needs to clean them? Bob is going to struggle to hold that line. If the reverse is true? Chad laughs as he\u2019ll easily deal with the Nephwrack.[/quote]<br /> <br /> Why would you send Chad to deal with a zombie battle group instead of Bob? What does cleaning silks have to do with any of this?<br /> <br /> And, of course, Chad faces the Nephwrack alone, and gets killed, because his ability to hit isn't enough to actually win (or gets removed because he's smacked with -9 to hit, a Defense penalty, and can't move to get away from the aura of doom).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bob is likely wanting to fight this thing as his character concept! </div> </div> </div>On two 1-5 range choices, Bob was built in the middle for both. That does not communicate (with the character creation resources in this game) a concept built to be a top tier fighter. If my players want to smash mortals with ease and spar with top tier NPCs from the book, they're taking at least 5 in their combat Ability to communicate that.<br /> <br /> You're presenting a false dichotomy where &quot;wants to fight&quot; is a binary state of, &quot;wants to fight at the highest levels and thus needs the best dice pools,&quot; or &quot;doesn't want to fight&quot; and skipping everyone that wants to make a combat secondary style character that can hold their own in minor fights, and is there to largely help the combat primary characters... who don't need to max their pools to accomplish that play goal.<br /> <br /> Bob is built like a combat secondary, and your examples show that he performs as such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That\u2019s saying you\u2019re character is second fiddle to Chad when it comes to combat,... </div> </div> </div>Chad's designed better for combat... and clearly so in a fashion that does not require system mastery to notice. If Bob's player needs to be told Bob is second fiddle to Chad in combat... the problem is not the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You need to give players the freedom to do what they want, and if there are less traps to deal with for both new ST\u2019s and players to deal with? The better. </div> </div> </div>Where's the trap? Bob didn't take Melee 5 and a specialty by choice, not because the system tricked him into thinking this wasn't a good idea. Hell, if Bob wants to invest heavily in Solar Melee, his player is going to look at the Charms and see that he'll need Melee 4 and 5 very quickly to actually buy them.<br /> <br /> That's not a trap. The book reinforces on multiple fronts that you should take advantage of the relatively cheap starting Abilities to get your main ones into the 4 or 5 range. This literally involves ignoring the book saying &quot;Think Larger Than Life,&quot; and things like the book saying to invest in your Caste/Favored Abilities at creation with bonus points over most other options. <br /> <br /> [quote]Maybe Bob is using his Father\u2019s sword?[/quotes]<br /> <br /> Swords can be light weapons. Also, if this is so important.. Specialty? You're asserting a lot about concept, but using stats that don't actually reflect the concept issues you're bringing up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don\u2019t shift the goalposts. </div> </div> </div>How is this a goal post shift? Are you saying your rule isn't being put in place to make Strength focused combat characters more fun to play? That seems to be very much what you've said about this so far. So I'm confused now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I said doing damage wasn\u2019t the point here, because if you can\u2019t hit then all the damage in the world isn\u2019t going to do jack. </div> </div> </div>And your math shows that Bob can hit, even if less reliably than Chad, so damage could start to matter if the system encouraged it to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you want a weapon that hits once out of a hundred times but does a 100 withering damage if it hits or do you want a weapon that hits 100/100 times and only does one damage each? </div> </div> </div>Hyperbole isn't helping on the civility front.<br /> <br /> Do I think the game would be better for making Strength focused combatants fun if there was more parity between the Initiative gains done between with less frequent hits with lots of damage and more frequent hits with lower damage? YES.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think it's actually what most people want out of a higher end Bob style build. They want a character that doesn't always hit, but makes up for it with big damage when they do. I don't think most people want Strength and Dexterity to overlap more in practice, and they want a Strength focused build to do it's own thing that's viable and different from a Dexterity focused build. IME people don't want Accuracy 1 with X other stuff, and Accuracy 2 with Y other stuff out of Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we can bring player\u2019s averages overall closer by letting them attack with Strength by default, why not do this? </div> </div> </div>Because I can bring their averages closer without it, not dilute the differences between Strength and Dexterity (which is different from wanting to make Dexterity less god-stat), and not deal with previously mentioned issues with Charm structures being based on these traits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not addressing weapon accuracy or damage. </div> </div> </div>You included weapon accuracy in your examples so.. no strawman. Also, please refresh yourself with the fallacy fallacy.<br /> <br /> Also, don't be rude, I know what a strawman is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know why I used excellencies and Melee in this example? </div> </div> </div>Because Solar Excellencies create the largest effective gap between base dice-pools but doubling the gap, where mortals would be just at the base gap, and Dragon-Blooded and Lunars would produce smaller gaps with their dice adding.<br /> <br /> Melee? I'd assume because it's the &quot;balanced&quot; combat Ability that does offense and defense, and is the most flexible for concept where the others have stronger build incentives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anything Bob can do Chad is likely going to do just as well if not better because his base dicepool is better. </div> </div> </div>Duh? Bigger dice pools are better.. we've agreed and stated this repeatedly.<br /> <br /> Also this doesn't explain why either choice was made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Excellent Strike will give a better return, Rising Sun Slash is going to proc a HELL of a lot harder with Chad, when Chad uses Fire and Stones he\u2019s likely to hit and do that bit of additional damage compared to Bob who wastes 5m and gets nothing if he misses (and the chances are against him). </div> </div> </div>These aren't Excellencies, and not Melee specific concerns.<br /> <br /> Also, Bob can't even buy Rising Sun Slash without raising Melee first. If Bob isn't Melee Supernal (though again, concept, why is Bob's concept awesome sword guy if he's not taking the awesome sword guy stuff?), it's not a huge deal to not have Melee 4+ yet for buying a bunch of Charms, but there's all of one Essence 2+ Melee Charm that's Melee 3 or less in requirements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can likely make builds for Bob that will allow him to fight against the Nephwrack better too. </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about stuff that applies to mortals as well, not just throwing Charms on a character to deal with a high end baddie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is going to much, much harder as you need to start from two bases rather than one. </div> </div> </div>So.. why not pull Accuracy out of Attributes completely and have if be like Essence so everyone's always on the same base? That's the only way to ensure one base. Letting people pick Strength or Dexterity doesn't mean they're going to pick 5s in either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That little change is going to affect the system a bit more. </div> </div> </div>Right, so all those words I posted there, about the idea no actually being a good rule to use? You read those, right? Because it's not good for civility to continue to do this ignore the words I posted thing. I don't need you to come up with reasons why the idea I posted is bad.. I said it wasn't good.<br /> <br /> I want you to explain why the fundamental reasoning of making damage from Strength more valuable - despite any level of system changes - isn't actually a better cure for what you're pointing at as something to change in the system. The simpler solution of Attribute swap default isn't inherently the most thorough and complete solution to address Strength focused builds vs. Dexterity focused builds.<br /> <br /> Making Strength more valuable at doing what Strength does so people feel they get value for investing also avoids the trap your idea creates where people might think they can pick between Strength and Dexterity, pick Strength, and then get demolished because being able to attack with Strength is not enough to make Strength Dexterity's equal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You\u2019re trading raw offense for less defense and utility. </div> </div> </div>It seems a pretty bad trade to me. It actually seems a lot of a trap trade to me, because new players are more likely to think Strength 5/Dexterity 1 builds are viable if they see you can swap them at will, and miss how it only applies to attacks and then have a crap character build.<br /> <br /> This reflects something I said to a different poster about an old WoD Revised house rule: the trade was never really worth it. It let Strength be OK for a bit, but you'd end up with Dexterity maxed to get the maximum fighter in the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Grapples need builds based around them specifically so if you want melee they\u2019re out </div> </div> </div>For Ability Exalts. IIRC the devs have said that the Grapple tag on a Melee weapon let you us Melee for your control roll. So for mortals and Attribute Exalts, you can Melee grapple with the appropriate weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Overall you will get a better a better deal with Dexterity. </div> </div> </div>So, again, what's the benefit of making Strength second fiddle Dexterity, instead of making Strength a good deal doing something Dexterity doesn't do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having 6 dice to hit is a bad thing when you literally have a one in ten chance of hitting a target? </div> </div> </div>If you purposefully built a character with a base of 6 dice, isn't the point that you're going to run into low odds as Difficult goes up unless you expend resources?<br /> <br /> My point is that 6 dice to hit should be a struggle to hit without spending resources/help. If that's the character you built that's probably on purpose.<br /> <br /> As the book says, even the Exalted have weakness in the form of low rated Abilities. They're a reminder that whatever you put towards getting into the 8-10 base dice-pool range making you feel powerful, there's stuff you're still not that great at too.<br /> <br /> Going on about how 6 base dice is bad as combat stakes go up is agreeing with me, not disagreeing with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why should Strength copy Dexterity when it comes to attacking with Brawl/Melee? As I said before, <i>to reduce trap options and make it so each player can have an enjoyable time with their build</i> <i>as the envision it</i>. </div> </div> </div>Except it introduces a new trap, and doesn't actually improve Strength to overcome everything you highlighted on why Exalted doesn't make it do enough.. The Dexterity build is still more enjoyable at the overlapping areas, so the Strength focused character isn't actually enacting their vision of their concept, because they're not getting Awesome Strength, they're getting Second Rate Dexterity; and that's not why they wanted Strength focus is it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bob doesn't feel like his he-man fighter should be a ballerina, why should he be forced to pick between being functional or playing the concept he wants? </div> </div> </div>I've thoroughly ripped this argument appart.<br /> <br /> If Bob doesn't want a ballerina, Bob doesn't invest in Performance. The broad abstractions in the Attributes mean you're always going to be good at things at high Attribute ratings that might not be part of your concept. This actually applies to all abstractions. &quot;Bob doesn't feel like his he-man fighter should be skilled with tricky weapons like a whip, but Melee makes him good with one anyway.&quot; &quot;Bob doesn't feel like his he-man boxer should be good with kicks, but Brawl doesn't care about punches vs. kicks.&quot; Abstract traits always means you're buying dots in things that might not be part of your concept; especially if you get too specific with your concept for the level of abstraction in the game.<br /> <br /> This is, ultimately, another false dichotomy. Bob isn't being forced to pick between being functional or player the concept he wants. Just because he has the Dexterity to be a good dancer doesn't mean the player ever has to choose to role-play Bob dancing. Bob can refuse to dancer for whatever reasons desired, and thus plays the concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That\u2019s a good idea. My point is why don\u2019t we go deeper and tackle the root issue with this rather than treating a surface problem. </div> </div> </div>Because the root issue isn't actually significant without the complexity introduced by something like the Lunar Charm paradigm. Lunar Charms aren't treating a surface problem, they're using a design space to differentiate from the other Charm sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T18:08:57-07:00","id":1239858,"title":"","content":"Could I just ask, if everything comes to pass as you would like, Sandact6, and everyone can use whatever attribute they want to do everything, what do the Lunars (and possibly Liminals and Alchemicals) get in return?<br /> <br /> I'm coming out and saying it straight, Exalted is a game of niches and niche protection. Every Exalt type has a thing that is special to them and that they are the best at.<br /> <br /> In my honest view, playing around with Attributes (So that you finally can play that Brute Archetype without depending on Dex all that much) is something that Lunars, Alchemicals and Liminals should get, by fictional conventions (after all, they represent the Werebeast, Giant Robot and Golem/Frankenstein's monster archetypes). So by taking it away and giving it to the Invincible Sword Princesses (Solars) and Old Wise Master Martial Artists (Sidereals) what do the Lunars (and Alchemicals and Liminals) get in return?<br /> <br /> If it is just satisfaction from not being a newbie trap anymore, I'm not sure I agree with taking cool stuff away from my favorite Exalt type and getting satisfaction in return. &gt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> Couldn't reasonable Storytellers just tell new players &quot;Most everyone has to be basically a nimble Wu Xia hero if he wants to hit things the best in combat. Its a convention of the Exalted RPG line. If you want to be the Hulk, you have to choose either Lunars, Alchemicals or Liminals&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T19:39:45-07:00","id":1239878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239858#post1239858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could I just ask, if everything comes to pass as you would like, Sandact6, and everyone can use whatever attribute they want to do everything, what do the Lunars (and possibly Liminals and Alchemicals) get in return?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever attribute they want? I'm advocating for at least letting Strength do double duty to attack and defend primarily. If other splats want to make some minor tweaks like using certain attributes <i>in specific instances</i> then that depends. I can see why people would want to limit it and have no issue with that, but I want first and foremost to be able to use Strength to be able to attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239858#post1239858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm coming out and saying it straight, Exalted is a game of niches and niche protection. Every Exalt type has a thing that is special to them and that they are the best at.</div> </div> </div> </div>I came out straight and said it as well. Using Strength to hit makes some characters more viable and less of a newbie trap and feat tax. I'm not advocating for letting Solars shapeshift.<br /> <br /> You know what was another, really drastic thing back in the day? Giving people reflexives outside of combos in 2e.<br /> <br /> &quot;THAT'S A DRAGONBLOODED NICHE! LET THE DRAGONBLOODED HAVE THE THING UNIQUE TO THEM!&quot;<br /> <br /> Then everyone got reflexives outside of combos, and the game was better for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239858#post1239858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my honest view, playing around with Attributes (So that you finally can play that Brute Archetype without depending on Dex all that much) is something that Lunars, Alchemicals and Liminals should get, by fictional conventions (after all, they represent the Werebeast, Giant Robot and Golem/Frankenstein's monster archetypes). So by taking it away and giving it to the Invincible Sword Princesses (Solars) and Old Wise Master Martial Artists (Sidereals) what do the Lunars (and Alchemicals and Liminals) get in return?</div> </div> </div> </div>A minor sacrifice to make the entire game better.<br /> <br /> Note minor compared to the Dragonblooded. Letting all the Exalts use reflexives at any time was a pretty big change to their metagame. The issue was literally every other's metagame sucked ass, it was nearly unbearable to the point where I was starting to explore alternative systems. It made the game vastly more enjoyable FOR EVERYONE as a whole.<br /> <br /> This change isn't as big as 2.5e was. Not mechanically at the base and isn't nearly big of an issue. Outside of Sail/Craft 3e runs very well and unlike the changes needed for 2e, 3e will continue running fine in most areas. What I'm saying is that this change is a minor one that has been clogging the gears of Exalted for nearly more than a decade. When we hopped over to 3e and took some of the stuff from 2.Xe we managed to take the broken rusted gears that was using dexterity only for attack. The system works, but I'm saying it can run better even if a tiny bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239858#post1239858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is just satisfaction from not being a newbie trap anymore, I'm not sure I agree with taking cool stuff away from my favorite Exalt type and getting satisfaction in return. &gt;_&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you love something critique it. Find out what you love about them but at the same time learn to take a step back and go &quot;What can be learned from this set, narratively and mechanically, and how can it be applied to the game as a whole.&quot; If you see something offense or can be improved for the good of the entire game, even if you really like that then, learn to kill your darlings and cut it out. I do this in my job a lot. I write something that seems to be really good, but I'm constantly forced to look at what I did and how I can make it better. Even if that means altering or changing something I like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239858#post1239858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't reasonable Storytellers just tell new players &quot;Most everyone has to be basically a nimble Wu Xia hero if he wants to hit things the best in combat. Its a convention of the Exalted RPG line. If you want to be the Hulk, you have to choose either Lunars, Alchemicals or Liminals&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>If this was 2e I think you'd have a point. For late 1e and most of 2e things were interpreted as largely based in Wuxia. You see big martial artists in there time to time, but the defacto kings at the ones who believe speed is everything. I disagreed with this in 2e, but you couldn't fix it as the fix was a lot more difficult. Lunar animal forms, monsters with huge strength pools, Gargantuan<br /> mutation, Increasing Strength Exercise, I could go on. I'd need to change a ton of charms from all the splats and books in order to make this so.<br /> <br /> In 3e this is no longer the case. The direction it wants to try to go towards is Conan (Even through I personally like Wuxia more) and that means if you want to make a barbarian warlord who is more focused on strength why shouldn't this be viable? Why do we want to punish new people or tell them &quot;No you cannot have your he-man character. He needs to be a ballerina to be remotely comparable&quot;? If he doesn't want to play as a Lunar, Alchemical, or a Liminal but just a barbarian warlord that's just that damn tough and strong? If he doesn't want to play what he perceives as a furry, Robot, or frankenstein to play up his concept or told to get fucked, why should that happen?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T01:48:51-07:00","id":1239941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This statement is not good for the civility of the discussion. If I say, &quot;I'll get to it later in the post,&quot; don't complain that it's not in the section you're quoting. It's rude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not using it bad faith and I\u2019m not using it to be rude or sarcastic. If you think I missed another point in any post you think is important, then please bring it up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why it remains a preference as you're constructing it, not a flaw that needs errata. There isn't a flaw in the system with PCs being able to get high dice-pools there's just a less broad method of doing so than you'd like, and free Strength/Dexterity switching for close combat attacks doesn't guarantee builds that resolve the planning issues you bring up. A Strength 2/Dexterity 3/Ability 3 character in a group with multiple 5/3 or 3/5 + 5s in their Ability characters remains a planning issue, and actually gets worse because you have more traits contributing to the dice-pool you're planning around to track.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a character that is remotely on par with other players or enemies is a preference?<br /> <br /> Look if a player wants to make a build when everyone else in the group is 5/5? That player is either not wanting combat as his primary focus or the players/ST\u2019s are being dicks to him and not at least giving him a fair warning about the system. Likely Chad knows about Ex3 and how it works. If we\u2019re going by Test 1 and Chad looked at Bob\u2019s sheet and heard he wants to do combat? If he the ST doesn\u2019t bring it up Chad should at least say \u201cUh dude? If you want to get into combat you might want to switch around those Dexterity and Strength scores because [insert dexterity godstat speech here we\u2019ve all heard multiple times before].\u201d He if doesn\u2019t then Chad hasn\u2019t seen his sheet (I think group checks of sheets are a good idea, or at least group chargen) or he\u2019s dicking over Bob.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the examples don't take into account &quot;pick for a group challenge,&quot; at all. Bob, in a group, isn't going to be facing the Nephrwrack (or whatever non-Legendary Size higher end solo enemy) at full Parry/Evasion, because the Chads are going to be going first most of the time, and bringing defense down to levels easier for Bob to handle.<br /> <br /> Something that's going to give a circle of Solars a decent fight doesn't really prove much in a one-on-one fight besides &quot;it has high enough stats to make that a questionable thing to throw at a new character.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Read my post closer and don\u2019t cherry pick. One thing I said in it is that when you design things in an encounter? Plan things out just in case a PC winds up having to face that opponent. Even if this means being solo temporarily. Notice how nearly all the enemies in the game are designed to be taken on by either a group of Bob\u2019s or single Chad if he put optimizes? Exalted can use teamwork, but for nearly any splat you can expect to be the big damn hero if you put investment into it.<br /> <br /> How would you feel if you wanted to make an investment into a specific character type, only to find out that another character just dabbling in it is exponentially better than you at your archtype? It makes you feel unheroic. This would be like Raiden vs Jetstream Sam in Metal Gear Rising. Spending all the time in the game powering up and finally getting to him for your big hyped up duel\u2026 only to have your teeth kicked in hard. Not like a hard fought battle full of tension, but more like the platter Sam gives you when he hands your ass the first time. Sorry bud, looks like you should\u2019ve invested into Dexterity.<br /> <br /> By letting a secondary attribute determine more stuff in a limit fashion, we lessen such things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &gt;But charms are what make the difference!<br /> <br /> If they are the same splat with the same attacking ability, then not by much. Chad can use all the charms Bob but put them to much better use. He\u2019ll get more dice on average with excellent strike, way more on Rising Sun Slash, actually hit with Solar Counterattack, more threshold successes on Hungry Tiger and so on. These charms will let Bob fight against the Nephwrack, but it won\u2019t solve the problem of being an entirely different weight class then Chad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the important part shouldn't be Bob or Chad's other stuff either; including Charms. And considering a Nephwrack can inflict -9 dice to hit it with two Charms that are scene length if you can't counter them (directly or other ways)... that's as important to his defense as Excellencies are to the other's offense. -9 to hit is a huge impact on &quot;how hard a Nephwrack is to hit&quot; even if it isn't expressed in boosted defense (because it's three different -3 penalties that can all be overcome separately).</div> </div> </div> </div>I said I randomly picked the Nephwrack out of the book as a example of something with higher defense. <i>We are not talking about the Nephwrack</i>. My point is if Bob has trouble just bypassing a Nephwreck, what I would regard as the lower part of the middle tier of the enemy difficulty list? Bob is going to be crushed by other things in the middle tier group. Octavian and Fakhara are higher tier examples and there will be more after those. How are you going to feel as a PC if Chad is capable of engaging these things one on one in a heroic duel while you are essentially relegated to support. If you want to fight in such a battle, then chances are you\u2019re going to only hold Chad back in the battle itself because you\u2019re a liability in direct combat.<br /> <br /> You can plan encounters for a group of Bob\u2019s or Chads, but when you mix them together things get real ugly real fast. This is why its important to keep people on the same page. To help keep them on the same page, making another attribute to allow attack would help greatly not only with new players but even Chad when he wants to try out some build variety. After all, Chad\u2019s got a high strength heavy lance ride character idea he\u2019ll want to use to terrorize the ST in the future with.<br /> <br /> The -9 penalty charm is also pointless. <i>It can apply equally to both Chad and Bob</i>. The only difference is Bob gets reamed harder by any penalties while Chad can live through some. Though if you\u2019re at a point in an encounter where you hit a -9 penalty, then something has gone very wrong in that encounter. Assuming it was well designed (Which the Nephwrack ain\u2019t that bad) then the players have taken the stairs down and are now forced to scale a sheer wall to get back up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. But lots of things matter. Onslaught negation matters a ton in planning encounters because something with them forces each PC to deal with its defense more directly, while one's without are easier on a mixed group where the more optimized characters will knock down high DVs, letting the lower dice-pool characters get hits in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it won\u2019t matter. If Bob can use the same charms, Chad will use them better. Bob can slam his defense and spam Dipping Swallow or Bulwark Stance to defend sure, but if Chad can just pop Bulwark Stance and laugh off enemies for the rest of the turn? Especially when Bob will need to slam his motepool for excellencies to both attack AND defend against the enemies Chad has an easy time with? Bob is going to tap out much, much faster.<br /> <br /> &gt;But enemies can have tailored stats!<br /> <br /> As I said before, anything that Bob finds fair Chad will go to sleep at. Anything that Chad finds challenging is going to be next to impossible for Bob. If they use the same charmset and have access to the same charms, anything Bob can do Chad will do better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why &quot;it's just about dice-pools,&quot; really isn't a sufficient logical basis for making this a universal rule: dice-pools aren't the only thing that matters, and such a rule needs to be examined in full context, not just if it has an impact on one aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charms will vary player to player. Allowing players to do different and various things. Base dice pools and defenses for NPC\u2019s are always going to remain.<br /> <br /> Can you reduce the base stats of an enemy to make it a better fit for a player? Absolutely! But some players might take it personally if you nerfed an enemy to make it beatable for them. Its demeaning to some because it feels like the ST is using kid gloves. When Bob asked why such a thing is true? Well Chad has a base numbers advantage and therefore can put his charms to better use than Bob can.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re fixated at the level above. The charms, the magic, the effects. I\u2019m not addressing that. I\u2019m going to a level below, the base layer which I\u2019m demonstrating where a fault is. You can layer over this with the layer above you\u2019re mentioning, but it will not get rid of that fault. It was the exact same thing with paranoia combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if you insist on dice-pools being the sole metric. You're artificially forcing Bob to measure up to Chad, by forcing Bob to fight like Chad, instead of the two fighting smart together and playing to each other's strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re fixated on the layer above. That\u2019s not where the base problem lies. You cannot fix it there. You can mask it there, but you cannot fix it. Dice pools and difficulties are a base mechanic of the system. They\u2019re a foundation that everything else operates on. If that skeleton isn\u2019t foundation isn\u2019t solid then the whole thing shakes apart.<br /> <br /> There also isn\u2019t any \u201cfighting together to cover each\u2019s other strengths\u201d. I\u2019ve said it time and time again, anything Bob can potentially do Chad can do much better. This is because Chad doesn\u2019t need Bob to cover his weaknesses, because to Chad Bob is just a liability. No player wants to be that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all the talk about expanding options, it's still keeping Accuracy as all that matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and by having Strength as a different method of calculating attack Bob would have a much better accuracy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though if we were talking about something like the Distract Gambit allowing different hit dice-pools? You'd sell me easily on that. Because &quot;I threaten the enemy to distract them,&quot; relying on hitting with Dexterity + Ability first is strange as a specific rule since it means your ability to be threatening doesn't actually matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go ahead and do so. I won\u2019t be covering that as it\u2019s a tangent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, which is why I said making the examples Solars distracts from the core of your argument. Things should be evident at mortal levels, not when you start getting into Solar Charms. You're skipping showing that things are &quot;messed up&quot; on that level when you jump right into Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are Solar dice caps calculated? Answer: But their base mortal stats. They can double what a mortal can of their own dice pool. I showed in the math how important these gaps can be and why this is important. Chad\u2019s blow further ahead and Bob\u2019s are left in the dust. Its because they\u2019re evident at mortal levels it only becomes more pronounced at the Exalted level. <i>Especially </i>when using charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Bob can close the gap, eliminate it, and even overcome that advantage with the tools in the system as it stands. Bob doesn't <b>need </b>your proposed rule to do so. You've simply set the terms of the example to deny those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strawman. That isn\u2019t the point I was making at all. My point for this was mentioned in the last reply above this: If things are bad at mortal they\u2019ll only become more pronounced at the Exalted level. This is because this is the base of the system. A bedrock.<br /> <br /> Sure Bob can use tools (charms) to overcome the soldier. Chad doesn\u2019t need any help to beat the soldier and can likely win using base stats alone. Do you not see a problem with this? At all?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Bob can close the gap without your house rule, where is the objective flaw in the system that it addresses?</div> </div> </div> </div>I answered this in the post where I used the math.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chad does more damage on average by hitting more frequently. The math on the thresholds leave Bob with the edge on average post-soak damage per hit. Not by much, but those are the numbers presented. That's even backed up by your link. Chard's +2 damage from thresholds is less than Bobs +3 higher base damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let\u2019s assume Chad and Bob a defense 7 enemy both using the same weapon. Since the weapon is the same we\u2019ll just ignore it and focus on threshold and strength. Both attack ten times.<br /> <br /> Chad has an 86% chance of hitting. Let\u2019s assume that means he hits 8/10 times. A threshold of 2.21 means that 17.68 damage overall is being added from threshold, let\u2019s round up for a solid 18. Add this into a Strength of 2 hitting 8 times is 16. Chad has 34 extra damage from all attacks.<br /> <br /> Bob\u2019s chance of hitting is 58.01%. Like Chad we\u2019re going to lop off all numbers than the front and assume 5/10 hit. Average threshold is 3.75, so 4. Hitting 5 times at Strength 5 means he\u2019s landing 25 extra damage. 29 damage overall extra.<br /> <br /> The only way Bob is breaking even with Chad is hope he hits 6/10 times. Chad is hitting more often that and that makes all the different. If we did not count threshold successes then Bob wins easily, but that\u2019s not how the system works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is saying otherwise. We're saying we don't need another default avenue of improving them. Bob with Melee 5 and a specialty closes the gap with Chad to 1 without needing to use Strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Purchasing the other two ability dots does make things mathematically closer yes, but it still doesn\u2019t stop Bob not wanting his character to be a ballerina. Why should his character need to do such a thing in the first place?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also<br /> <br /> &gt;Specialty<br /> <br /> No. Notice how Chad doesn\u2019t have one either? He can do the same thing get another dice added. If you\u2019re going to give things to Bob that Chad cannot access then the point of the experiment is moot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I can tell, the base math isn't fucked. The Bob and Chad examples are working entirely as the game says they should as much as can be assessed in constrained white-room examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the game is working by essentially kicking Bob\u2019s player in the nuts for daring not to be a Ballerina instead of his he-man concept.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you send Chad to deal with a zombie battle group instead of Bob? What does cleaning silks have to do with any of this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does any PC need to break off a fight to attend to something else? I dunno. Point I was making is that unexpected things happen and Bob can be suddenly left with dealing with the Nephwrack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, of course, Chad faces the Nephwrack alone, and gets killed, because his ability to hit isn't enough to actually win (or gets removed because he's smacked with -9 to hit, a Defense penalty, and can't move to get away from the aura of doom).</div> </div> </div> </div>Addressed previously.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On two 1-5 range choices, Bob was built in the middle for both. That does not communicate (with the character creation resources in this game) a concept built to be a top tier fighter. If my players want to smash mortals with ease and spar with top tier NPCs from the book, they're taking at least 5 in their combat Ability to communicate that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keyword: Your players. Without anyone to guide them new people may not think like that. I can open Scroll of Exalts and see Karal has a Melee stat of 3. In caste book she took on a Raksha raiding party. What does this communicate to a new player. \u201cOh OK, so 3 must mean you\u2019re good enough with the sword to match a retired army commander. That should be good!\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>Hell not even War, the ability that was likely emphasized the most in her story, is not at rating 5!</i><br /> <br /> This was upgraded to 4 in Tomb of Dreams, so hell we at least have a point there. Still several behind but baby steps.<br /> <br /> There are two statting methods. Book methods and optimizer method. One is Bob and the other is Chad, guess which one is which. How is something presented to someone <i>brand new</i> and how it actually is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're presenting a false dichotomy where &quot;wants to fight&quot; is a binary state of, &quot;wants to fight at the highest levels and thus needs the best dice pools,&quot; or &quot;doesn't want to fight&quot; and skipping everyone that wants to make a combat secondary style character that can hold their own in minor fights, and is there to largely help the combat primary characters... who don't need to max their pools to accomplish that play goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>No my dichotomy here is \u201cbeing relevant in combat\u201d and \u201cthe most you\u2019re going to do is apply onslaught so Chad can hit better\u201d camps. Things that Chad will find challenging will be nearly impossible for Bob. Do you not recognize that?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bob is built like a combat secondary, and your examples show that he performs as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said the characters are made to a style common I see pre-gens and newbies falling into such traps. The character may be a Zenith and have a shitton of social for roaring speeches or some Athletics to play up his strong man concept, but in terms combat? He may think he has it covered. After all, they\u2019re comparable to the pregens!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chad's designed better for combat... and clearly so in a fashion that does not require system mastery to notice. If Bob's player needs to be told Bob is second fiddle to Chad in combat... the problem is not the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, I heard literally the <i>exact</i> same thing when Immanent Solar Glory was a thing granting +50 motes in 2e. It was changed because Conan players didn\u2019t want to become librarians in order to be relevant at all in the game.<br /> <br /> Why does Bob need his he-man to become a ballerina in order to become relevant? Do you understand why Immanent Solar Glory was made available to all Solar castes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's the trap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Answered in thread previously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bob didn't take Melee 5 and a specialty by choice, not because the system tricked him into thinking this wasn't a good idea. Hell, if Bob wants to invest heavily in Solar Melee, his player is going to look at the Charms and see that he'll need Melee 4 and 5 very quickly to actually buy them.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK first, I purposefully left out the specialties. As I said before, both Bob and Chad could\u2019ve taken them. The point made overall would still be the same.<br /> <br /> Bob will eventually grab more melee yes, that much is a fact. There is the issue of being dunked on or making you feel irrelevant when Chad is in the area. A Nephwrack could also be a solid early game opponent for most players. Not first session perhaps be certainly first story. Bob is going to sure as hell going to get more Melee after that encounter. Then feel foolish for making such a mistake, then groan as he\u2019s forced to buy dexterity if he wants to be really good in combat. Wasting XP that could\u2019ve gone towards those shiny evocations where Chad can just buy them if he wants because he did chargen right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a trap.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Orange painted red is still an Orange. It does not become an Apple, no matter how much you want it to be so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book reinforces on multiple fronts that you should take advantage of the relatively cheap starting Abilities to get your main ones into the 4 or 5 range. This literally involves ignoring the book saying &quot;Think Larger Than Life,&quot; and things like the book saying to invest in your Caste/Favored Abilities at creation with bonus points over most other options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people I know when starting new games look up other characters or pregens as reference samples. Its entirely possible they may get conflicting signals. Secondly players are players. I could potentially hold up a giant neon sign at times and they might be liable to miss it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this a goal post shift? Are you saying your rule isn't being put in place to make Strength focused combat characters more fun to play? That seems to be very much what you've said about this so far. So I'm confused now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because as I said before, you\u2019re mistaking something on the upper layer (equipment) for the lower one (basic resolution). This does not solve a problem, it masks it. Chad can get a light sword as well. Hell I can give them both heavy weapons and the test and the principle behind it would still be the same, which in that case leap directly to decisive attack results.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And your math shows that Bob can hit, even if less reliably than Chad, so damage could start to matter if the system encouraged it to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve already shown Chad is going to hit more often, and therefore for more damage on average.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hyperbole isn't helping on the civility front.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I am using it quite literally. With the way 3e works, you want the 100 one damage attacks. Even if I was generous and let there be two out of every 100 100-damage attacks hit, you\u2019re still counting on luck when the first will hit and when the second will land with a decisive. In the meantime someone can peck away like a woodpecker. By the time you land the second hit for a decisive? You might not have enough initiative to actually KO the target anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I think the game would be better for making Strength focused combatants fun if there was more parity between the Initiative gains done between with less frequent hits with lots of damage and more frequent hits with lower damage? YES.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think it's actually what most people want out of a higher end Bob style build. They want a character that doesn't always hit, but makes up for it with big damage when they do. I don't think most people want Strength and Dexterity to overlap more in practice, and they want a Strength focused build to do it's own thing that's viable and different from a Dexterity focused build. IME people don't want Accuracy 1 with X other stuff, and Accuracy 2 with Y other stuff out of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one wants a character they cannot reliably hit with unless that hit is an OHKO or near it. To get what you want you\u2019re going to have to change some things with the system.<br /> <br /> And most people? You don\u2019t that just as I apparently don\u2019t know that. Just like you\u2019re claiming I\u2019m doing, you\u2019re pushing your own viewpoints as a world fact. The sheer principle that there are other people in this thread aside from you and I on both sides of the argument show that there are people invested on both sides of this.<br /> <br /> Secondly a weapons argument, I am not getting into this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I can bring their averages closer without it, not dilute the differences between Strength and Dexterity (which is different from wanting to make Dexterity less god-stat), and not deal with previously mentioned issues with Charm structures being based on these traits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool. Let\u2019s see it. You demanded proof from me and I showed it. If you want me to buy into this statement at all, back it up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You included weapon accuracy in your examples so.. no strawman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used accuracy to represent a point. You can use it to cover for withering to a certain extent, but when the moment comes to end a fight? You\u2019re on lady luck\u2019s side. A situation a lot swingier than other games. Secondly it was to show base mechanics, an underlying problem at the root of the game, one that effects everything from it onwards.<br /> <br /> So no, it wasn\u2019t a strawman. It was relevant to the entire core of my conversation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Solar Excellencies create the largest effective gap between base dice-pools but doubling the gap, where mortals would be just at the base gap, and Dragon-Blooded and Lunars would produce smaller gaps with their dice adding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars still have one major issue of if your attack accuracy is low enough to the point where you need to blow a potential +5 extra motes just to remotely keep up with other players before they\u2019re using heavy magic? You\u2019re fucked.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded don\u2019t have this as much, this is true. The ability scores \u2018merely\u2019 double. They won\u2019t feel the dice gap difference for most things in the game, but if they\u2019re in mixed circle they might want that gap closes because of how Celestials we\u2019ve seen so far have higher dice maximums.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Melee? I'd assume because it's the &quot;balanced&quot; combat Ability that does offense and defense, and is the most flexible for concept where the others have stronger build incentives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong.<br /> <br /> I could\u2019ve chosen Brawl and it wouldn\u2019t have mattered. Even if we entered a bizzaro world where using Strength for accuracy on Archery/Thrown then it still wouldn\u2019t matter. The entire point was <i>addressing base dice pools and why they are important</i>. If the character use the same base dice pools and same abilities, then charms are not as much of a factor as both characters could potentially get them and the one with higher values is highly probable to use them far more efficiently.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Bob can't even buy Rising Sun Slash without raising Melee first. If Bob isn't Melee Supernal (though again, concept, why is Bob's concept awesome sword guy if he's not taking the awesome sword guy stuff?), it's not a huge deal to not have Melee 4+ yet for buying a bunch of Charms, but there's all of one Essence 2+ Melee Charm that's Melee 3 or less in requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re cherry picking.<br /> <br /> Assume that Bob can use that charm, he\u2019s still going to be inferior to Chad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about stuff that applies to mortals as well, not just throwing Charms on a character to deal with a high end baddie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals are going to handle things completely differently. If both Bob and Chad are mortals and their boss is a Nephwrack? Unless a miracle happens Bob is going to be the person that provides onslaught support. A one in ten chance of hitting only makes him a liability. That problem will always remain for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.. why not pull Accuracy out of Attributes completely and have if be like Essence so everyone's always on the same base? That's the only way to ensure one base. Letting people pick Strength or Dexterity doesn't mean they're going to pick 5s in either.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have a character in DnD 4e who doesn\u2019t invest deeply into his class\u2019s primary and secondary attributes. If they don\u2019t contribute to combat then don\u2019t be surprised why.<br /> <br /> Again, if we can give players more choice why is this a bad thing? If it means a safety net which doesn\u2019t have that much impact on the game as a whole mechanically outside of improvements, why not implement it? If it\u2019s something we\u2019re going to be charged a feat tax for when it should be free, why are we getting feat taxes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want you to explain why the fundamental reasoning of making damage from Strength more valuable - despite any level of system changes - isn't actually a better cure for what you're pointing at as something to change in the system. The simpler solution of Attribute swap default isn't inherently the most thorough and complete solution to address Strength focused builds vs. Dexterity focused builds.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s a rule called KISS. It means \u201cKeep It Short and Sweet\u201d, it goes along with Occam\u2019s Razor (The best solution is usually the simplest one). After applying things such as the \u201cUse Strength as an APP bonus difference (-1 parry for every point of strength between targets, maximum -3)\u201d and others I\u2019ve forgotten over the ages, this is the shortest and easiest method I\u2019ve found that, by pure chance, also comes with the least wide sweeping chances to the system. I don\u2019t need to alter damage formulas, weapons, many charms, or anything like that at all.<br /> <br /> It may not be the most thorough and complete compared to others yes, but I\u2019m had pressed to find something simpler. You don\u2019t want base systems to be too complex\u2026 Unless you\u2019re Anima: Beyond Fantasy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making Strength more valuable at doing what Strength does so people feel they get value for investing also avoids the trap your idea creates where people might think they can pick between Strength and Dexterity, pick Strength, and then get demolished because being able to attack with Strength is not enough to make Strength Dexterity's equal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then go ahead and make such a thing. I fully encourage all homebrew.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems a pretty bad trade to me. It actually seems a lot of a trap trade to me, because new players are more likely to think Strength 5/Dexterity 1 builds are viable if they see you can swap them at will, and miss how it only applies to attacks and then have a crap character build.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know what the difference is the system RAW and my changes? Mine actually allows those high strength people to be scary in combat rather than punching bags. It\u2019s a lopsided trade as Dexterity still outweighs you. Only difference now is that when putting things on the feasibility scale? Dexterity doesn\u2019t weigh so much that it makes the Strength weight fly off the scale and into the ceiling.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reflects something I said to a different poster about an old WoD Revised house rule: the trade was never really worth it. It let Strength be OK for a bit, but you'd end up with Dexterity maxed to get the maximum fighter in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not know as I know nothing about WoD or its mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Ability Exalts. IIRC the devs have said that the Grapple tag on a Melee weapon let you us Melee for your control roll. So for mortals and Attribute Exalts, you can Melee grapple with the appropriate weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat. It still doesn\u2019t meant that you can use that STR to hit brawl charm for grappling on Melee weapon. If it does, it means that you can either go grappling or suck.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, again, what's the benefit of making Strength second fiddle Dexterity, instead of making Strength a good deal doing something Dexterity doesn't do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Strength becomes more viable, and like your requested earlier it does more damage. See that math example I did involving threshold successes? Imagine not only getting +15 additional damage on all rolls but those juicy threshold successes that Exalted loves so much? This actually solves one of your issues about Strength doing more when it hits: Hit by more threshold successes with a higher base damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you purposefully built a character with a base of 6 dice, isn't the point that you're going to run into low odds as Difficult goes up unless you expend resources?<br /> <br /> My point is that 6 dice to hit should be a struggle to hit without spending resources/help. If that's the character you built that's probably on purpose.<br /> <br /> As the book says, even the Exalted have weakness in the form of low rated Abilities. They're a reminder that whatever you put towards getting into the 8-10 base dice-pool range making you feel powerful, there's stuff you're still not that great at too.<br /> <br /> Going on about how 6 base dice is bad as combat stakes go up is agreeing with me, not disagreeing with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I\u2019ve seen builds which have done this accidently. They\u2019re done by newbies who don\u2019t know how the system works when put into actual practice. It\u2019s called newbie hazing, this is especially true when it comes to accuracy calculations. Plus Bob did have 8 dice in accuracy after weapon bonuses. He followed the book, that should be fine after all right?<br /> <br /> Well math says no.<br /> <br /> So if Bob has his higher strength, why not put that to better use?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it introduces a new trap, and doesn't actually improve Strength to overcome everything you highlighted on why Exalted doesn't make it do enough.. The Dexterity build is still more enjoyable at the overlapping areas, so the Strength focused character isn't actually enacting their vision of their concept, because they're not getting Awesome Strength, they're getting Second Rate Dexterity; and that's not why they wanted Strength focus is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are always going to be some imbalances amongst the attribute spread. Hell outside of Investigation, Awareness, and sometimes Occult perception is pretty lonely over there.<br /> <br /> Secondly no, this isn\u2019t near the trap it currently is. Strength in this case may still be suboptimal to Dexterity but at least <i>it actually has a chance</i>. Do you want to give people a chance or tell them to get fucked and put on the ballerina shoes?<br /> <br /> Secondly they are getting awesome strength. They can hit well, they can hit a bit harder than the Dex monkey, and if they use Athletics (Which most people playing he-men archtypes do) then he\u2019ll cut houses to pieces if they stand in his way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Bob doesn't want a ballerina, Bob doesn't invest in Performance. The broad abstractions in the Attributes mean you're always going to be good at things at high Attribute ratings that might not be part of your concept. This actually applies to all abstractions. &quot;Bob doesn't feel like his he-man fighter should be skilled with tricky weapons like a whip, but Melee makes him good with one anyway.&quot; &quot;Bob doesn't feel like his he-man boxer should be good with kicks, but Brawl doesn't care about punches vs. kicks.&quot; Abstract traits always means you're buying dots in things that might not be part of your concept; especially if you get too specific with your concept for the level of abstraction in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re bringing up the differences of <i>adding</i> functionality to a player versus <i>removing</i> functionality. You ripped apart a strawman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, ultimately, another false dichotomy. Bob isn't being forced to pick between being functional or player the concept he wants. Just because he has the Dexterity to be a good dancer doesn't mean the player ever has to choose to role-play Bob dancing. Bob can refuse to dancer for whatever reasons desired, and thus plays the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are entirely missing the central point I was trying to address. <i>Why is Bob forced to take Dexterity solely for his accuracy over Strength?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239847#post1239847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the root issue isn't actually significant without the complexity introduced by something like the Lunar Charm paradigm. Lunar Charms aren't treating a surface problem, they're using a design space to differentiate from the other Charm sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re doing this to basically diversify what dice pool maximums can be so in combat it can be STR/DEX+ATTRIBUTE rather than DEX+ATTRIBUTE. If this is the case why are we paying a feat tax for this \u2018luxury\u2019? Why don\u2019t we bring it to everything so we can see a little bit more diversity in builds instead of ballerinas everywhere?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T02:07:58-07:00","id":1239946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239878#post1239878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whatever attribute they want? I'm advocating for at least letting Strength do double duty to attack and defend primarily. If other splats want to make some minor tweaks like using certain attributes <i>in specific instances</i> then that depends. I can see why people would want to limit it and have no issue with that, but I want first and foremost to be able to use Strength to be able to attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, apologies for min-interpreting. Could I ask what breaks in Exalted play if you tell the bright eyed newbie that if they want to play a High Strength Character, (once the book is out with the Charm of course) that the most efficient way to do it is to play the very cool Exalt type: The Lunars (or later Alchemicals/Liminals to taste)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I came out straight and said it as well. Using Strength to hit makes some characters more viable and less of a newbie trap and feat tax. I'm not advocating for letting Solars shapeshift.<br /> <br /> You know what was another, really drastic thing back in the day? Giving people reflexives outside of combos in 2e.<br /> <br /> &quot;THAT'S A DRAGONBLOODED NICHE! LET THE DRAGONBLOODED HAVE THE THING UNIQUE TO THEM!&quot;<br /> <br /> Then everyone got reflexives outside of combos, and the game was better for it. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Dragonblooded got new special stuff, didn't they? They are basically the Exalted with the most points to spend during character creation for merits, bar none. Their Auras got buffed up in combat and they got a suite of Martial Arts that key off their aura and thus work best for them.<br /> <br /> Now mind, I'm not saying this puts them on par with any Celestial, because that would be nonsense. But it is not right to say that they just gave it up and everything was meadows and bunnies and sunshine.<br /> <br /> So I ask again, what cool new thing do you propose for Lunars to make up for them giving up this. Or you can just say &quot;Acceptable Losses&quot; as well, and I will understand then where you are coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A minor sacrifice to make the entire game better.<br /> <br /> Note minor compared to the Dragonblooded. Letting all the Exalts use reflexives at any time was a pretty big change to their metagame. The issue was literally every other's metagame sucked ass, it was nearly unbearable to the point where I was starting to explore alternative systems. It made the game vastly more enjoyable FOR EVERYONE as a whole.<br /> <br /> This change isn't as big as 2.5e was. Not mechanically at the base and isn't nearly big of an issue. Outside of Sail/Craft 3e runs very well and unlike the changes needed for 2e, 3e will continue running fine in most areas. What I'm saying is that this change is a minor one that has been clogging the gears of Exalted for nearly more than a decade. When we hopped over to 3e and took some of the stuff from 2.Xe we managed to take the broken rusted gears that was using dexterity only for attack. The system works, but I'm saying it can run better even if a tiny bit. </div> </div> </div>Ah, that answers my previous question then. &quot;Acceptable Losses&quot;, fair enough, I know where I stand with you on this discussion, Sandact6. No compromise necessary.<br /> <br /> For your other points, please see my previous reply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you love something critique it. Find out what you love about them but at the same time learn to take a step back and go &quot;What can be learned from this set, narratively and mechanically, and how can it be applied to the game as a whole.&quot; If you see something offense or can be improved for the good of the entire game, even if you really like that then, learn to kill your darlings and cut it out. I do this in my job a lot. I write something that seems to be really good, but I'm constantly forced to look at what I did and how I can make it better. Even if that means altering or changing something I like. </div> </div> </div>Sure... but in the same vein, I'm sure you've considered the failings of your proposal and the many people that don't agree with it. Ranging from my (admittedly pedestrian) protest on grounds of niche protection for Exalts to more mathematical arguments?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this was 2e I think you'd have a point. For late 1e and most of 2e things were interpreted as largely based in Wuxia. You see big martial artists in there time to time, but the defacto kings at the ones who believe speed is everything. I disagreed with this in 2e, but you couldn't fix it as the fix was a lot more difficult. Lunar animal forms, monsters with huge strength pools, Gargantuan<br /> mutation, Increasing Strength Exercise, I could go on. I'd need to change a ton of charms from all the splats and books in order to make this so.<br /> <br /> In 3e this is no longer the case. The direction it wants to try to go towards is Conan (Even through I personally like Wuxia more) and that means if you want to make a barbarian warlord who is more focused on strength why shouldn't this be viable? Why do we want to punish new people or tell them &quot;No you cannot have your he-man character. He needs to be a ballerina to be remotely comparable&quot;? If he doesn't want to play as a Lunar, Alchemical, or a Liminal but just a barbarian warlord that's just that damn tough and strong? If he doesn't want to play what he perceives as a furry, Robot, or frankenstein to play up his concept or told to get fucked, why should that happen? </div> </div> </div>Okay two points here:<br /> <br /> 1. I'm Chinese, and I've read Wu Xia in the original Chinese. Its nice to represent sometimes, cultural pride and all that.<br /> <br /> Exalted 3e, by my admittedly non-expert opinion is one of the most Wu Xia setting out there. Bar none. Legends of Wu Lin... possibly out Wu Xia-s it but nothing else, not even Qin comes close (because admittedly of Supernatural Martial Arts and Competing Schools and Sage Immortal Teachers and re-incarnating lovers and what not).<br /> <br /> So the fact that all characters have to be ballerinas if they want to hit things good, is very baked into the setting. Sure there is some Conan too, but Conan had at least a 4 dex so that he could sword things to death all the time.<br /> <br /> 2. So yes, if you are a responsible Storyteller, who is conversant with the system, you will tell your bright eyed new players that even Barbarian Overlords need that Dex to be competitive.<br /> <br /> Unless... you are one of these super special Other Exalt types that can play full Str and Sta, ignore Dex and just Hulk out all the time (even moreso with DBT).<br /> <br /> See, I think the reason we aren't able to come to a consensus here is that I see absolutely no problem with that. You think (welcome corrections, btw) that this is a fatal flaw (ish) in the system.<br /> <br /> But I guess the correct thing to say here is: I respect your point of view, even if I don't agree with it, and we shall agree to disagree then.<br /> <br /> After all, you might end up being right and I might end up eating crow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T03:00:13-07:00","id":1239959,"title":"","content":"Sandact, I really don't know how you expect people to <i>not </i>cherry pick your posts when they're <i>three fucking miles long.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T08:35:49-07:00","id":1240058,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1183_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1183\" data-vbnamecard=\"1183\">Sandact6</a> I really don't know why you're still bothering. It seems pretty freaking obvious that the opposition isn't engaging in good faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:10:43-07:00","id":1240078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239959#post1239959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sandact, I really don't know how you expect people to <i>not </i>cherry pick your posts when they're <i>three fucking miles long.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It was only 18 pages or so when I typed it up.<br /> <br /> Only.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1240058#post1240058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1183_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1183\" data-vbnamecard=\"1183\">Sandact6</a> I really don't know why you're still bothering. It seems pretty freaking obvious that the opposition isn't engaging in good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not wanting to make the mistakes of the past pretty much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:31:44-07:00","id":1240092,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1183_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1183\" data-vbnamecard=\"1183\">Sandact6</a> I'm not going to lie, I haven't really been following your posts. I've been debating a different point of contention. So my question is, how are you preventing Strength becoming the new god stat? As I see it, Dex provides bonuses to attack, defense, and moderate boosts to damage via extra successes on the attack roll. Subbing Str for Dex, means Str provides bonuses to attack, defense, and a substantial bonus to damage. Someone with a 5 Str, is already adding 5 dice to their withering damage pool. Your proposal has them now adding extra successes from that same stat. In essence, you're turning Str into a god stat greater then Dex ever was. This seems like the opposite of a fix to me. I assume you've already noticed this, so what's your fix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T11:26:20-07:00","id":1240147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239946#post1239946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, apologies for min-interpreting. Could I ask what breaks in Exalted play if you tell the bright eyed newbie that if they want to play a High Strength Character, (once the book is out with the Charm of course) that the most efficient way to do it is to play the very cool Exalt type: The Lunars (or later Alchemicals/Liminals to taste)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve shown how nothing mechanically breaks, so I won\u2019t go over that.<br /> <br /> But the most basic reason? What if a person doesn\u2019t want to play as a Lunar or cannot play as a Lunar?<br /> <br /> Theme wise you could say a person wants nothing to do with the silver pact or animals in his character? He was sold on the idea of Solars being peerless paragons of man and being the table rasa character? Solars offer the most freedom of any splat with the least downside, have been since 1e. You can make your character pretty much how you want and their powers are not far out there for newbies, good for being a gateway drug into the series as a whole. Lunars and Sidereals cannot do this as easily. Dragonblooded can but lose out on those merit dots (meaning it works for an all lost egg, not so much if you run a mixed one between Realm and lost eggs).<br /> <br /> But let\u2019s flip this? What if you\u2019re a Dragonblooded or a Sidereal? Big tough Martial Arts masters are a trope of wuxia, if not officially then throughout culture. Earth Dragon is a prime example of this. Many other martial arts are an example of this. As I said, a Dragonblooded won\u2019t feel it as much and Sidereals won\u2019t either (Let\u2019s assume their excellency from the QC stats what they\u2019ll get), but they\u2019re still going to feel it. As I mathematically shown if you get newbie hazed at that level and need to spend resources in order to catch up? You\u2019d feel like a sucker. You don\u2019t feel like a big damn prince of the earth if a medium soldier is going to force you to spend resources just to hit him. If that situation comes to past I can make characters in Fantasycraft, a good d20 knockoff, that make you feel far more heroic when you\u2019re a level 1 character as a mortal! Exalted is a game about demigods! Let people feel like they\u2019re powerful not only for the premise of Exalted, but powerful as a character! Loss of control should only really come from horror games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239946#post1239946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but Dragonblooded got new special stuff, didn't they? They are basically the Exalted with the most points to spend during character creation for merits, bar none. Their Auras got buffed up in combat and they got a suite of Martial Arts that key off their aura and thus work best for them.<br /> <br /> Now mind, I'm not saying this puts them on par with any Celestial, because that would be nonsense. But it is not right to say that they just gave it up and everything was meadows and bunnies and sunshine.<br /> <br /> So I ask again, what cool new thing do you propose for Lunars to make up for them giving up this. Or you can just say &quot;Acceptable Losses&quot; as well, and I will understand then where you are coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2.5e made the game more bearable. If 2e was a crack house then 2.5e made you go \u201cOh\u2026 They cleaned the house, painted, and put a new roof on it. The interior is still falling apart but now we can at least stay in this place without being worried that a stiff breeze could blow it over at any time!\u201d<br /> <br /> I mean you\u2019re still in a crack house, but at least it was far more bearable that it was in the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239946#post1239946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure... but in the same vein, I'm sure you've considered the failings of your proposal and the many people that don't agree with it. Ranging from my (admittedly pedestrian) protest on grounds of niche protection for Exalts to more mathematical arguments?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is an appeal to emotion, not an argument.<br /> <br /> I have demonstrated how, mathematically, it becomes less of a newbie trap with common newbie builds. There are people in this thread who feel the same way I do. The argument \u201cIt makes you feel bad\u201d applies to both sides of the spectrum. There will be people upset that it happens and people upset that it has happened.<br /> <br /> That is called Politics. When you get into it, it\u2019s the art of pissing off the least amount of people when making choices.<br /> <br /> If you want to say that you feel this should not be the case after my arguments, mathematical and theory crafting, are not right? Cool, that\u2019s for you to decide. If you want to try and refute them on grounds existing only of, \u201cIt makes Lunar fans feel bad\u201d then you\u2019re going to need to find something more substantial.<br /> <br /> DB fans felt worse after 2.5e hit, the salt mines expanded several kilometers that day. Everyone else on the other hand was estatic. It was not changed around because DB players felt bad. Essence ping was not reversed because Adorjan Infernals got a massive debuff and felt bad. It made the entire game objective better for everyone else based on changes to the underlying game and up. Exactly what I seek to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Let me add another thing. Vance has said that for the upcoming Lunar\u2019s book? It could literally the best written book in all of Exalted period, solid in fluff and mechanics. A subsection of the Lunars community would still complain over it. Hell, I\u2019m willing to bet that we\u2019re still going to see more than a few examples of Silver Solar charms in the Lunar charmset as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239946#post1239946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay two points here:<br /> <br /> 1. I'm Chinese, and I've read Wu Xia in the original Chinese. Its nice to represent sometimes, cultural pride and all that.<br /> <br /> Exalted 3e, by my admittedly non-expert opinion is one of the most Wu Xia setting out there. Bar none. Legends of Wu Lin... possibly out Wu Xia-s it but nothing else, not even Qin comes close (because admittedly of Supernatural Martial Arts and Competing Schools and Sage Immortal Teachers and re-incarnating lovers and what not).<br /> <br /> So the fact that all characters have to be ballerinas if they want to hit things good, is very baked into the setting. Sure there is some Conan too, but Conan had at least a 4 dex so that he could sword things to death all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my previous example about all wuxia tropes and how they\u2019re publicly presented. Master Ping in fluff is a feared Iron Mountain stylist whose tetsubo is said to crack the earth in two. He\u2019s not fast but holy shit is he ever big and strong. This falls apart mechanically as likely Master Ping will never hit anyone with how bad his Dex is even if his power is enough to crash you in a single hit with ease.<br /> <br /> Why should we universally screw over these characters? Why are they forced to take Dexterity to live out their character concept? If a charm exists, why are we charging something that people should get for free?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239946#post1239946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. So yes, if you are a responsible Storyteller, who is conversant with the system, you will tell your bright eyed new players that even Barbarian Overlords need that Dex to be competitive.<br /> <br /> Unless... you are one of these super special Other Exalt types that can play full Str and Sta, ignore Dex and just Hulk out all the time (even moreso with DBT).<br /> <br /> See, I think the reason we aren't able to come to a consensus here is that I see absolutely no problem with that. You think (welcome corrections, btw) that this is a fatal flaw (ish) in the system.<br /> <br /> But I guess the correct thing to say here is: I respect your point of view, even if I don't agree with it, and we shall agree to disagree then.<br /> <br /> After all, you might end up being right and I might end up eating crow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, why should you be forced to take Dexterity to remain remotely competitive? I\u2019m not against using single stats for things, hell in Infinity RPG you use Strength for Melee attacks and Perception for ranged. You want to swap between the two? Sorry son, get dunked on.<br /> <br /> But the important thing? There are two different builds you can make. There is some variety between them. You can tell the difference between a Melee user and a ranged user. This is unlike Exalted where you\u2019re told to get Dexterity regardless of your concept or get fucked. Why should you need to be a special exalt type to do something virtually every RPG does for the better?<br /> <br /> And a correction: I do not think this is a fatal flaw. Far, far, FAR from it. A fatal flaw is something like 2.0e before errata, a fatal flaw is something like bloated STR values that prevents widespread execution of a mechanic and require a lot of work to fix. Right now this is a relatively simple, but positive fix.<br /> <br /> And yes, if you don\u2019t want to continue we\u2019ll agree to disagree and move on.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T11:41:34-07:00","id":1240155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1240092#post1240092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1183_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1183\" data-vbnamecard=\"1183\">Sandact6</a> I'm not going to lie, I haven't really been following your posts. I've been debating a different point of contention. So my question is, how are you preventing Strength becoming the new god stat? As I see it, Dex provides bonuses to attack, defense, and moderate boosts to damage via extra successes on the attack roll. Subbing Str for Dex, means Str provides bonuses to attack, defense, and a substantial bonus to damage. Someone with a 5 Str, is already adding 5 dice to their withering damage pool. Your proposal has them now adding extra successes from that same stat. In essence, you're turning Str into a god stat greater then Dex ever was. This seems like the opposite of a fix to me. I assume you've already noticed this, so what's your fix?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have addressed this, so I'll give a summary.<br /> <br /> Even if we did use these rules, Dexterity still gives bonuses to Accuracy (all weapons), defense (Parry and Dodge), all movement (Disengage, rush, and overcoming difficult terrain), threshold successes on attacks and Stealth.<br /> <br /> Strength would give Accuracy, Defense (Or make it stamina, I think it shouldn't be split and stamina parry should be a Lunar thing, but tangent), threshold successes on attacks, higher base damage and feats of strength.<br /> <br /> Now see that higher base damage? We can cut that right now. All Exalted get some pretty fancy damage boosting charms that even the difference between 4 raw damage (STR 1 to STR 5) pretty negligible. This is why I was advocating this wasn't the important point of my issue, rather it was a side benefit. When we have charms that dish out 20 withering damage? At that point a few extra points of damage isn't going to break anything.<br /> <br /> What this allows Strength to do is compete. It becomes no where near a god stat. Dexterity still does a lot more to a lot more concepts. Universal accuracy and defense and movement (will which come into play a lot more than Feats of Strength on average) and Stealth (Very strong in nearly any game). Strength gets accuracy for Melee/Brawl and feats of strength. The tradeoff is lopsided still, Strength just has one of the more important aspects (Accuracy) now covered.<br /> <br /> Even then we get variety in builds. A thrown/Archery use? They're going to make a Strength 5 Dexterity 2 character's life a living hell. Forcing them to spend resources for magic to attack or be shot full of arrows/knives.<br /> <br /> It doesn't become a godstat on par with Dexterity. No where even close.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T21:10:10-07:00","id":1240318,"title":"","content":"I've been following this thread from the start, and all I can come up with is this: Why is combat the only way a character matters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T21:32:28-07:00","id":1240323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1240318#post1240318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been following this thread from the start, and all I can come up with is this: Why is combat the only way a character matters?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were having a recurring problem playing social characters, and someone told you to just play a combat monkey instead, would you find this helpful, or <i>obnoxious?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T03:24:05-07:00","id":1240376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1240155#post1240155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What this allows Strength to do is compete. It becomes no where near a god stat. Dexterity still does a lot more to a lot more concepts. Universal accuracy and defense and movement (will which come into play a lot more than Feats of Strength on average) and Stealth (Very strong in nearly any game). Strength gets accuracy for Melee/Brawl and feats of strength. The tradeoff is lopsided still, Strength just has one of the more important aspects (Accuracy) now covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just feel this actually shifts the balance in favour of Strength. Without charms, stealth can't be attempted in the open and disengage actions have to be performed at close range.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T04:55:51-07:00","id":1240391,"title":"","content":"Just stumbled into this thread and read the top post.<br /> <br /> Everybody seems pretty wound up, so I'm going to spend a couple motes for <b>[Serene Morning Houserule Contemplation]</b> and jot down a few ideas.<br /> <br /> I really like the ideas for having Strength available for Melee and Perception available for Ranged. Maybe even Wits for Thrown. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I was going to open that up at my table, here's what I'd be considering:<br /> <br /> * Don't step on another PC's concept. Especially if one player paid in with a Charm or something while the other gets a freeb.<br /> <br /> * Keep to my dice pool limits depending where we are in the Chronicle. That's a way I work with my players to make sure characters shine at what they ought to shine at, without forcing people into combat monkey builds. Changing a stat doesn't remove the limit.<br /> <br /> * I'd tend to allow a free lifetime choice or a paid option. Meaning: If you tell me at chargen that you want to be a StrengthBrawl fighter, I'm inclined to allow that as a free permanent choice for that character, or as a Chronicle-spanning rule if everybody at table likes it. If you rather have the option, then that could be a Charm or Specialization function.<br /> <br /> * If the players at table want to slice &amp; dice categories more than Core does it, then alternate Attributes might be a function of different weapon weights. <br /> <br /> * Sauce for the goose. If the Circle can do it, the enemy can do it.<br /> <br /> * If nobody at table really wants to work with this, then it's an extraneous mechanic and it goes back in the bin.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T05:05:20-07:00","id":1240393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1240323#post1240323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were having a recurring problem playing social characters, and someone told you to just play a combat monkey instead, would you find this helpful, or <i>obnoxious?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not what the &quot;Strength should be used for hitting people just as much as Dexterity&quot; crowd has been arguing.<br /> <br /> This is my take on the entire thread:<br /> 1) Everyone is able to houserule their own games. Do it, because one cannot expect others to agree with exactly the same things being &quot;wrong&quot; in the system. It's pretty evident in this case that not many agree with this particular idea.<br /> 2) Heavy Arms had a great thought that kept Dex and Str from being essentially the same stat with the &quot;double the effect of Str on damage rolls&quot; idea. This was dismissed out of hand while being thematically appropriate.<br /> 3) It seems that neither side in this debate is getting anywhere with their arguments, and several times have appeared to dip into condescension and/or outright ignoring potentially interesting, if not great or well-defined, ideas. It's a lot like the political landscape of the US right now... The other side thought of it, so it must be a terrible plan.<br /> 4) Ranged/thrown accuracy being moved to Perception is actually a pretty good idea to me.<br /> 5) Combat is all that matters in an Exalted game. I'm not sure I follow why this is, but with the several threads I've seen here about parts of the game of this nature, it must be. So every Exalt should have Physical primary (Str 5, Dex 5, Sta 1) and hope to destroy one's opponents before they get at chance to strike.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T05:22:41-07:00","id":1240397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1238940#post1238940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> The other issue with it is that quick characters don't have a 'strength score' they have an attack pool and a damage pool.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I think, is an excellent point. <br /> <br /> You probably want your best fighters to turn in an expected success (or two, or more) beyond what your average fighters expect to. Same way with average fighters over wimps. <br /> <br /> It's the pool that translates into the number of successes. The combination of Attribute and Ability doesn't so much matter as long as the pools are where they need to be for your game. The distinction remains for stunting and for Charms, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:48:55-07:00","id":1240654,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vJGvSbHmeco&amp;t=12s\" target=\"_blank\">this </a>is what we'd all actually like to see in a strength optimized build vs a dex optimized one","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T02:04:21-07:00","id":1241210,"title":"","content":"...Y'know, watching that video made me realise something. A lot of these arguments look at how high strength, low dex builds sacrifice their hit probability, like maybe 50% vs 80% or whatever.<br /> <br /> <i>That's exactly how strong, slow characters fight.</i> &quot;Miss, miss, miss, POW&quot;.<br /> <br /> They hit less often, but it counts more when they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T04:39:25-07:00","id":1241246,"title":"","content":"Tbh, that's why I think the suggestion to just double Strength when adding it to damage is probably the easiest, best, and most balanced one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:39:27-07:00","id":1241255,"title":"","content":"Another thought: One of the other issues was how if you're using a weapon you might build up a bunch of initiative but then fail to connect the decisive. <br /> <br /> Given how the decisive is supposed to be the point where you finally hit the perfect spot to strike, it seems logical that you should be able to split initiative between damage and accuracy, trading the effect of a blow for making sure it hits. The fact that successes don't naturally roll over actually plays right into this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T06:35:53-07:00","id":1241281,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I wrote this a few days ago and may as well post it rather than delete it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The false equivalence between potential threshold successes and additional raw damage:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On the mortal level each point of dexterity is worth 1 dice or half a success, this means that for every 2 points of dexterity you have over your opponent you can expect to get an additional threshold success. It\u2019s not really comparable to Strength for enhancing attack damage but more importantly it offers no advantage towards an opponent on a comparable skill level.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It gets murkier when we come to Exalts; a Solar can overpower a Dragon-Blooded on simple math the ability to add up to 10 dice is better than the ability to add up to 6 dice. There\u2019s scope for the Dragon-Blooded to be the more skilled of the two but still be overwhelmed by raw power.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s really a trap element to the assertion that Dexterity helps you with damage because threshold successes probably won\u2019t be there when you actually need them. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I'm going to use an example with one of my favourite NPCs from the rulebook, the Nephwrack. Their opponent is a Solar with dual light weapons Dexterity/Martial Arts 5, specialty but only strength 2 because who needs it, right?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So the Solar rolls their withering attack with a full excellency and a stunt bonus achieving an average of 14 successes, hitting the Nephwrack by 8 for a total of 20 damage, three more than their opponent's soak but still dealing only the same amount of damage as their Onslaught rating meaning all those additional successes were probably pointless. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The reason I use the Nephwrack as an example is because <i>it\u2019s not even that tough</i> while the Solar is approaching the pinnacle of their ability for making attacks based on pure skill and shows how much high stamina and good armour can potentially stonewall such a character build.<br /> <br /> Tangent on the true power of the Nephwrack because I love this evil bastard if he's used properly.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If the Solar couldn't reliably resist Dawn of Dead Stars they'd be in a pretty precarious situation, where they're steadily losing 2 points of initiative a round to an opponent they can only reliably do 3 dice of damage to. Which might not sound like a complete disaster because they're probably going to get lucky long before the Nephwrack slowly drains them enough to finish them off with Soul Destruction, except that the Nephwrack also has Mists of Eventide at its disposal that imposes a similar draining effect on the combat and incapacitates people it crashes... that could be a problem. </div></div> </div> </div> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This isn\u2019t intended to be an argument for Strength being equivalent to Dexterity just highlight how finesse isn\u2019t always a substitute for raw power. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:28:46-07:00","id":1241316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1241210#post1241210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Y'know, watching that video made me realise something. A lot of these arguments look at how high strength, low dex builds sacrifice their hit probability, like maybe 50% vs 80% or whatever.<br /> <br /> <i>That's exactly how strong, slow characters fight.</i> &quot;Miss, miss, miss, POW&quot;.<br /> <br /> They hit less often, but it counts more when they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much what I've been pointing out this whole thread. This is how the system runs combat. This is how Dex vs Str builds <i>work</i>. The issue seems more to be that the guy doing more damage per hit but hitting less just does less damage overall. And I'd agree, just adding double STR to the damage roll might help with that.<br /> <br /> Or maybe add your STR/2 to a weapon's overwhelming score, since it seems kinda weird that someone with STR 3 does the same minimum damage against someone with STR 5 against an armored opponent. As Lioness points out, the OVW rating of a weapon can be what you're relying on a lot with the big bads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:57:47-07:00","id":1241356,"title":"","content":"I had a big post, but I've been writing it and deleting it a lot.<br /> <br /> Anyway, addressing my own suggestion:<br /> <br /> I dismissed it myself because it's not that simple. One of the things you have to watch out for (and the OP's suggestion does while mine does not) is not leaving Stamina out in the cold. You don't want to strip tanks of the ability to tank just so brutes can break things better.<br /> <br /> While increasing raw damage and overwhelming to be more Strength dependent and less weapon dependent is a good thing (to me at least, to both make Strength more valuable, generate results more like people imagine, and make weapon selection less optimization focused), doing it in a vacuum isn't. It's a band-aid for what needs to be a much more thorough recalibration of the combat system to down play weapons, and increase the function of Strength and Stamina.<br /> <br /> One of the things I've grown to appreciate a lot about the Storypath system's evolution of the Tag based equipment, is that there's no base equipment stat blocs. All weapons and armor (at least those on the same Scale and not masterworks/Relics, but those boosts are still straight forward) work on the exact same rules except for what Tags they have. As well the system actually has a straight forward method for designing weapons/armor (Tags have a value, and normal stuff has a cap of 3) to your desires.<br /> <br /> You can't lift the Storypath Tag system into Exalted directly (the combat systems are too different), but I think you'd have to do something similar to make weapon/armor selection less important, and thus give more space for Strength and Stamina to feel like they matter in combat. Inflating the numbers alone tends to make things more cumbersome than fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T10:13:13-07:00","id":1241365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1239583#post1239583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;The enemies shown so far show that you don\u2019t need a maxed out pool!<br /> <br /> Do you know why this is the case Talos? Its for people who don\u2019t optimize (definition below) for combat have a chance. The people who do optimize? They use them to wipe their ass in combat. This is great for people who just want a pure power fantasy with nothing capable of remotely challenging them. You want an isekai power trip? Go ahead, others like to have more tactical combat choices.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Y'know, one thing I don't understand is why can't the people who like to have tactical combat choices and clearly have the system mastery to recognize the benefits of maximizing their dice pools just <i>exercise some basic self-restraint</i> and maybe go dex 3, ability 5, no spec instead of picking 5/5 and an omni-applicable specialty, especially when doing so would make the game more fun to them by their own metrics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:51:26-07:00","id":1241419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1241365#post1241365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Y'know, one thing I don't understand is why can't the people who like to have tactical combat choices and clearly have the system mastery to recognize the benefits of maximizing their dice pools just <i>exercise some basic self-restraint</i> and maybe go dex 3, ability 5, no spec instead of picking 5/5 and an omni-applicable specialty, especially when doing so would make the game more fun to them by their own metrics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, such is the curse of the min-maxer. There is a drive to create the 'best' possible character and then see it challenged against enemies of great strength.<br /> <br /> I've played with several min-maxers in my time and have even been guilty of doing it at some points myself, but while there is a thrill to utterly crushing your opposition, it gets dull fast. The min-maxer's I've known all also often the fastest to switch characters in a campaign, grow bored with a campaign entirely or, in at least one case, be that guy who has hios fun but being a dick to other characters in the guise of 'it's in character therefore it should be acceptable. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T12:28:51-07:00","id":1241445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1238731-a-concern-for-lunars-alternate-dice-pools?p=1241365#post1241365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Y'know, one thing I don't understand is why can't the people who like to have tactical combat choices and clearly have the system mastery to recognize the benefits of maximizing their dice pools just <i>exercise some basic self-restraint</i> and maybe go dex 3, ability 5, no spec instead of picking 5/5 and an omni-applicable specialty, especially when doing so would make the game more fun to them by their own metrics.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what most of us do these days. We just deliberately build characters in sub-optimal ways. For example, most of us never take Dex 5. The problem is... how sub-optimal? If one person makes it a bit sub-optimal, and another a lot, it can get awkward. And it is a game about being amazing demi-gods, so you don't want to make yourself rubbish.*<br /> <br /> *With my current character, I deliberately didn't take amazing attributes. He has Str/Dex/Sta 3, Martial Arts 5, no specialty. The other PCs think he's so bad at combat that they once tied him up so he couldn't come fight a Nephwrack with them, as they assumed he'd just die, and they're planning to tie him up again next session for the same reason.<br /> <br /> Basically, I just wish the game didn't encourage you to optimise so much, and punish you for not doing so (with high ability prereqs) so people could just not feel like there's a good and bad way to make characters. The easiest way to do that is by fiddling with character gen, which I've tried doing, and it helps a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The min-maxer's I've known all also often the fastest to switch characters in a campaign, </div> </div> </div>Ugh, yes. The player I had who was the worst for min-maxing played 5 characters in a game most people played 1-2, and they were all min-maxed except the first one. The first one was also the most fun and interesting, unsurprisingly.<br /> <br /> <br /> But anyway, this is why I want to run a Lunar game. The way Lunar character gen will probably work will, I suspect, have much less optimisation and min-maxing, because you can't buy 7 abilities at 5. In fact, probably people will have all their abilities at 1-3. And there's some other reasons about charm prereqs, excellencies, etc, that I've mentioned earlier.<br /> <br /> Of course, after suggesting it immediately some people were like &quot;I want to play a Solar.&quot; So I might allow Solars but say they can only start with one ability at 5, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-01-2018, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}